        "4076": {"comment":"BC+1 bytes"},
        "4078": {"comment":"First zero"},
        "4079": {"comment":"Clear the rest"},
        "4081": {"comment":"Back into the kernel"},
        "4082": {"synopsis":"Steps IY down EXOS's segment list for an address that has gone below a segment's start.\nEntry: HL = address, DE = amount to subtract (0: step at once), IY = list position.\nExit: A = the high byte of the address within its segment; IY moved one place for each 16K\nadded.","comment":"Nothing to subtract?"},
        "4087": {"comment":"Subtract it"},
        "4090": {"comment":"Still positive: done"},
        "4091": {"synopsis":"Steps one place down the list and adds 16K to the high byte until it carries.","comment":"One segment further down the list"},
        "4093": {"comment":"Add 16K"},
        "4095": {"comment":"Until back in range"},
        "4098": {"synopsis":"Before EXOS takes more RAM (EXOS 27 at $0D92, and $0A8B): when there is no shared segment\nand free segments remain, and the next free segment is a video segment ($FC-$FF) numbered\nabove one of EXOS's own segments, swaps them: the video segment takes that place in EXOS's\nsegment list (from $ABD0 down; $BF9A points at EXOS's lowest), the old segment's 16K is\ncopied into it and every link in the channel list that named the old segment is changed.\nRepeats, then sets $BF8A (FIND_VID_SEG). The swap was not run in the profile.","comment":"L = shared segment, H = free segments"},
        "4101": {"comment":"Shared segment in use?"},
        "4105": {"comment":"No free segments?"},
        "4108": {"synopsis":"Compares the next free segment with EXOS's segments, top down.","comment":"Next free segment's entry, below EXOS's"},
        "4112": {"comment":"Scan EXOS's list from the top"},
        "4115": {"synopsis":"Steps down EXOS's segment list while its entries are higher than the free one."},
        "4116": {"comment":"EXOS's segment"},
        "4117": {"comment":"Reached the free entry itself?"},
        "4120": {"comment":"EXOS's is higher: keep looking"},
        "4122": {"comment":"Keep EXOS's segment"},
        "4123": {"comment":"The free segment"},
        "4124": {"comment":"A video segment?"},
        "4126": {"comment":"No: nothing to swap"},
        "4128": {"comment":"It takes the place in EXOS's list"},
        "4129": {"comment":"Page 1 = the video segment"},
        "4131": {"comment":"A = the old segment"},
        "4132": {"comment":"Update the list"},
        "4135": {"comment":"No interrupts while page 0 changes"},
        "4136": {"comment":"Page 0 = the old segment"},
        "4138": {"comment":"Copy 16K from page 0 to page 1"},
        "4147": {"comment":"E = old segment"},
        "4149": {"comment":"D = video segment"},
        "4150": {"comment":"Caller's page 0"},
        "4153": {"comment":"Page 0 back"},
        "4156": {"comment":"Walk the channel list"},
        "4159": {"synopsis":"Changes every channel-list link that names segment E to segment D."},
        "4160": {"comment":"Link's segment"},
        "4161": {"comment":"The old segment?"},
        "4164": {"comment":"Name the video segment instead"},
        "4165": {"synopsis":"Follows the link to the next node."},
        "4166": {"comment":"Follow the link"},
        "4169": {"comment":"Until the end of the list"},
        "4171": {"comment":"Look again"},
        "4173": {"synopsis":"Sets $BF8A to the first segment from $FC up that sits at its own place among the top four\nentries of EXOS's segment list ($ABCD-$ABD0, where $ABD0 always holds $FF): the lowest\nsegment of the run of video segments at the top.","comment":"Entry before $ABCD"},
        "4176": {"comment":"Start below $FC"},
        "4178": {"synopsis":"Tries the next segment number against its place in the list.","comment":"Next segment number"},
        "4180": {"comment":"At its own place?"},
        "4183": {"comment":"Lowest video segment of the top run"},
        "4187": {"synopsis":"Close or destroy (from the channel calls, $0BD7, after the device's close entry ran through\nDEV_CALL_CHAN: IY = the channel's pointer, IX/B = the link above it): removes the channel's\nblock\nfrom the channel list and closes the hole. Each node below is moved up by the space freed\n(the block's size plus its gap), relinked and its device called with entry 13 (buffer\nmoved); a moved video channel also raises $BF8D. At the end of the list the EXOS boundary\n($BF91) rises by the space freed and each whole segment it passes goes back to the free list\n(RELEASE_SYS_SEG). Clears the channel cache ($BFA5) and returns the device's status.","comment":"Drop the stacked HL"},
        "4188": {"comment":"A = the device's status"},
        "4189": {"comment":"Keep it"},
        "4190": {"comment":"Segment of the channel's RAM"},
        "4191": {"comment":"Page it into page 1"},
        "4193": {"comment":"Total size of the block"},
        "4199": {"comment":"plus its gap"},
        "4205": {"comment":"Space freed"},
        "4206": {"comment":"DE = space freed"},
        "4207": {"comment":"HL = the channel pointer"},
        "4210": {"synopsis":"Per node below the freed block: follows the link to it, moves the gap of the node above into\nthe space to be closed and clears that gap."},
        "4211": {"comment":"Follow its link to the next node"},
        "4214": {"comment":"Keep the next node"},
        "4215": {"comment":"Keep its flags: Z = end of the list"},
        "4216": {"comment":"Segment of the node above"},
        "4218": {"comment":"To pointer-7"},
        "4222": {"comment":"BC = the next node's one-segment size"},
        "4228": {"comment":"Page in the node above"},
        "4230": {"comment":"Its gap"},
        "4237": {"comment":"HL = space freed plus that gap"},
        "4243": {"comment":"The node above has no gap now"},
        "4249": {"comment":"End of the list?"},
        "4250": {"comment":"Yes: the EXOS boundary rises"},
        "4277": {"synopsis":"Works out the node's new place: the destination address and, from EXOS's segment list ($ABD0\ndown), the destination segment."},
