      ],
      "lineAnnotations": {
        "0": {"synopsis":"IS-BASIC's call table for this page: the word at 2n is the run address of routine byte $80 +\nn, which a call list after RST 10h names (facts: the gate reaches $C000 + 2(n AND $7F)).\nEntries $80-$83 at $0000-$0007, then $88-$C5 at $0010-$008B; the places of $84-$87 hold the\nextension-ROM header's device chain word ($0008) and the two entry JPs ($000A, $000D). Bytes\n$8C-$8F and $B7-$C5 lead to routines above $1000 that other parts of this page describe.\nThe entries, routine byte then label: $80 VAR_LINK_HASH, $81 VAR_NEW_ENTRY, $82\nVAR_INIT_NUM, $83 VAR_INIT_STR, $88 VAR_CREATE, $89 VAR_DECLARE, $8A VAR_DECLARE_REF, $8B\nVAR_FIND_ANY, $8C VAR_FIND_VISIBLE, $8D VAR_ROOM_CHECK, $8E VAR_SCOPE_TEST, $8F\nVAR_FORGET_ABOVE, $90 FN_TABLE_INSTALL, $91 FP_PUSH_HL, $92 FP_PUSH_CONST, $93 FP_PUSH_AT,\n$94 FP_PUSH_R1, $95 FP_PUSH_R2, $96 FP_POP_AT, $97 FP_POP_R1, $98 FP_POP_R2, $99\nARG_NUM_PAREN, $9A ARG_NUM_OPEN, $9B ARG_NUM_COMMA, $9C ARG_STR_PAREN, $9D ARG_STR_OPEN, $9E\nARG_STR_COMMA, $9F ARG_ARRAY_OPEN, $A0 ARG_CLOSE, $A1 FN_FREE, $A2 FP_ATN, $A3 FP_ASIN, $A4\nFP_SIN, $A5 FP_COS, $A6 FP_TAN, $A7 FP_EXP, $A8 FP_RAD_TO_ANGLE, $A9 FP_ANGLE_TO_RAD, $AA\nFP_LOG10, $AB FP_MOD, $AC FP_SQR, $AD FP_RECIPROCAL, $AE FP_INT, $AF FP_ROUND_DIGITS, $B0\nFP_POWER, $B1 FP_IP, $B2 FP_SGN, $B3 SEG_FREE, $B4 SEG_ALLOC, $B5 SEG_SLOT_FIND, $B6\nSEG_TAG_FIND, $B7 STMT_SET, $B8 SETOPT_LOOKUP, $B9 LIST_RANGES, $BA LIST_LINES, $BB\nSTMT_AUTO, $BC STMT_RENUMBER, $BD PRINT_CHECK, $BE PRINT_EXEC, $BF ERR_TEXT_BUILD, $C0\nSTMT_WAIT_DELAY, $C1 LINES_REINDENT, $C2 STMT_TIME, $C3 STMT_DATE, $C4 STR_CASE_FLIP, $C5\nFKEYS_DEFAULT.","comment":"Bytes $80-$83"},
        "8": {"synopsis":"Extension-ROM header word: the device chain pointer, a page-1 address ($676A) of PRINTER's\nXX_SIZE byte at $276A, the first of this segment's built-in device descriptors (PRINTER,\nTAPE, SERIAL, NET).","comment":"Device chain: PRINTER's XX_SIZE byte at $276A (run as $676A)"},
        "10": {"synopsis":"Extension entry: EXOS calls $C00A in every ROM it scans with the action code in C; goes on\nat SEG1_EXT_ENTRY ($34E3).","comment":"Extension entry: action code in C"},
        "13": {"synopsis":"Service entry: segment 0's SEG1_SERVICE calls $C00D with A = a service number (0-6: clock,\ndate, tick, relocatable load, start-up); goes on at SEG1_SVC_ENTRY ($240F).","comment":"Service number in A"},
        "16": {"comment":"Bytes $88-$8B"},
        "24": {"comment":"Bytes $8C-$8F"},
        "32": {"comment":"Bytes $90-$93"},
        "40": {"comment":"Bytes $94-$97"},
        "48": {"comment":"Bytes $98-$9B"},
        "56": {"comment":"Bytes $9C-$9F"},
        "64": {"comment":"Bytes $A0-$A3"},
        "72": {"comment":"Bytes $A4-$A7"},
        "80": {"comment":"Bytes $A8-$AB"},
        "88": {"comment":"Bytes $AC-$AF"},
        "96": {"comment":"Bytes $B0-$B3"},
        "104": {"comment":"Bytes $B4-$B7"},
        "112": {"comment":"Bytes $B8-$BB"},
        "120": {"comment":"Bytes $BC-$BF"},
        "128": {"comment":"Bytes $C0-$C3"},
        "136": {"comment":"Bytes $C4-$C5"},
        "140": {"synopsis":"Constant table: 43 numbers of 7 bytes, constant n at $008C + 7n, pushed by FP_PUSH_CONST\n(byte $92 with n inline) and, through FP_PUSH_HL, by FP_ATN's offsets ($00BD, $00C4, $00CB).\nThe 7-byte form is item bytes +1..+6 then +8 (FP_PUSH_HL): bytes 0-5 a BCD mantissa, least\nsignificant first, whose leading digit is byte 5's high nibble (byte 0 the guard byte), and\nbyte 6 the sign (bit 7) and exponent (bits 0-6, bias $40): value = d.ddddddddddd x\n10^(exponent - $40). Constants 0-$0D are general (0.5, 1, the largest number, 32768, pi and\nits fractions, the angle factors, SQR's seed); $0E-$12 SIN's series; $13-$19 ATN's; $1A-$22\nLOG10's and the LOG/LOG2 factors; $23-$2A EXP's.","comment":"0: 0.5"},
        "147": {"comment":"1: 1"},
        "154": {"comment":"2: 9.999999999E62, the largest number (INF)"},
        "161": {"comment":"3: 32768"},
        "168": {"comment":"4: pi (3.14159265359)"},
        "175": {"comment":"5: 57.2957795131 = 180/pi, radians to degrees"},
        "182": {"comment":"6: 0.0174532925199 = pi/180, degrees to radians"},
        "189": {"comment":"7: pi/2 (1.57079632679)"},
        "196": {"comment":"8: pi/3 (1.0471975512)"},
        "203": {"comment":"9: pi/6 (0.523598775598)"},
        "210": {"comment":"$0A: 2*pi (6.28318530718)"},
        "217": {"comment":"$0B: 0.223607: SQR's first guess, added"},
        "224": {"comment":"$0C: 0.894427: SQR's first guess, the factor"},
        "231": {"comment":"$0D: 0.316227766017 = SQR(0.1)"},
        "238": {"comment":"$0E: -0.166666666088: SIN series"},
        "245": {"comment":"$0F: 0.00833333072056: SIN series"},
        "252": {"comment":"$10: -0.000198408328231: SIN series"},
        "259": {"comment":"$11: 2.75239710678E-6: SIN series"},
        "266": {"comment":"$12: -2.3868346406E-8: SIN series"},
        "273": {"comment":"$13: -1.44008344874: ATN series, numerator x^2"},
        "280": {"comment":"$14: -0.720026848898: ATN series, numerator x^4"},
        "287": {"comment":"$15: 4.32025038919: ATN series, denominator constant"},
        "294": {"comment":"$16: 4.75222584599: ATN series, denominator x^2"},
        "301": {"comment":"$17: 0.267949192431 = TAN 15 degrees: ATN reduction limit"},
        "308": {"comment":"$18: 1.73205080757 = SQR 3: ATN reduction"},
        "315": {"comment":"$19: 0.732050807569 = SQR 3 - 1: ATN reduction"},
        "322": {"comment":"$1A: -2.9156814379: LOG10 series"},
        "329": {"comment":"$1B: 3.16303491557: LOG10 series"},
        "336": {"comment":"$1C: -0.673581601478: LOG10 series"},
        "343": {"comment":"$1D: -10.0704069542: LOG10 series"},
        "350": {"comment":"$1E: 16.9669814021: LOG10 series"},
        "357": {"comment":"$1F: -8.19080045467: LOG10 series"},
        "364": {"comment":"$20: 0.868588963807 = 2/LN 10: LOG10"},
        "371": {"comment":"$21: 2.30258509299 = LN 10: LOG"},
        "378": {"comment":"$22: 3.32192809489 = 1/LOG10 2: LOG2"},
        "385": {"comment":"$23: 0.868588963807 = 2/LN 10: EXP"},
        "392": {"comment":"$24: 1.151, about LN(10)/2: EXP"},
        "399": {"comment":"$25: 0.000292546497023: EXP series"},
        "406": {"comment":"$26: 504.464889506: EXP series"},
        "413": {"comment":"$27: 14.0082997563: EXP series"},
        "420": {"comment":"$28: 0.0332873646516: EXP series"},
        "427": {"comment":"$29: 1008.92977901: EXP series"},
        "434": {"comment":"$2A: 112.094081097: EXP series"},
        "441": {"synopsis":"Allocates a RAM segment for IS-BASIC (byte $B4). Takes a free slot of the segment table at\n$0E54 (two bytes per slot: segment, tag), writes the tag C into it and asks EXOS 24 for a\nsegment, which goes into the slot.\nEntry: C = the tag (owner) of the new segment.\nExit: Z (A = 0) with C = the segment; M on an EXOS error (the slot keeps the tag, segment\nbyte 0); NZ and P for the .SHARE status ($7F): the shared segment is kept in ($020B), and if\nits EXOS boundary DE is 0 it is freed again through SEG_FREE, else A = D + 1.\nChanges: A, C, DE, HL.","comment":"Keep the tag"},
        "442": {"comment":"A shared segment held?"},
        "448": {"comment":"None: the tag also goes to ($020D)"},
        "451": {"synopsis":"Finds a free slot and asks EXOS for the segment.","comment":"HL = a free slot (segment byte 0)"},
        "455": {"comment":"Tag into the slot's second byte"},
        "460": {"comment":"EXOS error: return M"},
        "461": {"comment":"Segment into the slot"},
        "462": {"comment":"Got a segment of its own"},
        "463": {"comment":".SHARE: the shared segment goes to ($020B)"},
        "466": {"comment":"EXOS boundary DE = 0?"},
        "468": {"comment":"No room in it: free it again"},
        "470": {"comment":"A = boundary high byte + 1, NZ"},
        "473": {"synopsis":"Frees an IS-BASIC segment (byte $B3): finds the slot of the table at $0E54 that holds\nsegment C, empties it (clearing ($020B) too when it held that segment) and frees the segment\nwith EXOS 25.\nEntry: C = the segment.\nExit: NZ, A = $FF (EXOS's status is not looked at).\nChanges: A, C, HL.","comment":"HL = the slot holding segment C"},
        "477": {"comment":"Was it the shared one in ($020B)?"},
        "483": {"comment":"Yes: ($020B) = 0"},
        "486": {"synopsis":"Empties the slot and frees the segment.","comment":"Slot free"},
        "490": {"comment":"NZ, A = $FF"},
        "493": {"synopsis":"Looks for a free slot of the table at $0E54 (segment byte 0): SEG_SLOT_FIND with C = 0."},
        "495": {"synopsis":"Finds the slot of the segment table at $0E54 whose segment byte equals C (byte $B5). There\nis no end test: the slot must exist.\nEntry: C = the segment (0 for a free slot).\nExit: HL = the slot, Z, A = C.","comment":"The segment table"},
        "499": {"synopsis":"Steps two bytes at a time until the segment byte matches.","comment":"This slot?"},
        "505": {"synopsis":"Finds a used slot of the segment table at $0E54 tagged C (byte $B6), searching the (ix+$0C)\nslots.\nEntry: C = the tag.\nExit: Z, NC and HL = the slot when found; carry when none.\nChanges: A, B, HL."},
        "508": {"comment":"B = the number of slots, ($020C)"},
        "511": {"synopsis":"Tests one slot: skipped when free, else its tag is compared with C.","comment":"Free slot?"},
        "516": {"comment":"Its tag"},
        "519": {"comment":"Found: HL = the slot"},
        "520": {"synopsis":"Moves to the next slot until all are seen."},
        "524": {"comment":"None: carry"},
        "526": {"synopsis":"Raises IS-BASIC error 1000 \"Unexpected value given\" (RST 20h raises error HL). The error\nexits that follow share their RST 20h: each starts with LD L,n, and the next ones are hidden\nas LD L,n inside LD DE,$xx2E instructions.","comment":"Error 1000: Unexpected value given"},
        "530": {"synopsis":"Raises IS-BASIC error 1002 \"Overflow in numeric expression\".","comment":"Error 1002: Overflow in numeric expression"},
        "534": {"synopsis":"Raises IS-BASIC error $0B00 + L: 3004 \"Invalid argument to LOG\" here; LD L,n entries hidden\nat $0219, $021C and $021F give 3005-3007.","comment":"Error 3004: Invalid argument to LOG"},
        "536": {"comment":"Hides +1 LD L,$BD: error 3005, Invalid argument to SQR"},
        "539": {"comment":"Hides +1 LD L,$BE: error 3006 (MOD by zero)"},
        "542": {"comment":"Hides +1 LD L,$BF: error 3007, Invalid argument to ASIN or ACOS"},
        "545": {"comment":"H = $0B: errors 3004-3007"},
        "548": {"synopsis":"Raises IS-BASIC error $0F00 + L: 4002 \"Argument to CHR$ out of range\" here; LD L,n entries\nhidden at $0227-$0230 give 4003, 4004, 4008 and 4009.","comment":"Error 4002: Argument to CHR$ out of range"},
        "550": {"comment":"Hides +1 LD L,$A3: error 4003, Invalid argument to ORD"},
        "553": {"comment":"Hides +1 LD L,$A4: error 4004, Index to SIZE out of range"},
        "556": {"comment":"Hides +1 LD L,$A8: error 4008, Index to LBOUND out of range"},
        "559": {"comment":"Hides +1 LD L,$A9: error 4009, Index to UBOUND out of range"},
        "562": {"comment":"H = $0F: errors 4002-4009"},
        "565": {"comment":"Error 5000: Insufficient memory (reached by no jump)"},
        "569": {"synopsis":"Raises IS-BASIC error $2000 + L: 8201 \"Invalid USING string\" here; LD L,n entries hidden at\n$023C and $023F give 8202 and 8203.","comment":"Error 8201: Invalid USING string"},
        "571": {"comment":"Hides +1 LD L,$0A: error 8202, No format item in USING string"},
        "574": {"comment":"Hides +1 LD L,$0B: error 8203, USING format item too short"},
        "577": {"comment":"H = $20: errors 8201-8203"},
        "580": {"synopsis":"Raises IS-BASIC error $4E00 + L: 20000 \"Not understood\" here; LD L,n entries hidden at\n$0247-$025C give 20001, 20002, 20004, 20010, 20030, 20031, 20041 and 20052.","comment":"Error 20000: Not understood"},
        "582": {"comment":"Hides +1 LD L,$21: error 20001, Invalid line number"},
        "585": {"comment":"Hides +1 LD L,$22: error 20002, Invalid line number range"},
        "588": {"comment":"Hides +1 LD L,$24: error 20004, Line number does not exist"},
        "591": {"comment":"Hides +1 LD L,$2A: error 20010, Cannot do specified RENUMBER"},
        "594": {"comment":"Hides +1 LD L,$3E: error 20030, Identifier expected"},
        "597": {"comment":"Hides +1 LD L,$3F: error 20031, String identifier expected"},
        "600": {"comment":"Hides +1 LD L,$49: error 20041, Identifier declared twice"},
        "603": {"comment":"Hides +1 LD L,$54: error 20052, Too many nested blocks"},
        "606": {"comment":"H = $4E: errors 20000-20052"},
        "609": {"synopsis":"Installs this page's function keywords in IS-BASIC's name table (byte $90; the cartridge's\nstart-up calls it).\n1. Clears the 32 hash heads at $0DCB-$0E0A.\n2. For each entry of the keyword table at $0DE4 (flags, length, name, routine address; a 0\n   ends it), writes at DE a link word (left for the hash), the entry's flags, length, name\n   and address, then segment 1, and links it into its bucket with VAR_LINK_HASH ($11B2).\nEntry: HL = where the entries go.\nExit: HL = the end of the copies.\nChanges: A, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"DE = the destination"},
        "610": {"comment":"The 32 hash heads"},
        "613": {"comment":"64 bytes"},
        "615": {"synopsis":"Zeroes the hash heads."},
        "620": {"comment":"The keyword table at $0DE4"},
        "623": {"synopsis":"Copies and links one keyword entry.","comment":"A = the name length"},
        "626": {"comment":"Flags, length, name and address"},
        "631": {"comment":"Keep the entry start"},
        "632": {"comment":"Past the link word"},
        "636": {"comment":"The routine is in segment 1"},
        "640": {"comment":"HL = the new entry, keep the table pointer"},
        "642": {"comment":"VAR_LINK_HASH: into its hash bucket"},
        "647": {"comment":"End of the keyword table?"},
        "651": {"comment":"HL = the end of the copies"},
        "653": {"synopsis":"Pushes constant n of FP_CONSTANTS, n being the byte after this routine's byte in the call\nlist (byte $92).\nChanges: A, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"L = the inline byte n"},
        "656": {"comment":"HL = n"},
        "659": {"comment":"HL = 8n"},
        "663": {"comment":"HL = 7n"},
        "665": {"comment":"The constant table"},
        "669": {"comment":"Push it"},
        "671": {"synopsis":"Pushes the 7-byte number at the address given by the next word of the call list (byte $93).","comment":"HL = the inline word"},
        "676": {"synopsis":"Pushes the number register R1 at $0E0B (byte $94).","comment":"R1"},
        "681": {"synopsis":"Pushes the number register R2 at $0E12 (byte $95).","comment":"R2"},
        "684": {"synopsis":"Pushes the 7-byte number at HL onto IS-BASIC's value stack (byte $91) as a 9-byte number\nitem: type 2, the six mantissa bytes, a zero overflow byte, the sign-and-exponent byte;\n($0228) is lowered to the new item.\nEntry: HL = the 7-byte number.\nExit: HL = ($0228) = the new item.\nChanges: A, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"From the last byte"},
        "688": {"comment":"The stack top"},
        "692": {"comment":"Below it: item +8"},
        "693": {"comment":"Sign and exponent to +8"},
        "695": {"comment":"Overflow byte +7 = 0"},
        "698": {"comment":"Mantissa to +6..+1"},
        "704": {"comment":"Type 2: a number"},
        "706": {"comment":"New stack top"},
        "710": {"synopsis":"Pops the top number into the 7 bytes at the address given by the next word of the call list\n(byte $96).","comment":"HL = the inline word"},
        "713": {"comment":"DE = the destination"},
        "716": {"synopsis":"Pops the top number into R1 at $0E0B (byte $97).","comment":"R1"},
        "721": {"synopsis":"Pops the top number into R2 at $0E12 (byte $98).","comment":"R2"},
        "724": {"synopsis":"Pops the top number item into its 7-byte form at DE: bytes +1..+6, then +8 (the overflow\nbyte +7 is dropped); ($0228) moves past the item.\nEntry: DE = the destination.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL."},
        "727": {"comment":"Past the type byte"},
        "728": {"comment":"Mantissa +1..+6"},
        "733": {"comment":"Skip the overflow byte"},
        "734": {"comment":"Sign and exponent"},
        "736": {"comment":"Item popped"},
        "740": {"synopsis":"Reads a function's single numeric argument \"( expression )\" onto the value stack (byte $99):\nARG_NUM_OPEN, then falls into ARG_CLOSE.","comment":"ARG_NUM_OPEN: \"(\" and a number"},
        "743": {"synopsis":"Expects \")\" and reads the token after it (byte $A0).","comment":"Symbol $09: \")\""},
        "746": {"comment":"Expect symbol A, then read the next token"},
        "749": {"synopsis":"Expects \",\" and evaluates the next numeric argument (byte $9B). The LD HL,$083E hides\nARG_NUM_OPEN (byte $9A) at $02F0: LD A,$08, the same with \"(\".","comment":"Symbol $0C: \",\""},
        "751": {"comment":"Hides ARG_NUM_OPEN at +1: LD A,$08, symbol \"(\""},
        "755": {"comment":"Expect symbol A, then read the next token"},
        "756": {"comment":"Evaluate a numeric expression, pushed"},
        "759": {"synopsis":"Reads a function's single string argument \"( string expression )\" (byte $9C): ARG_STR_OPEN,\nthen ARG_CLOSE.","comment":"ARG_STR_OPEN: \"(\" and a string"},
        "762": {"comment":"Then \")\""},
        "764": {"synopsis":"Expects \",\" and evaluates the next string argument (byte $9E). The LD HL,$083E hides\nARG_STR_OPEN (byte $9D) at $02FF: LD A,$08, the same with \"(\".","comment":"Symbol $0C: \",\""},
        "766": {"comment":"Hides ARG_STR_OPEN at +1: LD A,$08, symbol \"(\""},
        "770": {"comment":"Expect symbol A, then read the next token"},
        "771": {"comment":"Evaluate a string expression, pushed"},
        "774": {"synopsis":"Reads \"(\" and an array name (byte $9F, for LBOUND, UBOUND and SIZE): the name is looked up\nwith VAR_FIND_VISIBLE and the token after it read.\nExit: HL = the array's value field, C = its flags (bit 1 set).\nError 20032 when the token is not a name or the name is not an array.","comment":"Symbol $08: \"(\""},
        "777": {"comment":"Expect symbol A, then read the next token"},
        "779": {"comment":"Token class"},
        "782": {"comment":"A numeric name?"},
        "786": {"comment":"A string name?"},
        "790": {"synopsis":"Looks the name up and checks it is an array."},
        "791": {"comment":"VAR_FIND_VISIBLE: HL = value field, C = flags"},
        "792": {"comment":"Read the next token"},
        "794": {"comment":"An array?"},
        "797": {"synopsis":"Raises IS-BASIC error 20032: the argument is not an array name.","comment":"Error 20032"},
        "801": {"synopsis":"ABS(x): the absolute value (the keyword table's entry for ABS)."},
        "802": {"comment":"ARG_NUM_PAREN: x"},
        "803": {"comment":"Make it non-negative"},
        "806": {"synopsis":"ACOS(x) = pi/2 - ASIN(x), in the current angle unit."},
        "807": {"comment":"ARG_NUM_PAREN: x"},
        "808": {"comment":"FP_ASIN: arcsine in radians"},
        "809": {"comment":"Negate it"},
        "810": {"comment":"Push constant n"},
        "811": {"comment":"Constant 7: pi/2"},
        "812": {"comment":"Add: pi/2 - ASIN(x)"},
        "813": {"comment":"FP_RAD_TO_ANGLE: to degrees if they are on"},
        "816": {"synopsis":"ANGLE(x,y): the angle of the point (x,y) from the x axis, in the current angle unit: 0 for y\n= 0 and x not negative, pi for y = 0 and x negative, else pi/2 - ATN(x/y) for y positive and\n-pi/2 - ATN(x/y) for y negative."},
        "817": {"comment":"ARG_NUM_OPEN: x"},
        "818": {"comment":"ARG_NUM_COMMA: y"},
        "819": {"comment":"ARG_CLOSE"},
        "820": {"comment":"Z when y (the top) is zero"},
        "822": {"comment":"y is not zero"},
        "825": {"comment":"Drop y"},
        "826": {"comment":"NZ when x is negative"},
        "828": {"comment":"x negative: pi"},
        "830": {"synopsis":"Sets the top number to integer 0 and returns: ANGLE's result for y = 0 and x not negative,\nand a shared exit that other functions jump to ($046E, $067F, $0B03, $0CC8)."},
        "831": {"comment":"Set the top to integer 0"},
        "834": {"synopsis":"y = 0, x negative: the result is pi."},
        "835": {"comment":"Drop x"},
        "836": {"comment":"Push constant n"},
        "837": {"comment":"Constant 4: pi"},
        "838": {"comment":"FP_RAD_TO_ANGLE"},
        "841": {"synopsis":"y not 0: ATN(x/y), negated, plus pi/2 for y positive or -pi/2 for y negative."},
        "842": {"comment":"NZ when y is negative"},
        "844": {"comment":"Keep y's sign"},
        "846": {"comment":"x/y"},
        "847": {"comment":"FP_ATN: ATN(x/y)"},
        "850": {"comment":"Negate it"},
        "851": {"comment":"Push constant n"},
        "852": {"comment":"Constant 7: pi/2"},
        "855": {"comment":"y positive?"},
        "858": {"comment":"y negative: -pi/2"},
        "860": {"synopsis":"Adds the quarter turn and converts to the angle unit."},
        "861": {"comment":"Add"},
        "863": {"comment":"FP_RAD_TO_ANGLE"},
        "866": {"synopsis":"ASIN(x) in the current angle unit."},
        "867": {"comment":"ARG_NUM_PAREN: x"},
        "868": {"comment":"FP_ASIN: arcsine in radians"},
        "869": {"comment":"FP_RAD_TO_ANGLE"},
        "872": {"synopsis":"Arcsine of the top number, in radians (byte $A3). x = 1 gives pi/2 and x = -1 gives -pi/2;\notherwise ATN(x / SQR(1 - x*x)) through FP_ATN, which follows.\nError 3007 \"Invalid argument to ASIN or ACOS\" when x > 1 or x < -1."},
        "873": {"comment":"Convert x to float form"},
        "874": {"comment":"Copy x"},
        "875": {"comment":"Push constant n"},
        "876": {"comment":"Constant 1: 1"},
        "877": {"comment":"Compare x with 1"},
        "879": {"comment":"x < 1"},
        "882": {"comment":"x > 1: error 3007 (hidden entry at $021F)"},
        "886": {"comment":"x = 1: drop it"},
        "887": {"comment":"Push constant n"},
        "888": {"comment":"Constant 7: pi/2"},
