        "1104": {"comment":"More digits?"},
        "1108": {"comment":"Keep the value"},
        "1110": {"comment":"Drop x"},
        "1114": {"comment":"Push HL as an integer"},
        "1117": {"synopsis":"CEIL(x): the smallest integer not below x. Integers are returned as they are; |x| < 1 gives\n0 or 1 by the sign; otherwise the fraction digits are cleared (a positive x is\nten's-complemented before and after, so its truncation rounds up), and a result of fewer\nthan 5 integer digits is turned into the integer form."},
        "1118": {"comment":"ARG_NUM_PAREN: x"},
        "1119": {"comment":"A = exponent byte; Z for integer form"},
        "1121": {"comment":"Already an integer"},
        "1122": {"comment":"Exponent without the sign"},
        "1124": {"comment":"A = the number of integer digits"},
        "1126": {"comment":"0.d"},
        "1128": {"comment":"At least one integer digit"},
        "1131": {"synopsis":"|x| < 1: 0 for a negative x, 1 for a positive one."},
        "1132": {"comment":"NZ when x is negative"},
        "1134": {"comment":"Negative: 0 (TOP_SET_ZERO)"},
        "1138": {"comment":"Positive: integer 1"},
        "1141": {"synopsis":"|x| >= 1, A = the integer digit count: a positive x is complemented first.","comment":"Keep the digit count"},
        "1143": {"comment":"NZ when x is negative"},
        "1148": {"comment":"Positive: ten's complement of the mantissa"},
        "1150": {"synopsis":"Clears the mantissa digits after the integer ones (positions A+4 to 15)."},
        "1152": {"comment":"B = the last integer digit's position"},
        "1155": {"synopsis":"Writes digit 0 at position B (the first pass, entered with NC, writes nothing)."},
        "1157": {"comment":"Digit 0 at position B"},
        "1162": {"comment":"Past the last position?"},
        "1167": {"comment":"NZ when negative"},
        "1172": {"comment":"Positive: complement back"},
        "1174": {"synopsis":"Normalises the result."},
        "1175": {"comment":"Normalise the top number"},
        "1177": {"synopsis":"Shared tail (also from $079B): pops A, the integer digit count, then NUM_INT_IF_SMALL."},
        "1178": {"synopsis":"Shared tail (from $0B14, $0CE5): with A the number of integer digits, turns the top number\ninto the integer form when A < 5.","comment":"Fewer than 5 integer digits?"},
        "1180": {"synopsis":"Shared tail (from $082E): returns on NC, else turns the top number into the integer form\n(pop as an integer, push again)."},
        "1182": {"comment":"Pop the top number into HL as an integer"},
        "1183": {"comment":"Push it back as an integer"},
        "1186": {"synopsis":"CHR$(n): a one-character string of code n. Error 4002 \"Argument to CHR$ out of range\" when n\nis not 0-255."},
        "1187": {"comment":"ARG_NUM_PAREN: n"},
        "1188": {"comment":"Pop it into HL as an integer"},
        "1190": {"comment":"E = the code"},
        "1191": {"comment":"Above 255?"},
        "1193": {"comment":"Error 4002"},
        "1196": {"comment":"The stack top"},
        "1200": {"comment":"The character"},
        "1202": {"comment":"Length 1"},
        "1205": {"comment":"Type 3: a string"},
        "1207": {"comment":"New stack top"},
        "1211": {"synopsis":"RGB(r,g,b): the colour byte of three intensities 0 to 1. Each is scaled to 0-7 by\nRGB_COMPONENT and its bits spread to every third bit: red's to bits 6, 3, 0, green's to 7,\n4, 1, blue's to 5, 2 (blue's lowest bit is shifted out). Pushed as an integer."},
        "1212": {"comment":"ARG_NUM_OPEN: r"},
        "1213": {"comment":"ARG_NUM_COMMA: g"},
        "1214": {"comment":"ARG_NUM_COMMA: b"},
        "1215": {"comment":"ARG_CLOSE"},
        "1217": {"comment":"Blue"},
        "1220": {"comment":"To bits 5, 2 (bit 8 lost)"},
        "1223": {"comment":"Green"},
        "1226": {"comment":"To bits 7, 4, 1"},
        "1228": {"comment":"Red: bits 6, 3, 0"},
        "1231": {"comment":"The colour byte"},
        "1237": {"comment":"Push HL as an integer"},
        "1240": {"synopsis":"Pops one intensity x, takes 7*x truncated as 0-7 (error 1000 above 7 or below 0) and spreads\nits bits: bit 0 to bit 6, bit 1 to bit 3, bit 2 to bit 0.\nExit: A = C = the spread bits.\nChanges: A, HL; BC kept."},
        "1241": {"comment":"Scale 7"},
        "1245": {"comment":"Push HL as an integer"},
        "1246": {"comment":"7*x"},
        "1247": {"comment":"Pop it into HL as an integer"},
        "1249": {"comment":"Above 255 (or negative)?"},
        "1254": {"comment":"Above 7?"},
        "1256": {"synopsis":"Out of range: error 1000.","comment":"Error 1000"},
        "1259": {"comment":"B = 3 bits, C = 0"},
        "1262": {"synopsis":"Moves the next bit of A into C, three places apart.","comment":"Two empty places"},
        "1266": {"comment":"Next bit (from bit 0) into carry"},
        "1267": {"comment":"Into C"},
        "1274": {"synopsis":"Colour constants BLACK, RED, BLUE, GREEN, YELLOW, CYAN, MAGENTA, WHITE: each keyword enters\nat an LD L,n (all but BLACK hidden in LD DE,$xx2E) and $09D5 pushes L as an integer. The\nvalues are 0, $49, $24, $92, $DB, $B6, $6D, $FF: red's bits are 0, 3, 6, green's 1, 4, 7,\nblue's 2, 5.","comment":"BLACK: 0"},
        "1276": {"comment":"Hides RED at +1: LD L,$49"},
        "1279": {"comment":"Hides BLUE at +1: LD L,$24"},
        "1282": {"comment":"GREEN enters at $0503: LD L,146"},
        "1285": {"comment":"YELLOW enters at $0506: LD L,219"},
        "1288": {"comment":"CYAN enters at $0509: LD L,182"},
        "1291": {"comment":"MAGENTA enters at $050C: LD L,109"},
        "1294": {"comment":"WHITE enters at $050F: LD L,255"},
        "1297": {"comment":"Push the colour byte L"},
        "1300": {"synopsis":"COS function (keyword entry): reads \"( x )\", turns degrees to radians when OPTION ANGLE\nDEGREES is on, and falls into FP_COS."},
        "1301": {"comment":"Read the argument \"( x )\""},
        "1302": {"comment":"Degrees to radians when DEGREES is on"},
        "1304": {"synopsis":"Cosine of the top number in radians (call byte $A5): adds pi/2 and takes the sine with\nFP_SIN ($0B86)."},
        "1305": {"comment":"Push a constant"},
        "1306": {"comment":"Constant 7: pi/2"},
        "1307": {"comment":"x + pi/2"},
        "1308": {"comment":"Its sine (FP_SIN)"},
        "1311": {"synopsis":"COSH function (keyword entry): reads \"( x )\" and pushes (e^x + 1/e^x) * 0.5."},
        "1312": {"comment":"Read the argument \"( x )\""},
        "1313": {"comment":"e^x"},
        "1314": {"comment":"Duplicate it"},
        "1315": {"comment":"1/e^x"},
        "1316": {"comment":"e^x + 1/e^x"},
        "1317": {"comment":"Push a constant"},
        "1318": {"comment":"Constant 0: 0.5"},
        "1319": {"comment":"Halve it"},
        "1322": {"synopsis":"COT function (keyword entry): the TAN keyword's routine ($0C9B, which reads the argument),\nthen FP_RECIPROCAL: 1/TAN(x).","comment":"TAN's routine: reads ( x ), pushes TAN(x)"},
        "1325": {"comment":"1/TAN(x)"},
        "1328": {"synopsis":"TIME$ function (keyword entry): reads the clock with EXOS 32 and pushes it as the\n8-character string \"hh:mm:ss\" (C = hours, D = minutes, E = seconds, BCD; the text is built\ndownwards from the top of the FP stack).\nExit: the string on the FP stack.","comment":"Read the time: C hours, D minutes, E seconds"},
        "1329": {"comment":"Read the next token"},
        "1330": {"comment":"Characters go below the FP stack's top"},
        "1333": {"comment":"Seconds"},
        "1337": {"comment":"Minutes, after a colon"},
        "1341": {"comment":"Hours, after a colon"},
        "1345": {"comment":"Length 8, type 3"},
        "1347": {"synopsis":"DATE$ function (keyword entry): reads the date with EXOS 34 and pushes it as the 8-character\nstring \"yyyymmdd\": the century (19 or 20), the year (C + 80 in BCD, carrying into the\ncentury), D the month, E the day.\nExit: the string on the FP stack.","comment":"Read the date: C year - 1980, D month, E day"},
        "1348": {"comment":"Expect symbol A"},
        "1352": {"comment":"Day"},
        "1356": {"comment":"Month"},
        "1360": {"comment":"Year: C + 80 in BCD"},
        "1363": {"comment":"Carry when the year passed 99"},
        "1364": {"comment":"Keep the carry"},
        "1369": {"comment":"Century 19"},
        "1371": {"comment":"Year below 2000?"},
        "1373": {"comment":"Century 20"},
        "1375": {"synopsis":"Writes the century digits (19, or 20 when the year carried) and finishes the string."},
        "1378": {"synopsis":"Finishes an 8-character string built below the FP stack's top: length 8, type 3, and makes\nit the new top.\nEntry: HL = the address of its first character.","comment":"Length byte 8"},
        "1381": {"comment":"Type 3: a string"},
        "1384": {"comment":"The new top of the FP stack"},
        "1388": {"synopsis":"Writes a \":\" below HL and falls into BCD_DIGIT_PAIR."},
        "1389": {"comment":"\":\""},
        "1391": {"synopsis":"Writes the BCD byte A as two ASCII digits below HL, low digit first (so they read high,\nlow).\nEntry: HL = just above where the digits go.\nExit: HL = the high digit's address.\nChanges: A, E.","comment":"Keep the BCD byte"},
        "1392": {"comment":"Low digit first"},
        "1395": {"comment":"High nibble to the low four bits"},
        "1400": {"synopsis":"Writes the low nibble of A as an ASCII digit at HL - 1.\nExit: HL lowered by one."},
        "1401": {"comment":"Nibble to an ASCII digit"},
        "1407": {"synopsis":"DEG function (keyword entry): reads \"( x )\" and multiplies it by 57.2957795131 (radians to\ndegrees)."},
        "1408": {"comment":"Read the argument \"( x )\""},
        "1409": {"comment":"Push a constant"},
        "1410": {"comment":"Constant 5: 57.2957795131 (degrees per radian)"},
        "1411": {"comment":"x * 57.2957795131"},
        "1414": {"synopsis":"Degrees to radians (call byte $A9): when OPTION ANGLE DEGREES is on (bit 0 of (ix+1)),\nmultiplies the top number by 0.0174532925199; otherwise returns at once.","comment":"OPTION ANGLE DEGREES on?"},
        "1420": {"comment":"Push a constant"},
        "1421": {"comment":"Constant 6: 0.0174532925199"},
        "1422": {"comment":"x * 0.0174532925199"},
        "1425": {"synopsis":"EPS function (keyword entry): reads \"( x )\" and pushes 10^(k-11), where k is x's decimal\nexponent (x = d.ddd * 10^k): the smallest step at x's size. A zero x, or one whose exponent\nbyte is below 11, gives exponent byte 0 (1E-64)."},
        "1426": {"comment":"Read the argument \"( x )\""},
        "1427": {"comment":"x zero? (Z = yes; rewritten as integer 0)"},
        "1429": {"comment":"Zero: exponent byte 0"},
        "1431": {"comment":"x is 0?"},
        "1434": {"comment":"Float form"},
        "1435": {"comment":"A = its exponent byte"},
        "1437": {"comment":"Drop the sign"},
        "1439": {"comment":"Ten digits below x's exponent"},
        "1441": {"comment":"Not below 0?"},
        "1444": {"comment":"Below 0: exponent byte 0"},
        "1445": {"synopsis":"Replaces the top number by 1.0 with exponent byte A (sign clear).","comment":"Keep the exponent byte"},
        "1447": {"comment":"Replace x by 1.0"},
        "1450": {"comment":"Top number"},
        "1454": {"comment":"Its exponent byte"},
        "1458": {"synopsis":"EXSTRING$ function (keyword entry): reads \"( n )\", builds error n's text with ERR_TEXT_BUILD\n(length at $0446, text from $0447), makes room for it and pushes the text as a string."},
        "1459": {"comment":"Read the argument \"( x )\""},
        "1460": {"comment":"HL = n"},
        "1461": {"comment":"Error n's text to $0446"},
        "1463": {"comment":"The message buffer: length, then text"},
        "1467": {"comment":"DE = its length"},
        "1472": {"comment":"Room for the text and its two bytes"},
        "1474": {"comment":"BC = length"},
        "1476": {"comment":"HL = the text's last character"},
        "1477": {"comment":"The length byte too"},
        "1478": {"comment":"Copy below the FP stack's top"},
        "1483": {"comment":"Copy text and length byte downwards"},
        "1486": {"comment":"Type 3 below the length"},
        "1488": {"comment":"The new top"},
        "1492": {"synopsis":"EXLINE function (keyword entry): pushes the number of the program line where the last error\nhappened: ($023E) is that line's address; when it is the line buffer $0248 (a typed command)\nthe result is 0.\nEXTYPE's entry ($05E6) is inside the LD IY,($023C) here: it loads HL from ($023C), the last\nerror's number, and pushes it.","comment":"Address of the line where the last error happened"},
        "1495": {"comment":"The line buffer (a typed command)?"},
        "1501": {"comment":"Yes: EXLINE is 0"},
        "1503": {"comment":"Back to the line's address"},
        "1505": {"comment":"Its line number (+1, +2)"},
        "1508": {"comment":"HL = line number"},
        "1509": {"comment":"EXTYPE enters at $05E6: LD HL,($023C), the last error"},
        "1513": {"synopsis":"Pushes HL as an integer and returns (EXLINE and EXTYPE)."},
        "1514": {"comment":"Push HL"},
        "1517": {"synopsis":"EXP function (keyword entry): reads \"( x )\" and falls into FP_EXP."},
        "1520": {"synopsis":"e to the power of the top number (call byte $A7).\n1. n = INT(x * 2/ln 10). A float n (too big for an integer) means overflow (error 1002) when\n   positive and the result 0 when negative; so do n >= 126 and n < -126.\n2. r = x - n * ln 10/2 (the constant in two parts, $24 and $25, for precision), so that e^x\n   = 10^(n/2) * e^r.\n3. e^r = (Q + P)/(Q - P) with P = r((c28 r^2 + c27) r^2 + c26) and Q = (r^2 + c2A) r^2 + c29\n   (constants $26-$2A); kept in R1.\n4. For an odd n R1 is multiplied by 0.316227766017 (10^-0.5) and n made even; then n/2 is\n   added to R1's exponent byte and R1 is pushed by FP_PUSH_R1.\nError 1002 \"Overflow in numeric expression\"."},
        "1521": {"comment":"Keep x"},
        "1522": {"comment":"Push a constant"},
        "1523": {"comment":"Constant $23: 2/ln 10 = 0.868588963807"},
        "1524": {"comment":"x * 2/ln 10"},
        "1525": {"comment":"n = INT(that)"},
        "1526": {"comment":"A = n's exponent byte; integer form?"},
        "1528": {"comment":"Integer form: n fits"},
        "1530": {"comment":"Too big: positive?"},
        "1531": {"comment":"Error 1002: Overflow in numeric expression"},
        "1534": {"synopsis":"Underflow: replaces x by 0 and returns."},
        "1535": {"comment":"Drop n"},
        "1536": {"comment":"x becomes 0"},
        "1539": {"synopsis":"x * 2/ln 10 fitted an integer n (DE): checks -126 <= n < 126, then computes e^r for the\nremainder (step 2 and 3 of FP_EXP).","comment":"The integer n's value at +2/+3"},
        "1547": {"comment":"HL = n"},
        "1549": {"comment":"n + 126"},
        "1553": {"comment":"n < -126?"},
        "1555": {"comment":"Yes: the result is 0"},
        "1558": {"comment":"n + 126 - 252"},
        "1563": {"comment":"n >= 126: error 1002"},
        "1566": {"comment":"Keep n"},
        "1568": {"comment":"R2 = n"},
        "1569": {"comment":"n"},
        "1570": {"comment":"Push a constant"},
        "1571": {"comment":"Constant $24: 1.151, ln 10/2's high part"},
        "1572": {"comment":"n * 1.151"},
        "1573": {"comment":"x - n * 1.151"},
        "1574": {"comment":"n"},
        "1575": {"comment":"Push a constant"},
        "1576": {"comment":"Constant $25: 2.92546497023E-4, its low part"},
        "1577": {"comment":"n * 2.925E-4"},
        "1578": {"comment":"r = x - n * ln 10/2"},
        "1579": {"comment":"r, r"},
        "1580": {"comment":"r, r, r"},
        "1581": {"comment":"r, r^2"},
        "1582": {"comment":"R1 = r^2"},
        "1583": {"comment":"r^2"},
        "1584": {"comment":"Push a constant"},
        "1585": {"comment":"Constant $2A: 112.094081097"},
        "1586": {"comment":"r^2 + c2A"},
        "1587": {"comment":"r^2"},
        "1588": {"comment":"(r^2 + c2A) r^2"},
        "1589": {"comment":"Push a constant"},
        "1590": {"comment":"Constant $29: 1008.92977901"},
        "1591": {"comment":"+ c29"},
        "1592": {"comment":"R2 = Q"},
        "1593": {"comment":"Push a constant"},
        "1594": {"comment":"Constant $28: 0.0332873646516"},
        "1595": {"comment":"r^2"},
        "1596": {"comment":"c28 r^2"},
        "1597": {"comment":"Push a constant"},
        "1598": {"comment":"Constant $27: 14.0082997563"},
        "1599": {"comment":"+ c27"},
        "1600": {"comment":"r^2"},
        "1601": {"comment":"* r^2"},
        "1602": {"comment":"Push a constant"},
        "1603": {"comment":"Constant $26: 504.464889506"},
        "1604": {"comment":"+ c26"},
        "1605": {"comment":"P = r * that"},
        "1606": {"comment":"R1 = P"},
        "1607": {"comment":"P"},
        "1608": {"comment":"Q"},
        "1609": {"comment":"P"},
        "1610": {"comment":"Q - P"},
        "1611": {"comment":"P/(Q - P)"},
        "1612": {"comment":"Push a constant"},
        "1613": {"comment":"Constant 0: 0.5"},
        "1614": {"comment":"0.5 + P/(Q - P)"},
        "1615": {"comment":"Twice that:"},
