        "1674": {"comment":"Constant 2: 9.999999999E62"},
        "1677": {"synopsis":"FREE function (call byte $A1, keyword entry): pushes the free memory in bytes.\n1. Moves the BASIC stack down onto the variables (cartridge byte $29), so that the room left\n   is from the stack's bottom ($0226) to the end of its 16K page.\n2. Adds what EXOS can still give (EXOS 24's DE: $4000 for a free segment, or the boundary of\n   a shared one), each allocated and freed again: nothing when a segment slot is tagged\n   (ix+$0A) + $80, one segment when one is tagged (ix+$0A), else up to two.\n3. Pushes the total as (total - 32767) + 32767, so that a sum over 32767 still makes a\n   number."},
        "1678": {"comment":"Move the BASIC stack down onto the variables"},
        "1680": {"comment":"The stack's bottom byte"},
        "1684": {"comment":"Total so far: 0"},
        "1688": {"comment":"IS-BASIC's segment tag"},
        "1692": {"comment":"Tag + $80"},
        "1695": {"comment":"A slot tagged (ix+$0A) + $80? (carry: none)"},
        "1698": {"comment":"A slot tagged + $80: no more segments"},
        "1701": {"comment":"A slot tagged (ix+$0A)? (carry: none)"},
        "1703": {"comment":"Already one segment: measure one more"},
        "1705": {"comment":"Allocate one segment (SEG_ALLOC)"},
        "1708": {"comment":"None to be had?"},
        "1711": {"comment":"Total + its size"},
        "1715": {"comment":"Measure one more"},
        "1720": {"comment":"Free the first again (SEG_FREE)"},
        "1724": {"comment":"Skip the next call"},
        "1725": {"synopsis":"One segment is already IS-BASIC's: measures one more."},
        "1728": {"comment":"Total + the size measured"},
        "1731": {"synopsis":"Adds the room from ($0226) to the end of its page and pushes the total.","comment":"Total"},
        "1732": {"comment":"HL = ($0226), total kept on the stack"},
        "1733": {"comment":"Offset in its 16K page"},
        "1739": {"comment":"$3FFF - offset: room to the page's end"},
        "1742": {"comment":"Plus the total"},
        "1744": {"comment":"32767"},
        "1748": {"comment":"Total - 32767 (fits an integer)"},
        "1751": {"comment":"Push total - 32767"},
        "1753": {"comment":"32767"},
        "1755": {"comment":"Push 32767"},
        "1756": {"comment":"The total"},
        "1759": {"synopsis":"Allocates a segment with SEG_ALLOC and frees it again.\nExit: DE = its usable size (EXOS 24's DE), 0 if none was given.","comment":"Allocate a segment"},
        "1762": {"comment":"None?"},
        "1765": {"comment":"Its size"},
        "1766": {"comment":"Free it again"},
        "1771": {"synopsis":"No segment: DE = 0."},
        "1775": {"synopsis":"HEX$ function (keyword entry): reads \"( s$ )\" through UCASE$ ($0D25) and turns its hex\nnumbers, separated by commas, into a string of those bytes (\"41,42\" gives \"AB\"), built at\n$0347 and copied over the argument. A character neither a hex digit nor a comma is error\n20000 \"Not understood\".","comment":"UCASE$'s routine: reads ( s$ ), upper case"},
