        "1912": {"synopsis":"INT of the top number (call byte $AE): rounds down. An integer form is left alone. For |x|\n>= 1 the digits after the point are cleared; a negative mantissa is cleared in ten's\ncomplement form, so it rounds down too. Results under five digits go back to the integer\nform ($0499). For |x| < 1 the result is 0, or -1 for a negative x."},
