        "2565": {"comment":"Read the byte from the asked segment"},
        "2566": {"comment":"Back to page 1's old segment"},
        "2567": {"comment":"Page 1 = its old segment again"},
        "2569": {"comment":"Push the byte as an integer"},
        "2571": {"synopsis":"PI function: pushes the constant pi (entry 4 of the constant table at $008C)."},
        "2572": {"comment":"Push a constant:"},
        "2573": {"comment":"Constant 4: pi"},
        "2576": {"synopsis":"POS function, POS(a$, b$[, n]): pushes the position of b$ in a$, searching from character n\n(1 when n is not given), or 0 when b$ is not found. An empty b$ gives n.\n1. Reads the two strings (b$ ends on top) and the optional start, then sets IY = a$ at\n   character n, DE = b$'s text, C = b$'s length, H = the position tried and L = the\n   characters of a$ left.\n2. At each position compares b$ with a$ character by character; a mismatch moves one\n   character on and tries again.\n3. Drops both strings and pushes the position as an integer.\nThe count of characters left is not restored after a partial match, so a match that follows\na partial one near the end can be missed: POS(\"aab\",\"ab\") and POS(\"aaab\",\"ab\") give 0 (run)."},
        "2577": {"comment":"Expect ( and the first string argument (a$)"},
        "2578": {"comment":"Expect , and the second string argument (b$)"},
        "2580": {"comment":"Is a third argument coming?"},
        "2583": {"comment":"Symbol $0C: \",\""},
        "2585": {"comment":"Start at character 1 by default"},
        "2590": {"comment":"Expect , and the start position"},
        "2591": {"comment":"Pop it into HL as an integer"},
        "2593": {"synopsis":"Expects \")\" and sets up the search (see FN_POS).","comment":"Expect \")\""},
        "2596": {"comment":"DE = start position"},
        "2599": {"comment":"HL = b$'s item on top of the stack"},
        "2603": {"comment":"BC = b$'s length"},
        "2606": {"comment":"DE = start - 1"},
        "2607": {"comment":"Keep b$'s text address"},
        "2608": {"comment":"Past b$: a$'s item comes next"},
        "2610": {"comment":"A = a$'s length"},
        "2612": {"comment":"IY = a$'s text at the start position"},
        "2616": {"comment":"L = characters of a$ left from the start"},
        "2622": {"comment":"H = the position tried"},
        "2623": {"comment":"DE = b$'s text"},
        "2624": {"comment":"1: do not count down before the first try"},
        "2626": {"synopsis":"Tries a match at position H: keeps the counts and pointers, then compares b$ with a$ from\nIY.","comment":"Keep b$'s length, b$'s text, a$'s place, H/L"},
        "2631": {"comment":"All of b$ matched?"},
        "2632": {"synopsis":"Counts one character of b$ matched; all of b$ matched is a find, no character of a$ left a\nmiss."},
        "2635": {"comment":"One character of a$ fewer (none when A = 1)"},
        "2638": {"comment":"None left: not found"},
        "2640": {"comment":"Position counter on"},
        "2641": {"comment":"Same character?"},
        "2648": {"comment":"Yes: compare the next one"},
        "2650": {"comment":"Mismatch: A = the position this try began at"},
        "2652": {"comment":"Restore a$'s place, b$'s text and length"},
        "2656": {"comment":"Try one character further on in a$"},
        "2659": {"comment":"A = 0: count the character skipped"},
        "2662": {"synopsis":"b$ matched at the position this try began at: L = that position.","comment":"H = the position this try began at"},
        "2664": {"comment":"L = that position"},
        "2665": {"synopsis":"Drops the two strings and pushes L (the position, or 0) as an integer; discards the four\nsaved words.","comment":"HL = the result"},
        "2669": {"comment":"Drop b$"},
        "2670": {"comment":"Drop a$"},
        "2674": {"comment":"Push HL as an integer"},
        "2676": {"comment":"Discard the four words saved for the try"},
