        "2746": {"comment":"Add: 65536"},
        "2747": {"comment":"Divide"},
        "2750": {"synopsis":"RND(n): pushes a random integer from 0 to n-1; error 1000 when n is not 1-32767.\nCounts the shifts that bring n's top bit to bit 15, takes random values shifted right that\nmany times (below twice n's top bit) and draws again while one is above n-1."},
        "2751": {"comment":"Read the ( numeric argument )"},
        "2752": {"comment":"Pop it into HL as an integer (n)"},
        "2754": {"comment":"Negative?"},
        "2756": {"comment":"Error 1000: Unexpected value given"},
        "2759": {"comment":"Zero?"},
        "2764": {"comment":"Keep n"},
        "2765": {"comment":"Count the shifts from 0"},
        "2766": {"synopsis":"Counts in A the left shifts of n until its top set bit reaches bit 15 (one more than\nneeded)."},
        "2768": {"comment":"Reached bit 15?"},
        "2773": {"comment":"HL = n - 1, the largest value wanted"},
        "2774": {"synopsis":"Draws a random value, shifts it into range and draws again while it is above n - 1."},
        "2777": {"comment":"Step the random generator: HL = new value"},
        "2780": {"comment":"B = shifts"},
        "2781": {"synopsis":"Shifts the random value right B times."},
        "2787": {"comment":"DE = the random value"},
        "2788": {"comment":"HL = n - 1"},
        "2790": {"comment":"Above n - 1?"},
        "2793": {"comment":"Yes: draw again"},
        "2796": {"synopsis":"Pushes HL as an integer and returns: RND(n)'s end, and the return address FN_USR leaves for\nthe machine code it calls.\nEntry: HL = the value."},
        "2797": {"comment":"Push HL as an integer"},
        "2800": {"synopsis":"ROUND function, ROUND(x, n): rounds x to n digits after the decimal point (n negative rounds\nto tens, hundreds ...).\n1. Zero stays zero; otherwise A = the digits before the point plus n, the digits to keep.\n2. No digit to keep gives 0 ($033E); otherwise FP_ROUND_DIGITS rounds the mantissa to A\n   digits.\n3. When n is 0 or negative the result is a whole number and goes to integer form when it has\n   fewer than 5 digits ($049A)."},
        "2801": {"comment":"Expect ( and the first numeric argument (x)"},
        "2802": {"comment":"Expect , and the next numeric argument (n)"},
        "2803": {"comment":"Expect )"},
        "2804": {"comment":"Pop it into HL as an integer (n)"},
        "2805": {"comment":"Is x zero?"},
        "2807": {"comment":"Zero stays zero"},
        "2810": {"comment":"Into float form"},
        "2811": {"comment":"A = the exponent byte"},
        "2813": {"comment":"Without the sign"},
        "2815": {"comment":"Digits before the decimal point"},
        "2818": {"comment":"Plus n: the digits to keep"},
        "2819": {"comment":"None: the result is 0"},
        "2826": {"comment":"Round to A digits"},
        "2830": {"comment":"n zero?"},
        "2834": {"comment":"n positive: leave it a float"},
        "2835": {"synopsis":"A whole result: A = its digits; $049A turns it into integer form when fewer than 5. TRUNCATE\nends the same way.","comment":"A = the result's digits"},
        "2836": {"comment":"Integer form when it is short enough"},
        "2839": {"synopsis":"Rounds the top number's mantissa to A significant digits: digit A+1 of 5 or more adds one to\ndigit A (carrying through 9s, up to the overflow digits), and every digit after A is\ncleared; then normalises.\nEntry: A = digits to keep (1-11).\nExit: A kept.\nChanges: B."},
        "2840": {"comment":"Ten's complement of a negative mantissa"},
        "2844": {"comment":"Position of the first digit dropped (4 is the leading one)"},
        "2848": {"comment":"Get the digit at position B"},
        "2851": {"comment":"5 or more?"},
        "2853": {"comment":"No: just clear the rest"},
        "2857": {"comment":"Position of the last digit kept"},
        "2858": {"synopsis":"Adds one at digit B: a 9 becomes 0 and the carry moves one digit up."},
        "2859": {"comment":"Get the digit at position B"},
        "2861": {"comment":"A 9?"},
        "2865": {"comment":"9 + 1: write 0"},
        "2867": {"comment":"Put the digit at position B"},
        "2869": {"comment":"Carry one digit up"},
        "2871": {"comment":"Still a digit position (2 or above)?"},
        "2877": {"synopsis":"Writes the digit plus one at position B."},
        "2879": {"comment":"Put the digit at position B"},
        "2881": {"synopsis":"Clears every digit from the first dropped one to position 15."},
        "2883": {"comment":"B = the first digit dropped"},
        "2884": {"synopsis":"Writes 0 at position B, for B up to 15."},
        "2886": {"comment":"Put the digit at position B"},
        "2890": {"comment":"Past the last position?"},
        "2895": {"comment":"Undo the ten's complement"},
        "2896": {"comment":"Normalise"},
