        "3082": {"synopsis":"SIZE function, SIZE(array[, d]): pushes the array's element count, or with d (1 or 2) the\nsize of dimension d; error 4004 when d is outside the array's dimensions.\nThe array's value field holds the dimension count at +0 and the element count at +1, then 12\nbytes per dimension: the lower bound at +7 (+19) and the size at +13 (+25), 6-byte numbers.","comment":"Expect ( and an array: HL = its value field"},
        "3085": {"comment":"Is a dimension given?"},
