        "3154": {"synopsis":"Square root of the top number (not negative).\n1. Zero stays zero. Otherwise the number goes to R1 with exponent byte $3F (a mantissa m in\n   [0.1, 1)), and A = the exponent taken off.\n2. Starts from 0.894427*m + 0.223607 in R2 and makes 4 Newton steps g = g + (m/g - g)/2.\n3. An odd exponent multiplies the root by 0.316227766017 (1/sqrt 10) and rounds it up; half\n   of it is added to R2's exponent, and R2 is pushed.\nChanges: R1, R2."},
        "3155": {"comment":"Into float form"},
        "3156": {"comment":"Is it zero?"},
        "3158": {"comment":"Zero stays zero"},
        "3159": {"comment":"Pop it into R1"},
        "3162": {"comment":"R1's exponent byte"},
        "3165": {"comment":"A = the exponent above $3F"},
        "3169": {"comment":"R1 = m, in [0.1, 1)"},
        "3172": {"comment":"Push R1 (m)"},
        "3173": {"comment":"Push a constant:"},
        "3174": {"comment":"Constant $0C: 0.894427"},
        "3175": {"comment":"Multiply"},
        "3176": {"comment":"Push a constant:"},
        "3177": {"comment":"Constant $0B: 0.223607"},
        "3178": {"comment":"Add"},
        "3179": {"comment":"Pop it into R2: the first guess"},
        "3181": {"comment":"4 Newton steps"},
        "3183": {"synopsis":"One Newton step: R2 = R2 + (R1/R2 - R2) * 0.5."},
        "3185": {"comment":"Push R2 (g)"},
        "3186": {"comment":"Push R1 (m)"},
        "3187": {"comment":"Push R2 (g)"},
        "3188": {"comment":"Divide: m / g"},
        "3189": {"comment":"Push R2 (g)"},
        "3190": {"comment":"Subtract: m/g - g"},
        "3191": {"comment":"Push a constant:"},
        "3192": {"comment":"Constant 0: 0.5"},
        "3193": {"comment":"Multiply"},
        "3194": {"comment":"Add g"},
        "3195": {"comment":"Pop it into R2"},
        "3200": {"comment":"A = the exponent taken off"},
        "3201": {"comment":"Odd?"},
        "3207": {"comment":"Push R2 (the root)"},
        "3208": {"comment":"Push a constant:"},
        "3209": {"comment":"Constant $0D: 0.316227766017"},
        "3210": {"comment":"Multiply"},
        "3211": {"comment":"Pop it into R2"},
        "3214": {"comment":"Make the exponent even"},
        "3215": {"synopsis":"Adds half of the exponent taken off to R2's exponent byte and pushes R2 (FP_PUSH_R2).","comment":"Half of it"},
        "3217": {"comment":"R2's exponent byte"},
        "3224": {"comment":"Push R2: the result"},
        "3227": {"synopsis":"TAN function: reads its argument, turns it into radians and falls into FP_TAN."},
        "3228": {"comment":"Read the ( numeric argument )"},
        "3229": {"comment":"Into radians when OPTION ANGLE DEGREES"},
        "3231": {"synopsis":"Tangent of the top number, in radians: sin(x) / sin(x + pi/2).\nChanges: R1, R2."},
        "3232": {"comment":"Duplicate x"},
        "3233": {"comment":"Pop it into R2"},
        "3234": {"comment":"Sine of x"},
        "3235": {"comment":"Push R2 (x)"},
        "3236": {"comment":"Push a constant:"},
        "3237": {"comment":"Constant 7: pi/2"},
        "3238": {"comment":"Add"},
        "3239": {"comment":"Sine of x + pi/2"},
        "3240": {"comment":"Divide"},
        "3243": {"synopsis":"TANH function: (e^x - e^-x) / (e^x + e^-x).\nChanges: R1, R2."},
        "3244": {"comment":"Read the ( numeric argument )"},
        "3245": {"comment":"e to the x"},
        "3246": {"comment":"Duplicate it"},
        "3247": {"comment":"1 / e^x"},
        "3248": {"comment":"Pop e^-x into R1"},
        "3249": {"comment":"Pop e^x into R2"},
        "3250": {"comment":"Push R2 (e^x)"},
        "3251": {"comment":"Push R1 (e^-x)"},
        "3252": {"comment":"Subtract"},
        "3253": {"comment":"Push R2 (e^x)"},
        "3254": {"comment":"Push R1 (e^-x)"},
        "3255": {"comment":"Add"},
        "3256": {"comment":"Divide"},
        "3259": {"synopsis":"TRUNCATE function, TRUNCATE(x, n): cuts x after n digits behind the decimal point (n\nnegative cuts tens, hundreds ...): every mantissa digit after them is cleared, so the result\nmoves toward zero. A whole result goes to integer form as in ROUND."},
        "3260": {"comment":"Expect ( and the first numeric argument (x)"},
        "3261": {"comment":"Into float form"},
        "3262": {"comment":"Expect , and the next numeric argument (n)"},
        "3263": {"comment":"Expect )"},
        "3264": {"comment":"Pop it into HL as an integer (n)"},
        "3265": {"comment":"A = x's exponent byte"},
        "3267": {"comment":"Without the sign"},
        "3269": {"comment":"Digits before the decimal point"},
        "3271": {"comment":"Plus n: the digits to keep"},
        "3272": {"comment":"None: the result is 0"},
        "3280": {"comment":"Position of the first digit dropped"},
        "3283": {"synopsis":"Writes 0 at mantissa position B, for B up to 15.","comment":"Digit 0"},
        "3285": {"comment":"Put the digit at position B"},
        "3289": {"comment":"Past the last position?"},
        "3295": {"comment":"n zero?"},
        "3299": {"comment":"n positive: leave it a float"},
        "3300": {"synopsis":"A whole result: A = its digits; $049A turns it into integer form when fewer than 5.","comment":"A = the result's digits"},
        "3301": {"comment":"Integer form when it is short enough"},
        "3304": {"synopsis":"UBOUND function, UBOUND(array[, d]): pushes the upper bound of dimension d (1 when not\ngiven), lower bound + size - 1; error 4009 when d is outside the array's dimensions.","comment":"Expect ( and an array: HL = its value field"},
        "3308": {"comment":"Is a dimension given?"},
        "3311": {"comment":"Symbol $0C: \",\""},
        "3313": {"comment":"Dimension 1 by default"},
        "3318": {"comment":"Expect , and the next numeric argument (d)"},
        "3319": {"comment":"Pop it into HL as an integer"},
        "3321": {"comment":"E = d"},
        "3322": {"synopsis":"Expects \")\" and checks d against the array's dimension count.","comment":"Expect \")\""},
        "3326": {"comment":"d - 1"},
        "3328": {"comment":"Error 4009: Index to UBOUND out of range"},
        "3331": {"comment":"More than the array's dimensions?"},
        "3332": {"comment":"Error 4009: Index to UBOUND out of range"},
        "3335": {"comment":"HL = +1"},
        "3336": {"comment":"+7: dimension 1's lower bound"},
        "3341": {"comment":"Dimension 1?"},
        "3343": {"comment":"+19: dimension 2's lower bound"},
        "3345": {"synopsis":"Pushes the lower bound at HL and the size 6 bytes on, adds them and subtracts 1."},
        "3348": {"comment":"Push the lower bound (6-byte number at HL)"},
        "3352": {"comment":"6 bytes on: the dimension's size"},
        "3354": {"comment":"Push the size (6-byte number at HL)"},
        "3355": {"comment":"Add"},
        "3361": {"comment":"Push HL (1) as an integer"},
        "3362": {"comment":"Subtract 1"},
        "3365": {"synopsis":"UCASE$ function (B = $60: a-z made upper case). LCASE$ enters at $0D28, inside the next\ninstruction, with B = $40 (A-Z made lower case). Reads the string argument and falls into\nSTR_CASE_FLIP.","comment":"Letters after $60: a-z"},
        "3367": {"comment":"LCASE$ enters at $0D28: LD B,$40 (A-Z)"},
        "3371": {"comment":"Read the ( string argument )"},
        "3375": {"synopsis":"Flips bit 5 of every character of the top string that lies in B+1 to B+26 (cartridge routine\n$26 with A = B).\nEntry: B = $60 (to upper case) or $40 (to lower case).\nChanges: A, C, E, HL.","comment":"HL = the string's length byte"},
        "3379": {"comment":"E = its length"},
        "3380": {"comment":"Empty?"},
        "3381": {"synopsis":"Counts the characters down; returns after the last one.","comment":"One character fewer: none left?"},
        "3383": {"comment":"Next character"},
        "3384": {"comment":"A = the range's base"},
        "3386": {"comment":"C = the character, bit 5 flipped when in range"},
        "3388": {"comment":"Store it back"},
        "3391": {"synopsis":"USR function, USR(address, value): calls the machine code at address with HL = value, and\npushes the HL it returns as an integer (its RET goes to INT_RESULT_PUSH). The code runs with\nsegment 1 in page 3.","comment":"Run address of INT_RESULT_PUSH"},
        "3394": {"comment":"The code returns there"},
        "3396": {"comment":"Expect ( and the first numeric argument (address)"},
        "3397": {"comment":"Pop it into HL as an integer"},
        "3399": {"comment":"The code's address: RET goes there"},
        "3401": {"comment":"Expect , and the next numeric argument (value)"},
        "3402": {"comment":"Expect )"},
        "3403": {"comment":"Pop it into HL as an integer"},
        "3405": {"comment":"Jump to the code with HL = value"},
        "3406": {"synopsis":"VAL function: reads a number from the start of its string argument with the cartridge's\nnumber reader (blanks skipped first) and pushes it; text after the number is ignored. The\ntoken reader's pointer ($0214) is kept and restored.","comment":"Read the ( string argument )"},
        "3409": {"comment":"Keep the text pointer"},
        "3413": {"comment":"The string on the stack's top"},
        "3417": {"comment":"Past its type and length bytes"},
        "3418": {"comment":"Read from the string's text"},
        "3422": {"comment":"Skip blanks"},
        "3423": {"comment":"Read a number into $0595"},
        "3424": {"comment":"Drop the string"},
        "3425": {"comment":"Push the number read"},
        "3427": {"comment":"Restore the text pointer"},
        "3432": {"synopsis":"VER$ function: pushes the 66 bytes of VER_TEXT as a string (copied with LDDR below the\nstack's top, then length $42 and type 3).","comment":"DE = the byte below the stack's top"},
        "3437": {"comment":"Run address of VER_TEXT's last byte"},
        "3440": {"comment":"66 bytes"},
        "3443": {"comment":"Copy the text below the stack's top"},
        "3446": {"comment":"Length 66"},
        "3449": {"comment":"Type 3: a string"},
        "3451": {"comment":"The new top of the stack"},
        "3455": {"synopsis":"VER$'s text, 66 bytes read by FN_VER: \"Enterprise IS-BASIC version 2.1\", CR LF, byte $80 (the character the start-up banner also puts before \"1985\"), \" 1985 Intelligent Software Ltd\", CR LF."},
        "3521": {"synopsis":"VERNUM function: pushes the 7-byte number VERNUM_VALUE (2.1) through FP_PUSH_HL.","comment":"Run address of VERNUM_VALUE"},
        "3524": {"comment":"Push it"},
        "3527": {"synopsis":"VERNUM's number in the 7-byte stored form: mantissa bytes 00 00 00 00 00 21 and exponent\n$40, the value 2.1 (run: PRINT VERNUM shows 2.1)."},
        "3534": {"synopsis":"WORD$ function (entry from the function table at FN_NAME_TABLE): reads \"( n )\", takes n as a\n16-bit integer and pushes a 2-character string of its low byte, then its high byte. No room\ncheck before the 4-byte push.\nExit: the string on the BASIC stack, ($0228) lowered by 4.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"WORD$: read the argument, pop it into HL"},
        "3535": {"comment":"$99 ARG_NUM_PAREN: read \"( numeric expression )\""},
        "3536": {"comment":"$0B: pop it into HL as a 16-bit integer"},
        "3537": {"comment":"End of the list"},
        "3538": {"comment":"DE = the word"},
        "3539": {"comment":"Top of the BASIC stack"},
        "3543": {"comment":"High byte is the second character"},
        "3545": {"comment":"Low byte the first"},
        "3547": {"comment":"Length 2"},
        "3550": {"comment":"Type 3: a string"},
        "3552": {"comment":"The new top"},
        "3556": {"synopsis":"Function-name table: the 76 built-in functions (ABS ... WORD$, alphabetical except WORD$\nlast) that FN_TABLE_INSTALL ($0261) copies into IS-BASIC's name table. Each entry is a flags\nbyte ($0C a numeric function, $0D a string one: bit 0 string, bit 2 declared, bit 3\nbuilt-in), the name's length n, the n characters, and the routine's run address (low byte\nfirst): n + 4 bytes. A 0 flags byte ends the table (at $104B). The copy puts a link word\nbefore each entry and a segment byte 1 after it.","comment":"ABS: numeric function, routine at offset $0321"},
        "3563": {"comment":"ACOS: numeric function, routine at offset $0326"},
        "3571": {"comment":"ANGLE: numeric function, routine at offset $0330"},
        "3580": {"comment":"ASIN: numeric function, routine at offset $0362"},
        "3588": {"comment":"ATN: numeric function, routine at offset $0426"},
        "3595": {"comment":"BIN: numeric function, routine at offset $042C"},
        "3602": {"comment":"BLACK: numeric function, routine at offset $04FA"},
        "3611": {"comment":"BLUE: numeric function, routine at offset $0500"},
        "3619": {"comment":"CEIL: numeric function, routine at offset $045D"},
        "3627": {"comment":"CHR$: string function, routine at offset $04A2"},
        "3635": {"comment":"COS: numeric function, routine at offset $0514"},
        "3642": {"comment":"COSH: numeric function, routine at offset $051F"},
        "3650": {"comment":"COT: numeric function, routine at offset $052A"},
        "3657": {"comment":"CSC: numeric function, routine at offset $0A8B"},
        "3664": {"comment":"CYAN: numeric function, routine at offset $0509"},
        "3672": {"comment":"DATE$: string function, routine at offset $0543"},
        "3681": {"comment":"DEG: numeric function, routine at offset $057F"},
        "3688": {"comment":"EPS: numeric function, routine at offset $0591"},
        "3695": {"comment":"EXLINE: numeric function, routine at offset $05D4"},
        "3705": {"comment":"EXP: numeric function, routine at offset $05ED"},
        "3712": {"comment":"EXSTRING$: string function, routine at offset $05B2"},
        "3725": {"comment":"EXTYPE: numeric function, routine at offset $05E6"},
        "3735": {"comment":"FREE: numeric function, routine at offset $068D"},
        "3743": {"comment":"FP: numeric function, routine at offset $067B"},
        "3749": {"comment":"GREEN: numeric function, routine at offset $0503"},
        "3758": {"comment":"HEX$: string function, routine at offset $06EF"},
        "3766": {"comment":"IN: numeric function, routine at offset $0746"},
        "3772": {"comment":"INKEY$: string function, routine at offset $0758"},
        "3782": {"comment":"INF: numeric function, routine at offset $0688"},
        "3789": {"comment":"INT: numeric function, routine at offset $0775"},
        "3796": {"comment":"IP: numeric function, routine at offset $081B"},
        "3802": {"comment":"JOY: numeric function, routine at offset $0831"},
        "3809": {"comment":"LBOUND: numeric function, routine at offset $084C"},
        "3819": {"comment":"LCASE$: string function, routine at offset $0D28"},
        "3829": {"comment":"LEN: numeric function, routine at offset $087F"},
        "3836": {"comment":"LOG: numeric function, routine at offset $089B"},
        "3843": {"comment":"LOG2: numeric function, routine at offset $0892"},
        "3851": {"comment":"LOG10: numeric function, routine at offset $08A4"},
        "3860": {"comment":"LTRIM$: string function, routine at offset $0912"},
        "3870": {"comment":"MAGENTA: numeric function, routine at offset $050C"},
        "3881": {"comment":"MAX: numeric function, routine at offset $092D"},
        "3888": {"comment":"MAXLEN: numeric function, routine at offset $0942"},
        "3898": {"comment":"MIN: numeric function, routine at offset $096F"},
        "3905": {"comment":"MOD: numeric function, routine at offset $0984"},
        "3912": {"comment":"ORD: numeric function, routine at offset $09B5"},
        "3919": {"comment":"PEEK: numeric function, routine at offset $09CE"},
        "3927": {"comment":"SPEEK: numeric function, routine at offset $09E7"},
        "3936": {"comment":"PI: numeric function, routine at offset $0A0B"},
        "3942": {"comment":"POS: numeric function, routine at offset $0A10"},
        "3949": {"comment":"RAD: numeric function, routine at offset $0A79"},
        "3956": {"comment":"RED: numeric function, routine at offset $04FD"},
        "3963": {"comment":"REM: numeric function, routine at offset $0A96"},
        "3970": {"comment":"RGB: numeric function, routine at offset $04BB"},
        "3977": {"comment":"RND: numeric function, routine at offset $0AA9"},
        "3984": {"comment":"ROUND: numeric function, routine at offset $0AF0"},
        "3993": {"comment":"RTRIM$: string function, routine at offset $0B54"},
        "4003": {"comment":"SEC: numeric function, routine at offset $0B7C"},
        "4010": {"comment":"SIN: numeric function, routine at offset $0B82"},
        "4017": {"comment":"SINH: numeric function, routine at offset $0BEB"},
        "4025": {"comment":"SIZE: numeric function, routine at offset $0C0A"},
        "4033": {"comment":"SGN: numeric function, routine at offset $0BF6"},
        "4040": {"comment":"STR$: string function, routine at offset $0C30"},
        "4048": {"comment":"SQR: numeric function, routine at offset $0C4B"},
        "4055": {"comment":"TAN: numeric function, routine at offset $0C9B"},
        "4062": {"comment":"TANH: numeric function, routine at offset $0CAB"},
        "4070": {"comment":"TIME$: string function, routine at offset $0530"},
        "4079": {"comment":"TRUNCATE: numeric function, routine at offset $0CBB"},
        "4091": {"comment":"UBOUND: numeric function, routine at offset $0CE8"},
        "4101": {"comment":"UCASE$: string function, routine at offset $0D25"},
        "4111": {"comment":"USR: numeric function, routine at offset $0D3F"},
        "4118": {"comment":"VAL: numeric function, routine at offset $0D4E"},
        "4125": {"comment":"VER$: string function, routine at offset $0D68"},
        "4133": {"comment":"VERNUM: numeric function, routine at offset $0DC1"},
        "4143": {"comment":"WHITE: numeric function, routine at offset $050F"},
        "4152": {"comment":"YELLOW: numeric function, routine at offset $0506"},
        "4162": {"comment":"WORD$: string function, routine at offset $0DCE"},
        "4171": {"comment":"End of the table"},
        "4172": {"comment":"Unused"},
        "4173": {"synopsis":"Makes a new name entry at ($0234) for the current name (length (ix+3), text at ($0347)) with\nflags A, and links it at the head of its hash bucket ($0DCB + VAR_NAME_HASH). The entry is:\nlink word, flags, length, name; its value follows.\nEntry: A = flags.\nExit: HL = the value field, ($0234) = HL.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Keep the flags"},
        "4174": {"comment":"Room for the name"},
        "4180": {"comment":"BC = the name's bucket offset"},
        "4183": {"comment":"Hash heads in IS-BASIC's RAM"},
        "4187": {"comment":"The new entry goes at ($0234)"},
        "4191": {"comment":"BC = the old head, the head = the new entry"},
        "4196": {"comment":"The entry's link = the old head"},
        "4202": {"comment":"Flags"},
        "4204": {"comment":"Name length"},
        "4210": {"comment":"Copy the name from the token text"},
        "4218": {"comment":"($0234) past the name"},
        "4220": {"synopsis":"Writes a numeric variable's initial value, the six bytes 00 00 00 00 FF 7F, at ($0234) and\nmoves ($0234) past it (room checked first).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE; HL kept."},
        "4221": {"comment":"6 bytes of room"},
        "4226": {"comment":"Four zero bytes"},
        "4231": {"synopsis":"Loop: clears the four bytes."},
        "4236": {"comment":"Then $FF"},
        "4239": {"comment":"And $7F"},
        "4244": {"synopsis":"Reserves a string variable's value at ($0234): the maximum length C, the length byte $FF,\nthen C bytes (room for C checked first), and moves ($0234) past it.\nEntry: C = maximum length.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE; HL kept."},
        "4245": {"comment":"Room for C bytes"},
        "4254": {"comment":"Maximum length"},
        "4256": {"comment":"Length $FF"},
        "4259": {"comment":"Past the C characters"},
        "4262": {"synopsis":"Stores the new allocation end in ($0234) and returns with HL restored."},
        "4267": {"synopsis":"Declares the current name in this scope (NUMERIC/STRING/DIM): a new entry with flags type +\n4 (declared) and its initial value (a numeric one, or a string of 132 characters), then the\ndeclaring line's address ($0216) after it.\n1. Error 20030 \"Identifier expected\" unless the token is a name ($20 numeric, $40 string).\n2. Error 20041 \"Identifier declared twice\" if VAR_SCOPE_TEST finds it in this scope.\n3. VAR_NEW_ENTRY, the value, the word ($0216).\nExit: ($0234) past the entry.","comment":"Token class: $20 numeric name?"},
        "4275": {"comment":"A string name ($40)?"},
        "4277": {"comment":"Error 20030: Identifier expected"},
        "4280": {"synopsis":"The token is a name: is it free in this scope?","comment":"May it be declared here?"},
        "4283": {"comment":"Error 20041: Identifier declared twice"},
        "4288": {"comment":"Bit 0 = string ($40 -> 1, $20 -> 0)"},
        "4292": {"comment":"Bit 2: declared"},
        "4297": {"comment":"String?"},
        "4300": {"comment":"Numeric: its initial value"},
        "4303": {"comment":"Z: no string value"},
        "4304": {"synopsis":"A string gets a 132-character value; then the declaring line is stored.","comment":"132 characters"},
        "4309": {"comment":"Room for a word"},
        "4312": {"comment":"The declaring line"},
        "4316": {"synopsis":"Stores DE at ($0234) and moves ($0234) past it."},
        "4323": {"synopsis":"Stores HL as the new ($0234)."},
        "4327": {"synopsis":"Creates an entry for the current name with flags from the name token's class in ($0202) (bit\n0 for a string; not declared) and its initial value: numeric, or a string of 132 characters.\nExit: HL = the entry's start.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE."},
        "4330": {"comment":"HL = where the entry goes"},
        "4335": {"comment":"Bit 0 = string"},
        "4344": {"comment":"Numeric name?"},
        "4349": {"comment":"A string of 132 characters"},
        "4353": {"synopsis":"Declares the current name as a reference: an entry with flags A + bit 4 whose value is the\nword HL, the address of the real value. Error 20041 \"Identifier declared twice\" if it is\nalready in this scope.\nEntry: A = flags, HL = the value's address.","comment":"The address the reference holds"},
        "4355": {"comment":"May it be declared here?"},
        "4358": {"comment":"Error 20041: Identifier declared twice"},
        "4362": {"comment":"Bit 4: a reference"},
        "4367": {"comment":"Room for the word"},
        "4370": {"comment":"Store the address as the value"},
        "4373": {"synopsis":"Asks for room for 2 bytes; falls into VAR_ROOM_CHECK."},
        "4375": {"synopsis":"Makes sure E bytes (and $40 spare) fit above ($0234): sets ($0238), the top of the variable\narea, to ($0234) + E + $40 and has the cartridge check it against the BASIC stack (error\n5000 \"Insufficient memory\" there).\nEntry: E = bytes.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL."},
        "4381": {"comment":"And $40 spare"},
        "4384": {"comment":"The variable area's new top"},
        "4387": {"comment":"Check the memory"},
        "4388": {"comment":"$27: room between the variables and the stack (cart MEM_ENSURE_12)"},
        "4389": {"comment":"End of the list"},
        "4391": {"synopsis":"Looks the current name (length ($0203), text at ($0347)) up in its hash bucket.\nExit: carry and HL = the entry when found; NC, Z and HL = 0 when not.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "4394": {"comment":"The name's bucket head"},
        "4398": {"synopsis":"Loop: follows the chain from the word at HL."},
        "4402": {"comment":"End of the chain?"},
        "4406": {"comment":"To the entry's length byte"},
        "4409": {"comment":"Same length?"},
        "4416": {"comment":"Compare the names"},
        "4421": {"synopsis":"Loop: compares the name a character at a time."},
        "4429": {"comment":"Found"},
        "4432": {"synopsis":"Not this one: on to the entry's link."},
        "4435": {"synopsis":"Says whether the current name may be declared in this scope.\nExit: carry when it may (not found, found below ($0236), the current scope's start, or found\nwith flag bit 3, a built-in function); NC when it is already declared in this scope. HL =\nthe entry (0 if not found).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE."},
        "4438": {"comment":"Start of the current scope"},
        "4443": {"comment":"Below it (or not found)?"},
        "4450": {"comment":"A built-in function name?"},
        "4453": {"comment":"NC: declared here already"},
        "4455": {"synopsis":"As VAR_FIND_ANY, but an entry with flag bit 3 (a built-in function) counts as missing, so a\nnew variable of that name is made.\nExit: HL = the value field, C = the flags (bit 4 cleared after following a reference)."},
        "4460": {"comment":"Not found?"},
        "4463": {"comment":"A built-in function?"},
        "4467": {"synopsis":"Missing: makes the entry, then reads its flags."},
        "4473": {"synopsis":"Steps past the length and the name to the value; a reference (bit 4) is followed."},
        "4474": {"comment":"E = the name length"},
        "4479": {"comment":"A reference?"},
        "4484": {"comment":"HL = the address it holds"},
        "4489": {"synopsis":"Finds the current name (making it with VAR_CREATE if missing).\nExit: HL = the value field, C = the flags; a reference (bit 4) is followed to the address it\nholds and bit 4 of C cleared.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE."},
        "4492": {"comment":"Missing: make it"},
        "4495": {"comment":"To the flags"},
        "4499": {"comment":"E = the name length"},
        "4504": {"comment":"A reference?"},
        "4509": {"comment":"HL = the address it holds"},
        "4514": {"synopsis":"Hashes the current name (length (ix+3), text at ($0347)): A is rotated left and XORed with\neach character, then ANDed with $3E.\nExit: BC = the bucket's offset (0-62, even) from the hash heads at $0DCB.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "4521": {"synopsis":"Loop: rotates and folds in each character."},
        "4526": {"comment":"32 buckets of 2 bytes"},
        "4530": {"synopsis":"Links the name entry at HL (length at +3, name at +4) at the head of its hash bucket;\nFN_TABLE_INSTALL calls it for every function. ($0347) is kept; ($0203) is left holding the\nlength.\nEntry: HL = the entry.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Keep the token text pointer"},
        "4535": {"comment":"DE = the entry"},
        "4540": {"comment":"Its name length as the token's"},
        "4545": {"comment":"And its name as the token text"},
        "4555": {"comment":"Old head in BC, the entry is the new head"},
        "4560": {"comment":"The entry's link = the old head"},
        "4564": {"comment":"Token text pointer back"},
        "4569": {"synopsis":"Forgets every name entry made after the mark ($021E): in each of the 32 hash buckets the\nhead is moved past the entries that lie above the mark (chains run newest first, so the rest\nis older).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"32 buckets"},
        "4574": {"synopsis":"Loop: one bucket."},
        "4575": {"synopsis":"Loop: steps along the chain while the entry is above the mark."},
        "4576": {"comment":"DE = the next entry"},
        "4579": {"comment":"Above the mark?"},
        "4586": {"comment":"The head = the first entry left"},
        "4591": {"comment":"Next bucket"},
        "4595": {"synopsis":"SET statement (call byte $B7). The forms:\n1. SET FKEY n string: programs function key n (1-16) with EXOS 11, special function 8\n   (@@FKEY) on channel 105 ($69).\n2. An option of SETOPT_TABLE that is an EXOS variable: SET option ON / OFF / n writes 0, 255\n   or n to it (EXOS 16).\n3. An option that is an escape sequence: ESC, its letter and its values are written to\n   channel 101/102 (or to ($0209) when Z on entry); missing values are sent as 0.\n4. Otherwise SET n, v writes v to EXOS variable n.\nEntry: B = the channel ($0209) is set to at the end; Z = send escape sequences to the\nchannel in ($0209).\nExit: ($0209) = B. EXOS errors are raised (error 9000 + code).","comment":"B: the channel to restore at the end"},
        "4597": {"comment":"\"FKEY\"?"},
        "4605": {"comment":"Key number"},
        "4609": {"comment":"Evaluate the key's text"},
        "4610": {"comment":"$24: evaluate a string expression and push it"},
        "4611": {"comment":"End of the list"},
        "4612": {"comment":"DE = the string's length byte"},
        "4618": {"comment":"C = key - 1"},
        "4620": {"comment":"Special function 8: program a function key"},
        "4622": {"comment":"Channel 105"},
        "4624": {"comment":"EXOS 11: special function"},
        "4626": {"comment":"Raise any EXOS error"},
        "4627": {"comment":"Drop the string"},
        "4628": {"comment":"$16: drop the top item"},
        "4629": {"comment":"End of the list"},
        "4630": {"comment":"Discard the entry flags"},
        "4633": {"synopsis":"Not FKEY: looks the word up in SETOPT_TABLE; an EXOS variable takes ON / OFF / a value, a\nletter an escape sequence.","comment":"An option name?"},
        "4636": {"comment":"No: SET n,v"},
        "4638": {"comment":"B = the value count"},
        "4642": {"comment":"An EXOS variable?"},
        "4648": {"comment":"Drop the entry flags"},
        "4649": {"comment":"Read the value word"},
        "4650": {"comment":"$20: next token"},
        "4651": {"comment":"End of the list"},
        "4652": {"comment":"\"ON\"?"},
        "4658": {"comment":"ON writes 0"},
        "4662": {"comment":"\"OFF\"?"},
        "4668": {"comment":"OFF writes 255"},
        "4672": {"comment":"Else a value 0-255"},
        "4676": {"comment":"Carry: the token is already read"},
        "4677": {"synopsis":"Writes D to EXOS variable C (after ON / OFF, reads the next token first).","comment":"Past ON / OFF"},
        "4680": {"comment":"Write"},
        "4682": {"comment":"EXOS 16: write EXOS variable C"},
        "4684": {"comment":"(no error check)"},
        "4686": {"synopsis":"An escape-sequence option: chooses the channel (the option's own unless Z on entry), then\nsends ESC and the letter.","comment":"D = the option's channel"},
        "4688": {"comment":"Z: keep the channel in ($0209)"},
        "4690": {"comment":"($0209) = the option's channel"},
        "4693": {"synopsis":"Sends ESC, the letter C, then B values.","comment":"ESC"},
        "4695": {"comment":"Write it"},
        "4696": {"comment":"$38: write A to channel ($0209)"},
        "4697": {"comment":"End of the list"},
        "4698": {"comment":"The escape letter"},
        "4700": {"comment":"$38: write A to channel ($0209)"},
        "4701": {"comment":"$20: next token"},
        "4702": {"comment":"End of the list"},
        "4703": {"comment":"(ix+$13) = bytes still owed + 1"},
        "4707": {"synopsis":"Loop: one value byte per pass; (ix+$13) counts the bytes still owed (an error pads them with\nzeros).","comment":"All sent?"},
        "4712": {"comment":"Values left in the statement?"},
        "4714": {"comment":"Yes: A = the next value"},
        "4717": {"comment":"Send it"},
        "4718": {"comment":"$38: write A to channel ($0209)"},
        "4719": {"comment":"End of the list"},
        "4720": {"comment":"A comma ($0C) follows?"},
        "4727": {"comment":"No: the rest are sent as 0"},
        "4729": {"synopsis":"After a comma reads the next token, then loops.","comment":"Past the comma"},
        "4734": {"synopsis":"Puts the channel passed in B back into ($0209) and returns.","comment":"The B pushed on entry"},
        "4739": {"synopsis":"SET n, v: writes v to EXOS variable n and raises any EXOS error.","comment":"Drop the entry flags"},
        "4740": {"comment":"C = the variable's number"},
        "4744": {"comment":"Expect a comma ($0C)"},
        "4746": {"comment":"Expect A, then read on"},
        "4747": {"comment":"$22: expect symbol A and read the next token"},
        "4748": {"comment":"End of the list"},
        "4749": {"comment":"D = the value"},
        "4753": {"comment":"Write"},
        "4755": {"comment":"EXOS 16: write EXOS variable C"},
        "4757": {"comment":"Raise any EXOS error"},
        "4760": {"synopsis":"Reads the next token, then falls into EVAL_BYTE_VALUE.","comment":"Past the current token"},
        "4761": {"comment":"$20: next token"},
        "4762": {"comment":"End of the list"},
        "4763": {"synopsis":"Evaluates a numeric expression that must be 0-255.\nExit: A = the value; error 1000 \"Unexpected value given\" when it is out of range.\nChanges: AF; BC, DE, HL kept."},
        "4766": {"comment":"Evaluate and pop it"},
        "4767": {"comment":"$23: evaluate a numeric expression and push it"},
        "4768": {"comment":"$0B: pop it into HL as a 16-bit integer"},
        "4769": {"comment":"End of the list"},
        "4770": {"comment":"Over 255 (H not 0)?"},
        "4772": {"comment":"Error 1000: Unexpected value given"},
        "4780": {"synopsis":"Finds the current word in SETOPT_TABLE. A first word is matched against the entries with\nflag bit 7 clear; one with bit 6 set (the first of a two-word name) makes it read the next\ntoken and look on for a matching second word (bit 7 set) in the entries that follow.\nExit: carry when found, B = the entry's flags, C = its value byte (bit 7: EXOS variable C\nAND $7F, else an escape letter), A = its channel byte; NC when absent.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"B bit 7: looking for a second word"},
        "4785": {"synopsis":"Loop: one table entry.","comment":"DE = the name's address (high byte first)"},
        "4789": {"comment":"Word kind (flag bit 7) differs?"},
        "4794": {"comment":"Same name?"},
        "4801": {"comment":"A second word or a one-word name?"},
        "4805": {"comment":"First of two words?"},
        "4809": {"comment":"Now look for its second word"},
        "4811": {"comment":"Read the second word"},
        "4812": {"comment":"$20: next token"},
        "4813": {"comment":"End of the list"},
        "4814": {"synopsis":"On to the next entry; a 0 ends the table (NC)."},
        "4818": {"comment":"End of the table?"},
        "4822": {"synopsis":"Found: returns the entry's last three bytes with carry.","comment":"Flags"},
        "4824": {"comment":"Value byte"},
        "4826": {"comment":"Channel byte"},
        "4829": {"synopsis":"SET's option table: 67 entries of 5 bytes, read by SETOPT_LOOKUP ($12AC), ended by a 0 at\n$142C. An entry is: the address of the option word (a length-prefixed text in the word list\nat $18D8-$1A2F, high byte first); a flags byte (bit 7 the second word of a two-word option,\nbit 6 the first word of one, bits 0-5 the number of values an escape sequence takes); a\nvalue byte (bit 7 set: EXOS variable value AND $7F; else the escape letter); and the channel\nan escape sequence goes to (101 or 102; 0 for a variable). A second word belongs to the\nnearest first word before it.","comment":"DEFAULT: first word of a two-word option"},
        "4834": {"comment":"DEFAULT CHANNEL: EXOS variable 4 DEF_CHAN"},
        "4839": {"comment":"TIMER: EXOS variable 5 TIMER"},
        "4844": {"comment":"KEY: first word of a two-word option"},
        "4849": {"comment":"KEY CLICK: EXOS variable 7 CLICK_KEY"},
        "4854": {"comment":"KEY RATE: EXOS variable 10 RATE_KEY"},
        "4859": {"comment":"KEY DELAY: EXOS variable 11 DELAY_KEY"},
        "4864": {"comment":"INTERRUPT: first word of a two-word option"},
        "4869": {"comment":"INTERRUPT STOP: EXOS variable 8 STOP_IRQ"},
        "4874": {"comment":"INTERRUPT KEY: EXOS variable 9 KEY_IRQ"},
        "4879": {"comment":"INTERRUPT NET: EXOS variable 19 NET_IRQ"},
        "4884": {"comment":"INTERRUPT CODE: EXOS variable 2 CODE_SOFT_IRQ"},
        "4889": {"comment":"TAPE: first word of a two-word option"},
        "4894": {"comment":"TAPE SOUND: EXOS variable 12 TAPE_SND"},
        "4899": {"comment":"TAPE PROTECT: EXOS variable 34 PROTECT"},
        "4904": {"comment":"TAPE LEVEL: EXOS variable 35 LV_TAPE"},
        "4909": {"comment":"FAST: first word of a two-word option"},
        "4914": {"comment":"FAST SAVE: EXOS variable 33 SP_TAPE"},
        "4919": {"comment":"SOUND: first word of a two-word option"},
        "4924": {"comment":"SOUND STOP: EXOS variable 13 WAIT_SND"},
        "4929": {"comment":"SOUND BUFFER: EXOS variable 15 BUF_SND"},
        "4934": {"comment":"SPEAKER: EXOS variable 14 MUTE_SND"},
        "4939": {"comment":"SERIAL: first word of a two-word option"},
        "4944": {"comment":"SERIAL BAUD: EXOS variable 16 BAUD_SER"},
        "4949": {"comment":"SERIAL FORMAT: EXOS variable 17 FORM_SER"},
        "4954": {"comment":"VIDEO: first word of a two-word option"},
        "4959": {"comment":"VIDEO MODE: EXOS variable 22 MODE_VID"},
        "4964": {"comment":"VIDEO COLOR: EXOS variable 23 COLR_VID"},
        "4969": {"comment":"VIDEO COLOUR: EXOS variable 23 COLR_VID"},
        "4974": {"comment":"VIDEO Y: EXOS variable 25 Y_SIZ_VID"},
        "4979": {"comment":"VIDEO X: EXOS variable 24 X_SIZ_VID"},
        "4984": {"comment":"BORDER: EXOS variable 27 BORD_VID"},
        "4989": {"comment":"BIAS: EXOS variable 28 BIAS_VID"},
        "4994": {"comment":"STATUS: EXOS variable 26 ST_FLAG"},
        "4999": {"comment":"EDITOR: first word of a two-word option"},
        "5004": {"comment":"EDITOR VIDEO: EXOS variable 29 VID_EDIT"},
        "5009": {"comment":"EDITOR KEY: EXOS variable 30 KEY_EDIT"},
        "5014": {"comment":"EDITOR BUFFER: EXOS variable 31 BUF_EDIT"},
        "5019": {"comment":"REM1: EXOS variable 36 REM1"},
        "5024": {"comment":"REM2: EXOS variable 37 REM2"},
        "5029": {"comment":"NET: first word of a two-word option"},
        "5034": {"comment":"NET CHANNEL: EXOS variable 20 CHAN_NET"},
        "5039": {"comment":"NET NUMBER: EXOS variable 18 ADDR_NET"},
        "5044": {"comment":"NET MACHINE: EXOS variable 21 MACH_NET"},
        "5049": {"comment":"PRIORITY: EXOS variable 38 SPRITE"},
        "5054": {"comment":"ATTRIBUTES: ESC \"a\" and 1 value to channel 101"},
        "5059": {"comment":"PALETTE: ESC \"C\" and 8 values to channel 101"},
        "5064": {"comment":"COLOR: ESC \"c\" and 2 values to channel 101"},
        "5069": {"comment":"COLOUR: ESC \"c\" and 2 values to channel 101"},
        "5074": {"comment":"PAPER: ESC \"P\" and 1 value to channel 101"},
        "5079": {"comment":"INK: ESC \"I\" and 1 value to channel 101"},
        "5084": {"comment":"CHARACTER: ESC \"K\" and 10 values to channel 102"},
        "5089": {"comment":"CURSOR: first word of a two-word option"},
        "5094": {"comment":"CURSOR CHARACTER: ESC \".\" and 1 value to channel 102"},
        "5099": {"comment":"CURSOR COLOR: ESC \"M\" and 1 value to channel 102"},
        "5104": {"comment":"CURSOR COLOUR: ESC \"M\" and 1 value to channel 102"},
        "5109": {"comment":"SCROLL: first word of a two-word option"},
        "5114": {"comment":"SCROLL ON: ESC \"S\" and 0 values to channel 102"},
        "5119": {"comment":"SCROLL OFF: ESC \"s\" and 0 values to channel 102"},
        "5124": {"comment":"SCROLL UP: ESC \"U\" and 2 values to channel 102"},
        "5129": {"comment":"SCROLL DOWN: ESC \"D\" and 2 values to channel 102"},
        "5134": {"comment":"BEAM: first word of a two-word option"},
        "5139": {"comment":"BEAM ON: ESC \"S\" and 0 values to channel 101"},
        "5144": {"comment":"BEAM OFF: ESC \"s\" and 0 values to channel 101"},
        "5149": {"comment":"LINE: first word of a two-word option"},
        "5154": {"comment":"LINE STYLE: ESC \".\" and 1 value to channel 101"},
        "5159": {"comment":"LINE MODE: ESC \"M\" and 1 value to channel 101"},
        "5164": {"comment":"End of the table"},
        "5165": {"synopsis":"LIST_RANGES's loop: after a \",\" the next token starts another range.","comment":"Next token: past the \",\""},
        "5166": {"comment":"Cart TOKEN_NEXT: read the next token"},
        "5168": {"synopsis":"Call $B9: parses the line ranges of LIST, LLIST and DELETE and runs LIST_LINES on each. A\nrange is \"n\", \"n-m\", \"n TO m\", \"-m\", \"TO m\", FIRST or LAST for n or m, or the name of a DEF\nroutine (its lines); ranges are separated by \",\". The mode (carry = list, no carry = delete)\nis in AF', set by the caller.\nEntry: the first token of the range read.\nExit: carry if STOP ended the listing; error 20000 if the ranges do not end the line.","comment":"Range start: DE = number, carry if none"},
        "5171": {"comment":"None: a DEF routine's name gives HL to DE"},
        "5176": {"comment":"Keep the start"},
        "5177": {"comment":"DE = the range's end"},
        "5180": {"comment":"HL = the start"},
        "5181": {"synopsis":"LIST_RANGES: lists or deletes lines HL to DE, then goes on after a \",\" or checks the line\nends.","comment":"List or delete lines HL to DE"},
        "5184": {"comment":"Stopped by STOP?"},
        "5185": {"comment":"Another range after \",\"?"},
        "5192": {"comment":"Symbol 1: the line's end"},
        "5195": {"comment":"Cart TOKEN_EXPECT: error 20000 unless the line ends here"},
        "5198": {"synopsis":"Reads the start of a line range.\nExit: NC with DE = the start's line number (a number, FIRST or LAST); with no start but a\n\"-\" or TO next, NC, Z and DE = the first line's number; carry when there is neither.\nChanges: A, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"A number, FIRST or LAST?"},
        "5201": {"comment":"Yes: DE = it"},
        "5202": {"comment":"No: \"-\" or TO next?"},
        "5205": {"comment":"Neither: carry, no range"},
        "5207": {"comment":"From the program's first line"},
        "5211": {"comment":"DE = its line number"},
        "5216": {"synopsis":"Reads the end of a line range when a \"-\" or TO comes next.\nExit: DE = the end's line number (10000 with carry when only \"-\" or TO was given); DE\nunchanged and NZ when neither comes.","comment":"\"-\" or TO?"},
        "5219": {"comment":"No: the range is one line"},
        "5221": {"comment":"Cart TOKEN_NEXT: past the \"-\" or TO"},
        "5223": {"synopsis":"Reads a line reference: a line number, FIRST (the program's first line) or LAST (its last\nline).\nExit: NC with DE = the line number, the token after it read; carry with DE = 10000 when the\ntoken is none of these.\nChanges: A, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"A line number token (word operand)?"},
        "5229": {"comment":"Yes: take it"},
        "5231": {"comment":"Text FIRST"},
        "5234": {"comment":"Is the name FIRST?"},
        "5237": {"comment":"HL = the program's first line"},
        "5240": {"comment":"FIRST: take its number"},
        "5242": {"comment":"Text LAST"},
        "5245": {"comment":"Is the name LAST?"},
        "5248": {"comment":"Neither: DE = 10000"},
        "5251": {"comment":"Carry: no reference"},
        "5253": {"comment":"LAST: walk from the program's first line"},
        "5258": {"synopsis":"LINE_REF_PARSE's walk for LAST: DE takes each line's number until the length byte 0 ends the\nprogram.","comment":"Length below 2: the program's end"},
        "5261": {"comment":"BC = length - 2"},
        "5264": {"synopsis":"LINE_REF_PARSE: DE = the line number at HL+1; for LAST it moves HL to the next line and\nloops while the length was not 2.","comment":"DE = this line's number"},
        "5268": {"comment":"HL = the next line"},
        "5269": {"comment":"Z only for FIRST (and a 2-byte line)"},
        "5271": {"synopsis":"Reads the next token and returns with no carry (OR A).","comment":"Next token"},
        "5272": {"comment":"Cart TOKEN_NEXT: read the next token"},
        "5274": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "5276": {"synopsis":"Z when the current token is symbol $0D (\"-\") or the name TO.\nChanges: A, HL.","comment":"Symbol $0D (\"-\")?"},
        "5282": {"comment":"Text TO"},
        "5285": {"comment":"Is the name TO?"},
        "5288": {"synopsis":"Call $BA: lists (carry in AF') or deletes (no carry in AF') every program line numbered HL\nto DE.\nEntry: HL = the first number, DE = the last, AF' = the mode.\nExit: carry if STOP was pressed (the STOP message printed); NC at the program's end or past\nDE.","comment":"Keep the last number"},
        "5289": {"comment":"Find the first line"},
        "5290": {"comment":"Cart LINE_FIND: HL = the line HL or the next one after it"},
        "5293": {"synopsis":"LIST_LINES's loop: one line per pass until the program ends or the line's number passes DE.","comment":"Length 0: the program's end"},
        "5296": {"comment":"BC = the line's number"},
        "5302": {"comment":"Past the last number?"},
        "5306": {"comment":"NC: done"},
        "5309": {"comment":"Keep the last number"},
        "5310": {"comment":"The mode: carry = list"},
        "5313": {"comment":"List the line"},
        "5314": {"comment":"Cart OUT_FLUSH_MEM: list line HL on channel ($0209)"},
        "5316": {"comment":"Carry back for AF'"},
        "5319": {"synopsis":"LIST_LINES, delete mode: removes the line; HL then holds the next one.","comment":"Delete the line"},
        "5320": {"comment":"Cart LINE_DELETE: remove line HL, the rest moved down"},
        "5322": {"synopsis":"LIST_LINES: puts the mode back into AF' and stops when STOP was pressed.","comment":"Mode back into AF'"},
        "5323": {"comment":"STOP pressed?"},
        "5328": {"comment":"Next line"},
        "5330": {"synopsis":"Gives the line range of the DEF routine named by the current token: the line that declared\nit and the line closing its block.\n1. A name token is needed (error 20030 \"Identifier expected\").\n2. The name is looked up; when missing, the program's state is reset and its definitions are\n   scanned, and the token is put back.\n3. The entry must be declared (flags bit 2) and not bit 3, else error 20002 \"Invalid line\n   number range\".\n4. The word after the value is the declaring line ($0216 is set to it); its first keyword,\n   unless it is $0D, gives the block's end through the cartridge's LINE_FIND_LEVEL.\nExit: HL = the first line's number, DE = the last line's number, carry.","comment":"The token's class"},
        "5333": {"comment":"A numeric name?"},
        "5337": {"comment":"A string name?"},
        "5339": {"comment":"Error 20030: Identifier expected"},
        "5342": {"synopsis":"DEF_LINE_RANGE: looks the name up, keeping the token state in the other registers.","comment":"Keep the read pointer"},
        "5345": {"comment":"Keep the name's text"},
        "5349": {"comment":"Keep the name's length"},
        "5353": {"comment":"Name in the name table? (carry = found)"},
        "5358": {"comment":"Not known yet: define the routines"},
        "5359": {"comment":"Cart RUN_STATE_RESET: reset the program's variables and stack"},
        "5360": {"comment":"Cart LINES_SCAN_DEFS: declare the program's definitions"},
        "5362": {"comment":"Put the token state back"},
        "5373": {"synopsis":"DEF_LINE_RANGE: finds the entry (HL = its value field, C = its flags) and checks it is a\ndeclared one.","comment":"Find the name, next token"},
        "5374": {"comment":"VAR_FIND_ANY: HL = the value field, C = the flags"},
        "5375": {"comment":"Cart TOKEN_NEXT: read the next token"},
        "5377": {"comment":"Flag bit 3 set?"},
        "5379": {"comment":"Error 20002: Invalid line number range"},
        "5382": {"comment":"Not declared (bit 2 clear)?"},
        "5387": {"comment":"DE = the value field"},
        "5388": {"comment":"A string?"},
        "5390": {"comment":"Numeric value: 6 bytes"},
        "5394": {"comment":"String: maximum length + 2 bytes"},
        "5398": {"synopsis":"DEF_LINE_RANGE: the word after the value is the declaring line; its number is the range's\nstart.","comment":"HL = past the value"},
        "5401": {"comment":"The declaring line's address"},
        "5405": {"comment":"Current line = the declaring one"},
        "5408": {"comment":"DE = its line number"},
        "5412": {"comment":"Keep it: the range's start"},
        "5413": {"comment":"To the first keyword's number (line+5)"},
        "5416": {"comment":"Keyword $0D?"},
        "5421": {"comment":"Find the block's end"},
        "5422": {"comment":"Cart LINE_FIND_LEVEL: HL = the next line at this nesting level"},
        "5424": {"comment":"DE = the word at HL+1 (the end's line number)"},
        "5428": {"synopsis":"DEF_LINE_RANGE: HL = the start's number, carry.","comment":"HL = the range's start"},
        "5431": {"synopsis":"Tests the STOP request (bit 2 of ($0200)): when set, clears it and prints the STOP message.\nExit: carry if STOP was pressed, NC otherwise.","comment":"No carry: not stopped"},
        "5432": {"comment":"STOP requested?"},
        "5437": {"comment":"Clear the request"},
        "5441": {"comment":"Print the STOP message"},
        "5442": {"comment":"Cart PRINT_STOP_MSG: \"STOP\" and \" at line n\""},
        "5446": {"synopsis":"Call $BB: the AUTO statement. Offers line numbers from 100 (AT n) in steps of 10 (STEP n):\nprints each number, reads a line from the editor and stores it, until an empty line or\nnumber 10000.\nThe numbering is in the other register set: HL' = the next number, DE' = the step, BC' =\n10000.\nErrors: 20000 for another word, 20001 \"Invalid line number\" for 0.","comment":"Start at 100"},
        "5449": {"comment":"Step 10"},
        "5452": {"comment":"Stop at 10000"},
        "5456": {"synopsis":"STMT_AUTO's options: AT n and STEP n in any order until the line ends.","comment":"The line's end?"},
        "5463": {"comment":"Text STEP"},
        "5466": {"comment":"Is the name STEP?"},
        "5469": {"comment":"C = 0: STEP"},
        "5473": {"comment":"C = 1: AT"},
        "5474": {"comment":"Text AT"},
        "5480": {"comment":"Error 20000: Not understood"},
        "5483": {"synopsis":"STMT_AUTO: the number after AT or STEP goes to HL' (AT) or DE' (STEP).","comment":"Read the number"},
        "5484": {"comment":"Cart TOKEN_NEXT: read the next token"},
        "5486": {"comment":"The number"},
        "5491": {"comment":"0: error 20001, Invalid line number"},
        "5495": {"comment":"STEP?"},
        "5498": {"comment":"STEP: on to $157E (POP DE inside the next instruction)"},
        "5500": {"comment":"AT: HL' = the first number"},
        "5501": {"comment":"Entry $157E is POP DE (STEP: DE' = the step); skipped for AT"},
        "5504": {"comment":"Past the number"},
        "5505": {"comment":"Cart TOKEN_NEXT: read the next token"},
        "5509": {"synopsis":"STMT_AUTO: the numbering registers become the main ones."},
        "5510": {"synopsis":"STMT_AUTO's loop: one line per pass while the number is below 10000.","comment":"Below 10000?"},
        "5514": {"synopsis":"STMT_AUTO: ends with a new line when the number reached 10000 or the typed line is empty."},
        "5516": {"comment":"CR"},
        "5518": {"comment":"Print CR"},
        "5519": {"comment":"Cart PRINT_CHAR: write A to channel ($0209)"},
        "5521": {"comment":"LF"},
        "5523": {"comment":"Print LF"},
        "5524": {"comment":"Cart PRINT_CHAR: write A to channel ($0209)"},
        "5527": {"synopsis":"STMT_AUTO: prints the number, reads the typed line and stores it under that number; then the\nnumber grows by the step.","comment":"HL = the number, in the main set too"},
        "5530": {"comment":"The line number to store"},
        "5533": {"comment":"Fill with spaces, 4 places"},
        "5536": {"comment":"Print the number"},
        "5537": {"comment":"Cart PRINT_DECIMAL: HL in 4 places, leading spaces"},
        "5539": {"comment":"Write EXOS variable 32 (FLG_EDIT)"},
        "5542": {"comment":"Value $18"},
        "5544": {"comment":"EXOS 16: FLG_EDIT = $18"},
        "5546": {"comment":"Space"},
        "5548": {"comment":"Print it and read the line"},
        "5549": {"comment":"Cart PRINT_CHAR: write A to channel ($0209)"},
        "5550": {"comment":"Cart INPUT_LINE: read a line into $0248"},
        "5552": {"comment":"The line's text"},
        "5555": {"comment":"Empty?"},
        "5559": {"comment":"Read the text from there"},
        "5562": {"comment":"The line's length byte at $0248"},
        "5566": {"comment":"Grow the text by 5 bytes"},
        "5570": {"comment":"Room for the line's header"},
        "5571": {"comment":"Cart LINEBUF_RESIZE: open a gap at ($0214)"},
        "5576": {"comment":"Store the line"},
        "5577": {"comment":"Cart LINE_STORE: tokenise and insert line ($0218)"},
        "5579": {"comment":"Next number: + the step"},
        "5583": {"synopsis":"Call $BC: the RENUMBER statement. Renumbers a range of lines (all by default: 1 to 9999; a\nrange as LIST takes it, or a DEF routine's name) from a new start (100, or the range's\nstart, or AT n) in steps (10, or STEP n), and changes every line-number reference in the\nprogram.\n1. Recomputes the nesting depths (LINES_REINDENT).\n2. Reads the options (RENUM_OPT_LOOP): the range in HL to DE, the new numbering in the other\n   set (BC' = start, DE' = step).\n3. Applies them (RENUM_APPLY).\nErrors: 20001 for AT 0 or STEP 0, 20010 \"Cannot do specified RENUMBER\" when the new numbers\ndo not fit.","comment":"Recompute every line's nesting depth"},
        "5586": {"comment":"New numbers from 100"},
        "5589": {"comment":"Step 10"},
        "5593": {"comment":"Range from line 1"},
        "5596": {"comment":"To line 9999"},
        "5599": {"synopsis":"STMT_RENUMBER's options, until the line ends: a range (its start also becomes the new\nstart), STEP n, AT n or a DEF routine's name.","comment":"The line's end?"},
        "5606": {"comment":"Keep the range"},
        "5608": {"comment":"A range start?"},
        "5613": {"comment":"Yes: the new numbers start there"},
        "5618": {"comment":"Drop the old range"},
        "5620": {"comment":"DE = the range's end"},
        "5623": {"comment":"HL = its start"},
        "5626": {"synopsis":"STMT_RENUMBER: STEP n sets DE' (the step).","comment":"Text STEP"},
        "5629": {"comment":"Is the name STEP?"},
        "5634": {"comment":"The step's value"},
        "5635": {"comment":"Cart TOKEN_NEXT: read the next token"},
        "5637": {"comment":"The number"},
        "5642": {"comment":"0: error 20001, Invalid line number"},
        "5647": {"comment":"DE' = the step"},
        "5650": {"synopsis":"STMT_RENUMBER: AT n sets BC' (the new start).","comment":"Text AT"},
        "5653": {"comment":"Is the name AT?"},
        "5658": {"comment":"The new start"},
        "5659": {"comment":"Cart TOKEN_NEXT: read the next token"},
        "5661": {"comment":"The number"},
        "5666": {"comment":"0: error 20001, Invalid line number"},
        "5671": {"comment":"BC' = the new start"},
        "5672": {"synopsis":"STMT_RENUMBER: past the option's number, the range back in HL and DE."},
        "5673": {"comment":"Past the number"},
        "5674": {"comment":"Cart TOKEN_NEXT: read the next token"},
        "5676": {"comment":"The range back"},
        "5680": {"synopsis":"STMT_RENUMBER: a DEF routine's name gives the range, and the new numbers start at its first\nline's number.","comment":"Drop the old range"},
        "5683": {"comment":"Keep the step"},
        "5684": {"comment":"HL to DE = the routine's lines"},
        "5689": {"comment":"BC' = its first number"},
        "5694": {"synopsis":"STMT_RENUMBER, the work:\n1. Finds the range's first line; none: done. The line at or after the new start must not lie\n   before it (error 20010).\n2. A first pass of RENUM_NUMBER over the range only checks that every new number stays below\n   10000 (error 20010), and the last one must stay below the next line's number (error\n   20010).\n3. With bit 7 of ($0200) set, LINES_FIX_REFS turns every line-number reference into the\n   address of the line it names.\n4. RENUM_NUMBER writes the new numbers.\n5. With bit 7 clear, LINES_FIX_REFS turns the addresses back into (new) numbers.","comment":"Keep the new start"},
        "5696": {"comment":"BC' = the step"},
        "5699": {"comment":"BC = the new start"},
        "5700": {"comment":"Keep the range's end and the new start"},
        "5702": {"comment":"Find the range's first line"},
        "5703": {"comment":"Cart LINE_FIND: HL = line HL or the next one after it"},
        "5705": {"comment":"Past the program's end: nothing to do"},
        "5709": {"comment":"Keep it; HL = the new start"},
        "5710": {"comment":"Find the line at the new start"},
        "5711": {"comment":"Cart LINE_FIND: HL = line HL or the next one after it"},
        "5713": {"comment":"BC = the range's first line"},
        "5715": {"comment":"Does it lie before the range?"},
        "5717": {"comment":"Error 20010: Cannot do specified RENUMBER"},
        "5721": {"comment":"DE = the range's end"},
        "5723": {"comment":"Find the line after the range"},
        "5726": {"comment":"Cart LINE_FIND: HL = line HL or the next one after it"},
        "5728": {"comment":"DE = the line after the range"},
        "5732": {"comment":"HL = the range's first line"},
        "5734": {"comment":"BC = the step"},
        "5735": {"comment":"HL = the new start"},
        "5737": {"comment":"Less one step: the first pass adds it"},
        "5739": {"comment":"Keep both for the writing pass"},
        "5743": {"comment":"First pass: check only"},
        "5750": {"synopsis":"STMT_RENUMBER: nothing in the range: drops two saved words and returns."},
        "5753": {"synopsis":"STMT_RENUMBER: the last new number must stay below the number of the line after the range.","comment":"No line after the range?"},
        "5757": {"comment":"BC = its number"},
        "5761": {"comment":"HL = the last new number"},
        "5765": {"comment":"Not below it?"},
        "5767": {"comment":"Error 20010: Cannot do specified RENUMBER"},
        "5770": {"synopsis":"STMT_RENUMBER: references to addresses, new numbers written, then addresses back to numbers\n(falls into LINES_FIX_REFS)."},
        "5771": {"comment":"Pass 1: references to line addresses"},
        "5779": {"comment":"HL = the range's first line"},
        "5781": {"comment":"BC' = the step, HL' = the new start - step"},
        "5784": {"comment":"Write the new numbers (no carry)"},
        "5787": {"comment":"Pass 2: addresses to the new numbers"},
        "5791": {"synopsis":"Walks every program line and converts the line-number references in it (token class $A0):\nwith bit 7 of ($0200) set into the address of the named line (a missing line's number is\nkept XOR $C000), with bit 7 clear back into the number now at that address.\nChanges: A, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"From the program's first line"},
        "5794": {"synopsis":"LINES_FIX_REFS's loop: one line per pass until the length byte 0.","comment":"The program's end?"},
        "5798": {"comment":"Fix this line's references"},
        "5802": {"comment":"Next line: + its length"},
        "5808": {"synopsis":"Walks the tokens of the program line at HL (from its first token at +4) and runs the class\nroutine of TOKEN_CLASS_TAB for each, until the line's end (symbol 1), a 0 byte or a keyword\nwhose flag bit 6 is clear.","comment":"Past the length and the line number"},
        "5811": {"synopsis":"LINE_FIX_REFS's loop: Z from the last token's routine ends the walk.","comment":"Line's end?"},
        "5812": {"comment":"The next token"},
        "5815": {"comment":"A 0 byte: done"},
        "5816": {"comment":"Its class: the top 3 bits"},
        "5818": {"comment":"As 0-7"},
        "5821": {"comment":"Run the class routine of the table after the call"},
        "5824": {"comment":"Next token"},
        "5826": {"synopsis":"TOKEN_CLASS_TAB: LINE_FIX_REFS's token routines, one word per class (the top 3 bits of the\ntoken's first byte), read by JUMP_INLINE_TAB through the return address of the CALL at\n$16BD: 0 symbol (TOKEN_SYMBOL), 1 numeric name and 2 string name (TOKEN_SKIP_LEN), 3 keyword\n(TOKEN_KEYWORD), 4 string literal ($16D7, inside TOKEN_SKIP_LEN), 5 line-number reference\n(TOKEN_LINE_REF), 6 numeric constant (TOKEN_SKIP_LEN). There is no word for class 7."},
        "5840": {"synopsis":"LINE_FIX_REFS, a symbol token (one byte): Z when it is symbol 1, the line's end."},
        "5841": {"comment":"Symbol 1: Z"},
        "5843": {"synopsis":"LINE_FIX_REFS, a name or a numeric constant: skips the number of bytes in the token's low 5\nbits. Entry $16D7 (inside the LD DE at $16D6), a string literal: skips the length in the\nbyte after the class byte.","comment":"Name length or constant size"},
        "5846": {"comment":"Entry $16D7: INC HL / LD A,(HL), a literal's length"},
        "5849": {"comment":"Skip that many bytes"},
        "5854": {"synopsis":"A keyword token: reads its number (HL+1) and its flags.\nExit: HL = the keyword number's byte, C = the number, E = the flags byte (cart\nKEYWORD_FLAGS); Z when flag bit 6 is clear.\nChanges: A, BC, DE.","comment":"The keyword's number"},
        "5857": {"comment":"Its flags"},
        "5858": {"comment":"Cart KEYWORD_FLAGS: E = keyword C's flags byte"},
        "5860": {"comment":"Bit 6 clear: the line's walk ends"},
        "5864": {"synopsis":"LINE_FIX_REFS, a line-number reference (class $A0, a word after the class byte): converts it\nin place.\n1. Bit 7 of ($0200) set: the number becomes the address of its line (cart LINE_FIND), or,\n   when there is no such line, the number XOR $C000.\n2. Bit 7 clear: a word whose top bits are 11 is such a marked number and is put back; any\n   other is a line's address and becomes that line's number.\nExit: NZ (OR H of the word's address), so the walk goes on.","comment":"The word"},
        "5869": {"comment":"A = its high byte XOR $C0"},
        "5872": {"comment":"Pass 1 (to addresses)?"},
        "5878": {"comment":"A marked number ($C000 up)?"},
        "5882": {"comment":"An address: read that line's number"},
        "5887": {"comment":"Carry: store the number"},
        "5890": {"synopsis":"TOKEN_LINE_REF, pass 1: finds the line the number names.","comment":"HL = the number"},
        "5891": {"comment":"Find its line"},
        "5892": {"comment":"Cart LINE_FIND: HL = the line, carry if it does not exist"},
        "5894": {"synopsis":"TOKEN_LINE_REF: chooses what to store: the line found (pass 1), or the number in DE.","comment":"High byte XOR $C0 (the mark or its removal)"},
        "5895": {"comment":"Missing line or a number: store DE"},
        "5897": {"comment":"DE = the line's address"},
        "5898": {"synopsis":"TOKEN_LINE_REF: writes DE over the reference."},
        "5902": {"comment":"NZ: go on with the line"},
        "5904": {"synopsis":"Gives the lines from HL up to (not including) DE new numbers: HL' + BC' for the first, then\neach BC' more.\nEntry: HL = the first line, DE = the line to stop at, HL' = the first number less the step,\nBC' = the step; carry = check only.\nExit: NC, Z when the walk stopped at DE exactly; HL' = the last number. Error 20010 when a\nnumber reaches 10000."},
        "5905": {"comment":"DE' = 10000, the limit"},
        "5909": {"comment":"Keep the mode"},
        "5910": {"synopsis":"RENUM_NUMBER's loop: one line per pass until HL reaches DE.","comment":"Reached the stop line?"},
        "5916": {"comment":"Next number"},
        "5918": {"comment":"10000 or more?"},
        "5922": {"comment":"Error 20010: Cannot do specified RENUMBER"},
        "5926": {"comment":"BC = the new number"},
        "5927": {"comment":"Check only?"},
        "5930": {"comment":"Write it as the line's number"},
        "5936": {"synopsis":"RENUM_NUMBER: keeps the mode and moves to the next line.","comment":"Keep the mode"},
        "5937": {"comment":"Next line: + its length"},
        "5943": {"synopsis":"Jumps through the word table that follows the CALL to this routine: runs entry A (0 up) of\nit, and that routine returns to the instruction just before the table (the CALL's return\naddress); HL is kept.\nEntry: A = the entry number.\nChanges: A, BC.","comment":"HL = the return address (the table - 2)"},
        "5945": {"comment":"Entry A at return address + 2(A+1)"},
        "5951": {"comment":"BC = the routine"},
        "5954": {"comment":"Return address back on the stack"},
        "5956": {"comment":"Jump to the routine"},
        "5958": {"synopsis":"Call $C0: WAIT [DELAY] n. Pages the system segment into page 2, clears SECOND_COUNTER\n($BFF0) and waits until it reaches n seconds; STOP raises error 9229 (\"STOP key pressed\").\nPage 2 is put back.","comment":"Text DELAY"},
        "5961": {"comment":"Is the name DELAY?"},
        "5964": {"comment":"Yes: past it"},
        "5967": {"comment":"The number of seconds"},
        "5968": {"comment":"Cart EVAL_NUMERIC: push the expression's value"},
        "5969": {"comment":"Cart NUM_POP_INT: pop it into HL"},
        "5971": {"comment":"DE = the seconds"},
        "5972": {"comment":"Page 2's segment"},
        "5978": {"comment":"Page 2 = segment $FF (the system segment)"},
        "5981": {"comment":"SECOND_COUNTER = 0"},
        "5984": {"synopsis":"STMT_WAIT_DELAY's loop: until SECOND_COUNTER reaches DE or STOP is pressed.","comment":"STOP requested?"},
        "5988": {"comment":"Error code $E5"},
        "5990": {"comment":"STOP: error 9229, STOP key pressed"},
        "5991": {"comment":"Seconds so far"},
        "5995": {"comment":"Not there yet?"},
        "6000": {"comment":"Page 2 back"},
        "6003": {"synopsis":"Call $C1: recomputes the nesting depth (the byte at line+3) of every program line from its\nfirst keyword's flags (cart KEYWORD_FLAGS): bit 3 opens a block (the next lines one deeper),\nbit 2 closes one (this line one less), both a middle line (this line one less, the next ones\nas before).\nError 20052 \"Too many nested blocks\" at depth 128.\nChanges: A, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"From the program's first line"},
        "6006": {"comment":"Depth 0"},
        "6008": {"synopsis":"LINES_REINDENT's loop: one line per pass until the length byte 0.","comment":"The program's end?"},
        "6011": {"comment":"HL = the depth byte (line+3)"},
        "6015": {"comment":"The first token"},
        "6017": {"comment":"E = its keyword's flags"},
        "6020": {"comment":"D = the depth"},
        "6023": {"comment":"This line's depth"},
        "6024": {"comment":"Opens and closes?"},
        "6031": {"comment":"Depth 0: leave it"},
        "6035": {"comment":"This line one less"},
        "6038": {"synopsis":"LINES_REINDENT: a closing line is one less deep, and so are the lines after it.","comment":"Closes a block?"},
        "6042": {"comment":"Depth 0: leave it"},
        "6046": {"comment":"One less, this line too"},
        "6050": {"synopsis":"LINES_REINDENT: an opening line makes the lines after it one deeper.","comment":"Opens a block?"},
        "6054": {"comment":"The next lines one deeper"},
        "6055": {"comment":"128 levels?"},
        "6057": {"comment":"Error 20052: Too many nested blocks"},
        "6060": {"synopsis":"LINES_REINDENT: back to the line's start, then on by its length."},
        "6063": {"comment":"Next line: + its length"},
        "6069": {"synopsis":"Call $C2: the TIME statement. The string must be 8 characters \"hh:mm:ss\" of decimal digits;\nit sets the clock with EXOS 31 (C = hours, D = minutes, E = seconds, BCD). Error 9235\n\"Invalid date or time value\" for another string or when EXOS refuses it. Drops the string.","comment":"A = hh (BCD)"},
        "6073": {"comment":"\":mm\""},
        "6077": {"comment":"\":ss\""},
        "6081": {"comment":"EXOS 31: set the time"},
        "6085": {"synopsis":"Call $C3: the DATE statement. The string must be 8 digits \"yyyymmdd\", year 1980-2079; it\nsets the date with EXOS 33 (C = year - 1980, D = month, E = day, BCD). Error 9235 \"Invalid\ndate or time value\" otherwise.","comment":"D = the century (BCD)"},
        "6089": {"comment":"The year in the century"},
        "6092": {"comment":"Less 80"},
        "6095": {"comment":"C = year - 1980 (BCD)"},
        "6096": {"comment":"Century less the borrow"},
        "6100": {"comment":"Must give 19 (1980-2079)"},
        "6104": {"comment":"D = the month"},
        "6108": {"comment":"E = the day"},
        "6112": {"comment":"EXOS 33: set the date"},
        "6114": {"synopsis":"STMT_TIME and STMT_DATE: raises the EXOS error if any, then drops the string.","comment":"EXOS error: 9000 + A"},
        "6115": {"comment":"Drop the string"},
        "6116": {"comment":"Cart ITEM_DROP: pop the top item"},
        "6119": {"synopsis":"Reads \":\" and two decimal digits at HL+1.\nExit: A = the two digits as BCD, HL at the second; error 9235 when the \":\" or a digit is\nmissing.","comment":"Must be \":\""},
        "6125": {"synopsis":"Reads two decimal digits from HL+1.\nExit: A = them as BCD, HL at the second; error 9235 for a character below \"0\" or a total\nabove 99.\nChanges: A, E, HL."},
        "6127": {"comment":"The first digit"},
        "6130": {"comment":"To the high nibble"},
        "6135": {"synopsis":"Adds the digit at HL+1 to E as BCD.\nExit: A = the sum, NC; error 9235 for a character below \"0\" or a carry out.","comment":"The next character"},
        "6137": {"comment":"Below \"0\"?"},
        "6141": {"comment":"Add it to the high digit"},
        "6144": {"synopsis":"Raises error 9235 (\"Invalid date or time value\") through RST 18h.","comment":"Error code $EB"},
        "6146": {"comment":"NZ"},
        "6147": {"comment":"Error 9235: Invalid date or time value"},
        "6148": {"synopsis":"Evaluates the string argument of TIME or DATE (left on the stack) and reads its first two\ndigits.\nExit: A = them as BCD, HL at the second; error 9235 unless the string has 8 characters.","comment":"The string"},
        "6149": {"comment":"Cart EVAL_STRING: push the string expression"},
        "6151": {"comment":"Its length byte"},
        "6155": {"comment":"8 characters?"},
        "6160": {"comment":"The first two digits"},
        "6162": {"synopsis":"Call $C5: programs the 16 function keys with the texts of FKEY_TEXTS: key 15 gets the first\ntext, key 0 the last. Each is sent as $A5, the text, $A1 and CR (EXOS 11 on channel 105,\nspecial function 8, DE = $0348, a length byte first).\nExit: A = 0 and Z, or NZ with the EXOS error.","comment":"The texts"},
        "6165": {"comment":"B = 8 (program a function key), C = key 15"},
        "6168": {"synopsis":"FKEYS_DEFAULT's loop: one key per pass, key 15 down to 0."},
        "6169": {"comment":"Build the string at $0349"},
        "6172": {"comment":"Code $A5 first"},
        "6175": {"comment":"The text's length"},
        "6182": {"comment":"Copy the text"},
        "6185": {"comment":"Then code $A1"},
        "6188": {"comment":"And CR"},
        "6192": {"comment":"The length byte at $0348"},
        "6193": {"comment":"Text + 3"},
        "6198": {"comment":"Channel 105"},
        "6200": {"comment":"EXOS 11: program function key C with the string at DE"},
        "6203": {"comment":"Error: return it"},
        "6204": {"comment":"Next key down"},
        "6208": {"comment":"Done: A = 0"},
        "6210": {"synopsis":"FKEY_TEXTS: texts stored as a length byte followed by the characters, one after the other\nwith no end mark. The first 16 ($1842-$18D7) are the function keys' texts read by\nFKEYS_DEFAULT ($1812), key 15 first: TYPE, TOGGLE SPEAKER, DISPLAY GRAPHICS, DISPLAY TEXT,\nTOGGLE REM2, RENUMBER, LLIST, CONTINUE, INFO, TOGGLE KEY CLICK, GRAPHICS, TEXT, TOGGLE REM1,\nAUTO, LIST, START (key 0). From $18D8 the words of SET/TOGGLE/ASK's options and of the\nstatements here follow, in alphabetical order (ATTRIBUTES ... X, Y), each found by its\naddress: SETOPT_TABLE ($12DD) holds the addresses, and WORD_MATCH ($1A31) compares the\ncurrent name with one (FIRST $1953, LAST $1977, TO $1A1B, AT $18E3, STEP $19F5, DELAY $1934,\nTAB $1A0C, USING $1A21, FKEY $1959, ON $199F, OFF $19A2)."},
        "6360": {"synopsis":"The option and statement words: ATTRIBUTES, AT, BAUD, BORDER, BEAM, BIAS, BUFFER, CHANNEL,\nCHARACTER, CLICK, CODE, COLOR, COLOUR, CURSOR, DELAY, DEFAULT, DOWN, EDITOR, FAST, FIRST,\nFKEY, FORMAT, INK, INTERRUPT, KEY, LAST, LINE, LEVEL, MACHINE, MODE, NET, NUMBER, ON, OFF,\nPALETTE, PAPER, PRIORITY, PROTECT, RATE, REM1, REM2, SAVE, SCROLL, SERIAL, SOUND, SPEAKER,\nSTEP, STOP, STATUS, STYLE, TAB, TAPE, TIMER, TO, UP, USING, VIDEO, X, Y (length byte, then\nthe letters)."},
        "6705": {"synopsis":"Compares the current name token (length (ix+3), text at ($0347)) with the text at HL (a\nlength byte, then the letters).\nExit: Z (A = 0) when they are the same, HL past the text; NZ otherwise, HL at the first\ndifference.\nChanges: A, HL."},
        "6707": {"comment":"The name's text"},
        "6711": {"comment":"Its length"},
        "6715": {"comment":"Compare the length byte and the letters"},
        "6716": {"synopsis":"WORD_MATCH's loop: one byte per pass, the length byte first.","comment":"Different?"},
        "6720": {"comment":"The name's next letter"},
        "6724": {"comment":"Same: Z, A = 0"},
        "6725": {"synopsis":"WORD_MATCH: restores BC and DE and returns the result in Z."},
        "6728": {"synopsis":"Call $BD: PRINT's check while a line is stored. Reads the prefixes before the print list\n(\"#\" channel, AT row,col, USING line or string), separated by \",\", and checks they end with\nsymbol $10; the rest of the statement is skipped (STMT_SKIP). C counts the prefixes; an item\nafter a \",\" that is not a prefix is error 20000.\nExit: the statement passed.","comment":"No prefix yet"},
        "6731": {"synopsis":"PRINT_CHECK's loop: one prefix per pass, classified by PRINT_CLAUSE (3 USING, 2 AT, 1 \"#\", 0\nother).","comment":"Next token"},
        "6732": {"comment":"Cart TOKEN_NEXT: read the next token"},
        "6734": {"comment":"A = the prefix's kind"},
        "6737": {"comment":"None?"},
        "6741": {"comment":"\"#\"?"},
        "6743": {"comment":"USING?"},
        "6746": {"comment":"AT: the row"},
        "6747": {"comment":"Cart TOKEN_NEXT: read the next token"},
        "6748": {"comment":"Cart SKIP_NUM_EXPR: parse a number, not computed"},
        "6750": {"comment":"Symbol $0C: \",\""},
        "6752": {"comment":"Expect it"},
        "6753": {"comment":"Cart TOKEN_EXPECT: error 20000 unless symbol A"},
        "6755": {"comment":"Then the column"},
        "6757": {"synopsis":"PRINT_CHECK: USING n or USING string. A number is a line reference: its token is rewritten\nas class $A2 so that RENUMBER changes it.","comment":"Past USING"},
        "6758": {"comment":"Cart TOKEN_NEXT: read the next token"},
        "6760": {"comment":"A number (an integer or line number token)?"},
        "6767": {"comment":"Its token's first byte"},
        "6771": {"comment":"Becomes $A2: a line reference"},
        "6773": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "6774": {"comment":"Cart TOKEN_NEXT: read the next token"},
        "6778": {"synopsis":"PRINT_CHECK: the format of USING as a string expression.","comment":"Parse the format string"},
        "6779": {"comment":"Cart SKIP_STR_EXPR: parse a string, not computed"},
        "6783": {"synopsis":"PRINT_CHECK: not a prefix: allowed only before any prefix (C = 0), else error 20000.","comment":"Any prefix before?"},
        "6787": {"comment":"Error 20000: Not understood"},
        "6790": {"synopsis":"PRINT_CHECK: \"#\" and the channel number.","comment":"Past \"#\""},
        "6791": {"comment":"Cart TOKEN_NEXT: read the next token"},
        "6793": {"synopsis":"PRINT_CHECK: a numeric expression (the channel or AT's column).","comment":"Parse the number"},
        "6794": {"comment":"Cart SKIP_NUM_EXPR: parse a number, not computed"},
        "6796": {"synopsis":"PRINT_CHECK: after a prefix, \",\" brings another; otherwise symbol $10 must end them.","comment":"One more prefix"},
        "6797": {"comment":"\",\"?"},
        "6804": {"comment":"Symbol $10"},
        "6806": {"comment":"Expect it"},
        "6807": {"comment":"Cart TOKEN_EXPECT: error 20000 unless symbol A"},
        "6809": {"synopsis":"PRINT_CHECK: skips the print list to the statement's end.","comment":"Skip the rest"},
        "6810": {"comment":"Cart STMT_SKIP: to the statement's end"},
        "6813": {"synopsis":"Call $BE: PRINT's action on channel ($0209), put back at the end.\n1. Prefixes, separated by \",\": \"#\" n sets the channel; AT row,col sends ESC \"=\" row+32\n   col+32 (PRINT_AT_ESC); USING takes a format from a line (the text after \":\" on that line)\n   or from a string (copied to $0496, 127 at most). The stack keeps the format's end and\n   start and a flag word (bit 0 of its A: USING).\n2. Without USING (PRINT_ITEM_LOOP): strings, numbers (PRINT_NUMBER: spaces around), \",\" a\n   TAB character, \";\" nothing, TAB(n) the cursor to column n.\n3. With USING (USING_ITEMS): the format's literal text and one format item per value.\n4. A new line at the end unless the list ended with \",\" or \";\".\nEntry: carry = read the first token first.","comment":"Keep the channel"},
        "6817": {"comment":"Flags: no USING"},
        "6819": {"comment":"Room for the format's end and start"},
        "6821": {"synopsis":"PRINT_EXEC's prefix loop: carry reads the next token first."},
        "6823": {"comment":"Next token"},
        "6824": {"comment":"Cart TOKEN_NEXT: read the next token"},
        "6826": {"synopsis":"PRINT_EXEC: the prefix's kind from PRINT_CLAUSE (3 USING, 2 AT, 1 \"#\", 0 none).","comment":"A = the prefix's kind"},
        "6829": {"comment":"None: the items"},
        "6833": {"comment":"Not \"#\"?"},
        "6835": {"comment":"The channel"},
        "6836": {"comment":"Cart EVAL_BYTE_ARG: \"#\" and a value 0-255 in A"},
        "6838": {"comment":"Print on it"},
        "6843": {"synopsis":"PRINT_EXEC: AT row,col moves the cursor.","comment":"USING?"},
        "6846": {"comment":"AT: the row"},
        "6847": {"comment":"Cart TOKEN_NEXT: read the next token"},
        "6849": {"comment":"Compute it"},
        "6851": {"comment":"Evaluate the row"},
        "6852": {"comment":"Cart EVAL_NUMERIC: push the expression's value"},
        "6853": {"comment":"Cart NUM_POP_INT: pop it into HL"},
        "6855": {"comment":"Keep the row"},
        "6856": {"comment":"Past \",\""},
        "6857": {"comment":"Cart TOKEN_NEXT: read the next token"},
        "6861": {"comment":"Evaluate the column"},
        "6862": {"comment":"Cart EVAL_NUMERIC: push the expression's value"},
        "6863": {"comment":"Cart NUM_POP_INT: pop it into HL"},
        "6865": {"comment":"E = the row"},
        "6866": {"comment":"D = the column"},
        "6867": {"comment":"ESC \"=\" row col: move the cursor"},
        "6872": {"synopsis":"PRINT_EXEC: USING. Sets the USING flag; the format comes from a line (a line number token)\nor a string expression.","comment":"Drop the room kept for the format"},
        "6875": {"comment":"USING on"},
        "6878": {"comment":"Past USING"},
        "6879": {"comment":"Cart TOKEN_NEXT: read the next token"},
        "6881": {"comment":"A line number?"},
        "6888": {"comment":"Find the line"},
        "6892": {"comment":"Cart LINE_FIND: HL = the line, carry if it does not exist"},
        "6894": {"comment":"Error 20004: Line number does not exist"},
        "6897": {"comment":"Past the number"},
        "6898": {"comment":"Cart TOKEN_NEXT: read the next token"},
        "6900": {"comment":"DE = the line's last byte"},
        "6908": {"comment":"Its text after the keyword (line+6)"},
        "6911": {"synopsis":"PRINT_USING: skips spaces in the format line."},
        "6913": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "6917": {"comment":"Still in the line?"},
        "6922": {"synopsis":"PRINT_USING: the format line's text must start with \":\" (error 20000 otherwise); the format\nfollows it.","comment":"\":\"?"},
        "6924": {"comment":"Error 20000: Not understood"},
        "6929": {"synopsis":"PRINT_USING: a string expression is the format: copied into the string variable at $0496\n(127 characters at most) and ended by a 0.","comment":"The format string"},
        "6930": {"comment":"Cart EVAL_STRING: push the string expression"},
        "6932": {"comment":"A string variable at $0496"},
        "6935": {"comment":"Maximum length 127"},
        "6938": {"comment":"Store the format there"},
        "6939": {"comment":"Cart STR_POP_VAR: pop the string into the variable at HL"},
        "6942": {"comment":"Its length"},
        "6947": {"comment":"Past its last character"},
