        "7070": {"comment":"Cart PRINT_NUMBER: print it with spaces around"},
        "7072": {"synopsis":"PRINT_EXEC: drops the printed value; no carry: a new line is due.","comment":"Drop it"},
        "7073": {"comment":"Cart ITEM_DROP: pop the top item"},
        "7076": {"comment":"No carry: new line at the end"},
        "7079": {"synopsis":"PRINT_EXEC's end: a new line unless the last item was a separator; the channel is put back."},
        "7080": {"comment":"CR LF unless after \",\" or \";\""},
        "7084": {"comment":"The channel back"},
        "7088": {"synopsis":"PRINT_EXEC with USING: HL' walks the format (BC' its start, DE' its last character); bit 0\nof E stays set while no format item has been used."},
        "7089": {"comment":"The format's first character"},
        "7090": {"comment":"BC = it, for starting again"},
        "7093": {"comment":"E bit 0 set: no item yet; entry $1BB6 is RES 0,E"},
        "7096": {"synopsis":"PRINT_EXEC with USING: prints the format's literal text up to the next format character,\nthen looks at the item list: its end, a separator or an item.","comment":"Print the literal text"},
        "7099": {"comment":"Symbol $10?"},
        "7106": {"comment":"The line's end?"},
        "7113": {"comment":"\",\"?"},
        "7117": {"comment":"\";\"?"},
        "7121": {"synopsis":"PRINT_EXEC with USING: a separator is skipped and sets the carry (no new line at the end).","comment":"Past it"},
        "7122": {"comment":"Cart TOKEN_NEXT: read the next token"},
        "7124": {"comment":"Carry: ended with a separator"},
        "7129": {"synopsis":"PRINT_EXEC with USING: an item needs a format item; at the format's end a new line starts\nthe format again, or error 8202 when no format item was found in it.","comment":"Format left?"},
        "7139": {"comment":"No format item at all?"},
        "7141": {"comment":"Error 8202: No format item in USING string"},
        "7144": {"comment":"New line"},
        "7148": {"comment":"The format again from its start"},
        "7150": {"comment":"Print its literal text"},
        "7153": {"synopsis":"PRINT USING, one item: a string literal or string name goes to USING_STRING; any other item\nis evaluated as a number and printed by USING_NUMBER through the format item at the format\npointer. Part of PRINT_EXEC's USING loop: the main registers hold B (compute flag) and E\n(bit 0 set while no format item has been used), the other set the format pointer (HL), its\nlast character (DE) and its first (BC).","comment":"Class of the item's first token"},
        "7156": {"comment":"String literal?"},
        "7160": {"comment":"String name?"},
        "7165": {"comment":"Evaluate a numeric expression and push it"},
        "7167": {"comment":"Print it through the format item"},
        "7170": {"synopsis":"Drops the printed item, clears the trailing-separator flag kept on the stack and goes back\ninto the USING loop at $1BB6, which marks a format item as used."},
        "7171": {"comment":"Drop the top item"},
        "7173": {"comment":"The flags pushed by PRINT_EXEC"},
        "7174": {"comment":"No separator after this item yet"},
        "7176": {"comment":"Mark an item used, print the next literals"},
        "7178": {"synopsis":"PRINT USING, a string item: evaluates it; when the format is used up, starts a new line and\nthe format again from its first character (printing its leading literals). Then measures the\nfield (USING_STR_FIELD).","comment":"Compute, not only parse"},
        "7180": {"comment":"Evaluate a string expression and push it"},
        "7181": {"comment":"Evaluate a string expression and push it"},
        "7183": {"comment":"Format pointer before its last character?"},
        "7190": {"comment":"Format used up: new line"},
        "7193": {"comment":"Restart at the format's first character"},
        "7195": {"comment":"Print its leading literal characters"},
        "7199": {"synopsis":"Measures the string field at the format pointer: D = its width (a leading < or > and every\n#, % and * after it), E = the alignment (0 for <, 2 for >, 1 when neither: centred).","comment":"The item's first format character"},
        "7201": {"comment":"Width 0, alignment 0"},
        "7204": {"comment":"< left aligns"},
        "7208": {"comment":"Centred unless it is >"},
        "7209": {"comment":"> right aligns?"},
        "7214": {"synopsis":"Counts one field position and moves the format pointer past it.","comment":"One more position"},
        "7215": {"comment":"Past it in the format"},
        "7218": {"synopsis":"Loop: every #, % or * that follows widens the field; any other character ends it.","comment":"Next format character"},
        "7221": {"comment":"#, % and * are positions"},
        "7233": {"comment":"The string's length byte"},
        "7239": {"comment":"A = width - length, the padding"},
        "7242": {"comment":"Longer than the field: error 8203"},
        "7246": {"comment":"Left aligned?"},
        "7250": {"comment":"Right aligned: all padding before it"},
        "7251": {"comment":"Centred: half the padding before it"},
        "7255": {"synopsis":"Leaves the padding that goes after the string in A.","comment":"Padding after the string"},
        "7256": {"synopsis":"Prints the padding before the string (C spaces, none for a left-aligned field), the string,\nthen the padding after it, and goes on with the next item."},
        "7258": {"comment":"Spaces before, unless left aligned"},
        "7262": {"comment":"Print the counted string at HL"},
        "7265": {"comment":"Spaces after it"},
        "7268": {"comment":"Drop it and go on"},
        "7271": {"synopsis":"Tells what the current PRINT token starts: A = 3 for the word USING, 2 for AT, 1 for symbol\n$03 (the # of a channel number), 0 for anything else (a print item). Used by PRINT_CHECK and\nPRINT_EXEC.\nExit: A = the kind.\nChanges: HL.","comment":"The text USING"},
        "7274": {"comment":"Current name the same?"},
        "7280": {"comment":"The text AT"},
        "7289": {"comment":"Symbol # (channel)?"},
        "7297": {"comment":"A print item"},
        "7299": {"synopsis":"Writes the cursor-moving escape sequence ESC = to the current output channel, then E + 32\nand D + 32 (PRINT AT's two values, E the first). Falls into PRINT_COORD for the last byte.\nEntry: E, D = the two coordinates.\nChanges: A, E.","comment":"ESC"},
        "7302": {"comment":"Print A"},
        "7304": {"comment":"="},
        "7307": {"comment":"Print A"},
        "7309": {"comment":"First coordinate"},
        "7312": {"comment":"Then the second"},
        "7313": {"synopsis":"Writes E + 32 to the current output channel (an escape sequence's coordinate byte)."},
        "7314": {"comment":"Coordinates go as value + 32"},
        "7317": {"comment":"Print A"},
        "7320": {"synopsis":"Entry to USING_LITERALS with the main registers active: switches to the other set first, so\nboth entries finish in the same set."},
        "7321": {"synopsis":"Prints the format's literal characters from the format pointer (HL of the other set) up to\nthe next character that starts a format item (one of USING_FMT_CHARS).\nExit: Z when one was found, HL' at it; NC and NZ when the format ended first. Both entries\nreturn with the main set active.","comment":"Do not step past the first character"},
        "7322": {"synopsis":"Loop: steps past a printed literal (carry set) and tests the next character."},
        "7323": {"comment":"First pass: stay on this character"},
        "7325": {"comment":"Past the printed literal"},
        "7327": {"synopsis":"Compares the format pointer with the format's last character and reads the character there.","comment":"At or before the format's last character?"},
        "7330": {"comment":"The format character"},
        "7334": {"comment":"Past the end: NC"},
        "7335": {"synopsis":"Looks the character up in USING_FMT_CHARS; a format character returns Z, any other is\nprinted as a literal.","comment":"Characters that start a format item"},
        "7338": {"comment":"9 of them"},
        "7340": {"synopsis":"Loop over the 9 format characters."},
        "7341": {"comment":"A format item starts here"},
        "7345": {"comment":"A literal: print it"},
        "7346": {"comment":"Print A (the literal)"},
        "7348": {"comment":"Step past it"},
        "7351": {"synopsis":"The 9 characters that start a PRINT USING format item: < > # * % + - $ ^, searched by\nUSING_LIT_CHAR. Any other character in a format string is printed as it is."},
        "7360": {"synopsis":"PRINT USING, a numeric item: prints the top number through the format item at the format\npointer.\n1. Reads the item's characters (USING_NUM_PARSE, USING_NUM_CHARS) into counters: L digit\n   positions, H those after the point, D the ^ (exponent) positions, E the fill character (*\n   or 0 given by % ), C the sign and currency flags (bit 0 negative, bit 1 $, bit 6 +, bit 7\n   -), BC' the position of the point (or of the first ^, or of the character that ended the\n   item).\n2. Rounds the number to the digits shown (USING_FIXED, USING_ROUND), makes it positive and\n   keeps its sign in C bit 0.\n3. Counts the integer positions that stay empty (USING_INT_SCAN); error 8203 (USING format\n   item too short) when the digits, the sign or the $ do not fit.\n4. Prints the fill or spaces, the sign and $, the integer digits with their commas, the\n   point and the fraction digits, and with ^ an exponent E+nn (USING_EXP_OUT).\nExit: the other set's HL (the format pointer) past the item.\nChanges: the main set and IY.","comment":"Format pointer set"},
        "7361": {"comment":"Keep its first and last character"},
        "7363": {"comment":"IY walks the format item"},
        "7366": {"comment":"No point seen yet (BC' = 0)"},
        "7370": {"comment":"All counters 0"},
        "7376": {"synopsis":"Loop: reads the next format character and jumps to its handler through USING_NUM_JUMPS (the\ncomma's handler is this loop: it is skipped here); a character not in USING_NUM_CHARS ends\nthe item (USING_PARSE_END).","comment":"Next format character"},
        "7383": {"comment":"The 11 characters of a numeric item"},
        "7389": {"comment":"C = 10 - its position"},
        "7391": {"comment":"Not one: the item ends"},
        "7393": {"comment":"Word offset"},
        "7395": {"comment":"Handlers in reverse order of the characters"},
        "7399": {"comment":"The handler's address"},
        "7404": {"comment":"Handler on the stack, HL back"},
        "7405": {"comment":"Jump to it"},
        "7406": {"synopsis":"+ in a numeric item: always print the sign (C bit 6)."},
        "7410": {"synopsis":"- in a numeric item: print - for a negative number and a space for a positive one (C bit 7)."},
        "7412": {"synopsis":"Sets sign flag A ($40 or $80) in C, clearing the other one; only before any digit position,\notherwise the sign character ends the item (a trailing sign is not part of it).","comment":"After a digit position?"},
        "7414": {"comment":"Yes: it ends the item"},
        "7417": {"comment":"Set this sign flag"},
        "7420": {"comment":"Clear the other one, keep bits 0-1"},
        "7426": {"synopsis":"$ in a numeric item: print a $ before the number (C bit 1); only before any digit position.","comment":"After a digit position?"},
        "7430": {"comment":"Print a $"},
        "7434": {"synopsis":"< or > in a numeric item: one digit position, only before any other.","comment":"After a digit position?"},
        "7438": {"comment":"One position"},
        "7441": {"synopsis":"* in a numeric item: a digit position, with * filling the unused leading ones.","comment":"Fill with *"},
        "7445": {"synopsis":"% in a numeric item: a digit position, with 0 filling the unused leading ones.","comment":"Fill with 0"},
        "7447": {"synopsis":"Counts a fill position; it must come before the point (BC' still 0), else error 8201.","comment":"One more digit position"},
        "7449": {"comment":"Point seen already?"},
        "7454": {"synopsis":"Raises error 8201 (Invalid USING string).","comment":"Error 8201: Invalid USING string"},
        "7457": {"synopsis":"# in a numeric item: a digit position; after the point it also counts as a fraction digit\n(H).","comment":"One more digit position"},
        "7459": {"comment":"Point seen yet?"},
        "7464": {"comment":"A fraction digit"},
        "7467": {"synopsis":"^ in a numeric item: an exponent position (D); the first one marks where the mantissa ends\nwhen there was no point.","comment":"Point (or a ^) seen yet?"},
        "7472": {"comment":"No: the mantissa ends here"},
        "7476": {"synopsis":"Counts one exponent position."},
        "7477": {"comment":"One more ^"},
        "7480": {"synopsis":". in a numeric item: keeps its position in BC'; a second point (or a point after ^) is error\n8201.","comment":"Point (or a ^) seen already?"},
        "7483": {"comment":"Yes: error 8201"},
        "7485": {"comment":"The point's position"},
        "7492": {"synopsis":"The item ended on a character that is not a numeric format character: drops the lookup's\nsaved registers."},
        "7494": {"synopsis":"The item is read: with no point and no ^, the character that ended it stands for the point.\nMakes the number a float and checks the exponent field: 1-3 ^ characters are error 8203.","comment":"Point or ^ seen?"},
        "7499": {"comment":"No: the end character is the point"},
        "7503": {"synopsis":"Converts the number to float form, keeping both register sets, then picks fixed or exponent\nform."},
