        "7919": {"comment":"New format pointer"},
        "7925": {"synopsis":"The 11 characters of a numeric format item, searched by USING_NUM_PARSE: + - $ < > * % # , ^\n. . A character's position k selects word 10 - k of USING_NUM_JUMPS."},
        "7936": {"synopsis":"USING_NUM_PARSE's handlers, in reverse order of USING_NUM_CHARS: . USING_POINT, ^\nUSING_CARET, , USING_NUM_PARSE (skipped), # USING_HASH, % USING_ZERO, * USING_STAR, > and <\nUSING_ALIGN, $ USING_DOLLAR, - USING_MINUS, + USING_PLUS."},
        "7958": {"synopsis":"Prints a $ when the format had one (C bit 1), then the sign: - for a negative number (C bit\n0); for a positive one a space when the format had - (bit 7), + when it had + (bit 6),\nnothing otherwise.\nEntry: C = the flags.\nChanges: A.","comment":"Print a $?"},
        "7965": {"comment":"Print the $"},
        "7967": {"synopsis":"Prints the sign.","comment":"Negative?"},
        "7973": {"comment":"The format's sign flags"},
        "7976": {"comment":"- in the format: a space"},
        "7982": {"comment":"No + either: no sign"},
        "7985": {"synopsis":"Prints the sign character in A."},
        "7986": {"comment":"Print the sign"},
        "7989": {"synopsis":"Prints A spaces to the current output channel (none when A is 0).\nEntry: A = the count (below 128).\nChanges: A, flags.","comment":"None left?"},
        "7992": {"comment":"A space"},
        "7995": {"comment":"Print the space"},
        "8000": {"synopsis":"Prints CR and LF to the current output channel.\nChanges: A.","comment":"CR"},
        "8003": {"comment":"Print CR"},
        "8005": {"comment":"LF"},
        "8008": {"comment":"Print LF"},
        "8011": {"synopsis":"IS-BASIC call $BF: builds the text of error HL in the buffer at $0446 as a length byte, a\nspace and the text.\n1. Divides by 1000 (A = the thousands). 9000-9999 are EXOS errors: EXOS 28 explains code HL\n   - 9000; when EXOS has a text it is used.\n2. Otherwise looks HL up in ERR_NUMBERS; when it is there, its entry in ERR_MESSAGES is\n   unpacked (TEXT_UNPACK_BUF) and carry is returned.\n3. Otherwise (and for any number below 256) the text is the error's class from ERR_CLASSES,\n   chosen by the thousands: 0-12 directly, 20 syntax, any other system; no carry.\nEntry: HL = the error number.\nExit: carry when the text is the error's own, NC for a class name; ($0446) the length + 1.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, the other register set."},
        "8012": {"comment":"1000"},
        "8015": {"comment":"Count the thousands"},
        "8018": {"synopsis":"Loop: A = how many times 1000 goes into HL."},
        "8023": {"comment":"9000-9999: an EXOS error?"},
        "8028": {"comment":"9000"},
        "8032": {"comment":"Text after the length byte at $0447"},
        "8035": {"comment":"A = the EXOS error code"},
        "8039": {"comment":"EXOS 28: explain error code into ($0447)"},
        "8041": {"comment":"Its length, + 1 "},
        "8047": {"comment":"... at $0446"},
        "8050": {"comment":"A space before the text"},
        "8054": {"comment":"Had a text: done (carry from the NEG)"},
        "8055": {"comment":"No text: class 9 (EXOS)"},
        "8057": {"synopsis":"BC = the error number; numbers below 256 have only a class text, others are searched in\nERR_NUMBERS."},
        "8060": {"comment":"Below 256?"},
        "8064": {"comment":"Entry counter from -1"},
        "8066": {"comment":"The error numbers"},
        "8069": {"synopsis":"Loop over ERR_NUMBERS: A counts the entries; a word with a zero high byte ends the table."},
        "8074": {"comment":"End of the table?"},
        "8078": {"comment":"This error?"},
        "8087": {"comment":"The packed messages; A = which"},
        "8090": {"synopsis":"Unpacks text A of the packed table at HL into the buffer ($0447 length, text from $0448),\nthen makes it a space plus the text, with the length at $0446.\nExit: carry.","comment":"Unpack into $0447"},
        "8097": {"comment":"The length "},
        "8098": {"comment":"... becomes a leading space"},
        "8101": {"comment":"Length + 1 at $0446"},
        "8103": {"comment":"The error's own text"},
        "8105": {"synopsis":"No text of its own: the class from ERR_CLASSES by the thousands: 0-12 directly, 20 is entry\n13, every other entry 14.","comment":"The class names"},
        "8108": {"comment":"A = the thousands"},
        "8111": {"comment":"0-12: the class directly"},
        "8114": {"comment":"20000s: syntax"},
        "8118": {"comment":"Others: system"},
        "8119": {"synopsis":"A = 13 (syntax) or 14 (system)."},
        "8120": {"synopsis":"Unpacks the class name; returns NC (no specific text)."},
        "8124": {"comment":"Only a class name: no carry"},
        "8126": {"synopsis":"The IS-BASIC error numbers that have their own text, 60 words in ascending order (1000,\n1001, 1002, 1051, 1106, 2001 ... 20081, 30000), ended by $0000 at $2036. Entry k's text is\ntext k of ERR_MESSAGES. Searched by ERR_SEARCH_LOOP."},
        "8248": {"synopsis":"The 60 error texts of ERR_NUMBERS, packed (TEXT_UNPACK reads them): a bit stream read from\nbit 7 of each byte, in 4-bit codes. 0 ends a text; 1-13 are E O N R T A I S C L D U and\nspace (TEXT_CHARS); 14 and a 4-bit n is one of P K F B V Y W M G H Q X Z $ - / ; 15 and a\n5-bit n is TEXT_WORDS' word n - 1, or with n = 0 makes the letters up to the next space\ncapitals. Letters come out in lower case; TEXT_UNPACK_BUF capitalises the first. Text 0 is\n\"unexpected value given\" (error 1000), text 59 \"BASIC data has been corrupted\" (error\n30000). Texts follow each other with no padding, so a text is found by unpacking every one\nbefore it."},
        "8806": {"synopsis":"Fifteen error class names in the same packed form, chosen by ERR_CLASS_TEXT from the\nthousands of the error number: user, overflow, subscript, mathematical, parameter, storage\nexhausted, matrix, file use, input-output, EXOS, control, graphical, real-time, syntax\n(20000s), system (any other)."},
        "8879": {"synopsis":"The packed word list that code 15 + n selects (word n - 1), 31 words in the same packed\nform, each ending with a space except three (identifier expected, parameter, too long):\nfile, error, invalid, EXOS, editor, argument to, channel, editor load file, number,\ninsufficient, end of block, identifier, identifier expected, argument, out of range,\noverflow, EXOS function, parameter, video, not, string, open, memory, index to, module, does\nnot exist, statement, too long, line number, device, network. Shared by IS-BASIC's error\ntexts and EXOS's own (the extension's explain error code, EXOS_ERR_TEXTS, and the help code\nat $3515\nboth unpack through TEXT_UNPACK_BUF)."},
        "9052": {"synopsis":"Unpacks text A of a packed text table (ERR_MESSAGES' form) to DE' as plain characters: skips\nA texts code by code, then decodes codes until a 0. A word code calls TEXT_UNPACK again on\nTEXT_WORDS, so the words are packed the same way.\nEntry: HL = the table, A = the text's index, DE' = the output.\nExit: DE' after the last character.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, B'.","comment":"No bits left: the first read loads a byte"},
        "9054": {"comment":"Texts to skip"},
        "9055": {"synopsis":"Loop: skips one more text, or starts decoding when none is left.","comment":"All skipped?"},
        "9059": {"synopsis":"Loop over one text's codes until the 0 that ends it; codes 14 and 15 skip their extra 4 or 5\nbits.","comment":"Next 4-bit code"},
        "9063": {"comment":"0 ends the text"},
        "9066": {"comment":"14 or 15?"},
        "9071": {"comment":"Code 14: 4 more bits"},
        "9073": {"comment":"Code 15: 5 more bits"},
        "9078": {"synopsis":"Reads past the code's extra bits."},
        "9083": {"synopsis":"Decodes the text: B' = $20 makes letters lower case."},
        "9084": {"comment":"Lower case"},
        "9087": {"synopsis":"Loop: reads a 4-bit code; 0 ends the text, 1-13 index TEXT_CHARS.","comment":"Next 4-bit code"},
        "9092": {"comment":"0: end of the text"},
        "9093": {"comment":"14 or 15?"},
        "9100": {"comment":"Base of TEXT_CHARS (code 1 is its first)"},
        "9103": {"synopsis":"Picks character A of the table at HL."},
        "9108": {"synopsis":"A space switches back to lower case.","comment":"The character"},
        "9109": {"comment":"A space ends a capitals run"},
        "9114": {"synopsis":"Stores the character, lower-cased unless capitals are on (bit 5 from B').","comment":"Lower case unless capitals are on"},
        "9115": {"comment":"Into the output"},
        "9120": {"synopsis":"Code 14: a 4-bit index into the 16 rarer characters at $23FF.","comment":"Code 15?"},
        "9124": {"comment":"4-bit index"},
        "9128": {"comment":"P K F B V Y W M G H Q X Z $ - /"},
        "9133": {"synopsis":"Code 15: 5 more bits; 0 turns capitals on up to the next space, n inserts word n - 1 of\nTEXT_WORDS.","comment":"5-bit argument"},
        "9138": {"comment":"A word?"},
        "9142": {"comment":"0: capitals on"},
        "9146": {"synopsis":"Unpacks word A - 1 of TEXT_WORDS into the output, keeping this text's reading position.","comment":"Keep this text's bit position"},
        "9148": {"comment":"The word list"},
        "9151": {"comment":"Word n - 1"},
        "9159": {"synopsis":"Reads the next 4 bits of the packed stream into A. Falls into BITS_GET.","comment":"Marker bit: 4 shifts bring it to carry"},
        "9161": {"synopsis":"Reads bits of the packed stream into A, most significant first, until the marker bit preset\nin A ($10 for 4 bits, $08 for 5) shifts out.\nEntry: HL = the next byte, C = the bits left in the current byte, B = their count.\nExit: A = the bits; HL, B, C moved on.","comment":"Bits left in this byte?"},
        "9163": {"comment":"Load the next byte"},
        "9165": {"comment":"8 bits in it"},
        "9167": {"synopsis":"Shifts the byte's top bit into A; loops until the marker bit leaves A.","comment":"Top bit of the byte "},
        "9169": {"comment":"... into A; the marker out?"},
        "9173": {"synopsis":"Unpacks text A of the packed table at HL into a counted buffer at DE: the text from DE + 1,\nits last space dropped, its first letter made a capital, its length at DE. Used by\nERR_TEXT_BUILD and by EXOS code ($3515, EXOS_ERR_UNPACK).\nEntry: HL = the table, A = the text's index, DE = the buffer.\nExit: DE = the buffer; L = the length.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL, the other register set."},
        "9174": {"comment":"DE' = the buffer + 1, the output"},
        "9179": {"comment":"Unpack the text"},
        "9183": {"comment":"Where the text started"},
        "9184": {"comment":"The last character a space?"},
        "9190": {"comment":"No: keep it"},
        "9191": {"synopsis":"Capitalises the first letter and stores the length before the text."},
        "9192": {"comment":"First letter in capitals"},
        "9196": {"comment":"The length"},
        "9200": {"comment":"Before the text"},
        "9202": {"synopsis":"TEXT_UNPACK's two character tables: E O N R T A I S C L D U and space for codes 1-13 (the\ncode indexes from $23F1), then P K F B V Y W M G H Q X Z $ - / for code 14 and n (n = 0-15,\nfrom $23FF). The first 13 are the letters the error texts use most."},
        "9231": {"synopsis":"Segment 1's service entry, reached through the JP at $000D ($C00D) from segment 0's\nSEG1_SERVICE with segment 1 in page 3. A = the service number: 0 read time, 1 set time, 2\nread date, 3 set date, 4 the one-second tick, 5 load a relocatable module, 6 start-up (cold\nstart). 0 falls into SVC_READ_TIME; numbers above 6 also end there.","comment":"Service 6: start-up"},
        "9236": {"comment":"Service 1: set time"},
        "9239": {"comment":"Service 2: read date"},
        "9242": {"comment":"Service 3: set date"},
        "9245": {"comment":"Service 4: the one-second tick"},
        "9248": {"comment":"Service 5: load relocatable"},
        "9252": {"synopsis":"Service 0, EXOS 32 (read time): returns C = hours, D = minutes, E = seconds (BCD) from\n$BF74, $BF73 and $BF72, read with interrupts off so the tick cannot change them halfway.\nExit: A = 0.","comment":"Seconds to E, minutes to D"},
        "9257": {"comment":"Hours"},
        "9262": {"comment":"Status 0"},
        "9264": {"synopsis":"Service 2, EXOS 34 (read date): returns C = year, D = month, E = day (BCD) from $BF77, $BF76\nand $BF75, read with interrupts off.\nExit: A = 0.","comment":"Day to E, month to D"},
        "9269": {"comment":"Year"},
        "9274": {"comment":"Status 0"},
        "9276": {"synopsis":"Service 1, EXOS 31 (set time): C = hours, D = minutes, E = seconds (BCD). Each must be a BCD\nnumber below $24, $60 and $60 (CHECK_BCD); a bad one returns error $EB (.ITIME) without\nchanging the clock. Otherwise the three bytes go to $BF72-$BF74 with interrupts off.\nExit: A = 0 or $EB.","comment":"Seconds below $60?"},
        "9282": {"comment":"Minutes below $60?"},
        "9288": {"comment":"Hours below $24?"},
        "9294": {"comment":"Store with the tick held off"},
        "9304": {"comment":"Status 0"},
        "9306": {"synopsis":"Service 3, EXOS 33 (set date): C = year, D = month, E = day (BCD). The year must be BCD\n(00-99), the month 01-12 and the day 1 to the month's length in that year (DAYS_IN_MONTH,\nFebruary 29 in a leap year); a bad value returns error $EB (.ITIME) unchanged. Otherwise the\nbytes go to $BF75-$BF77 with interrupts off.\nExit: A = 0 or $EB.","comment":"Year: any BCD number"},
        "9312": {"comment":"Month 01-12?"},
        "9318": {"comment":"B = days in this month"},
        "9321": {"comment":"Day 1 to the last day?"},
        "9326": {"comment":"Store with the tick held off"},
        "9336": {"comment":"Status 0"},
        "9338": {"synopsis":"Service 4, the one-second tick (segment 0's 1 Hz interrupt paths ask for it).\n1. On about one tick in eight (the low three bits of R are 0) checks the bytes of this\n   segment: the byte at $BF7E (set by SVC_STARTUP from 25 bytes of this ROM, $A7) minus the\n   229 bytes from SVC_STARTUP (CHECK_LEN, subtracted with borrow) minus the byte at $FFFD\n(offset\n   $3FFD) must be 0. If not, the byte at $BF00 + the low byte of $BFEC (the interrupt\n   counter) is decremented: a system-segment byte picked by the counter is corrupted. With\n   this ROM's bytes the result is 0.\n2. Adds 1 to SECOND_COUNTER ($BFF0).\n3. If TIMER (EXOS variable 5, $BFCA) is not 0 it counts down; reaching 0 sets FLAG_SOFT_IRQ\n   ($BFF2) to $40, the software interrupt for the timer.\n4. Advances the clock at $BF72-$BF77 (TICK_CLOCK).","comment":"Refresh counter as a random number"},
        "9340": {"comment":"One tick in eight?"},
        "9344": {"comment":"HL = CHECK_LEN"},
        "9347": {"comment":"B = 229 bytes"},
        "9348": {"comment":"Start from the value kept at $BF7E"},
        "9351": {"synopsis":"Loop: subtracts the next byte, with borrow, for B bytes.","comment":"Next byte"},
        "9355": {"comment":"The byte at offset $3FFD"},
        "9358": {"comment":"Result 0: the bytes are intact"},
        "9361": {"comment":"Low byte: the interrupt counter"},
        "9364": {"comment":"Points at a byte of $BF00-$BFFF"},
        "9366": {"comment":"Corrupt it"},
        "9367": {"synopsis":"Counts the second and runs TIMER, then the clock (all ticks).","comment":"SECOND_COUNTER"},
        "9374": {"comment":"TIMER (variable 5)"},
        "9378": {"comment":"Stopped?"},
        "9381": {"comment":"Count down; zero now?"},
        "9384": {"comment":"Software interrupt $40: timer"},
        "9389": {"synopsis":"Advances the clock and the calendar by one second. CLOCK_INC_FIELD steps through $BF72\n(seconds, wraps after $59), $BF73 (minutes, $59), $BF74 (hours, $23), $BF75 (day: wraps to 1\nafter the month's last day from DAYS_IN_MONTH), $BF76 (month: wraps to 1 after $12) and\n$BF77 (year, BCD 99 then 00); the first field that does not wrap ends the tick\n(CLOCK_INC_FIELD returns from here).","comment":"HL steps to $BF72 first"},
        "9392": {"comment":"Seconds wrap after $59"},
        "9397": {"comment":"Minutes: B still $59"},
        "9400": {"comment":"Hours wrap after $23"},
        "9405": {"comment":"Midnight: keep the field pointer"},
        "9407": {"comment":"L = month, H = year"},
        "9410": {"comment":"D = month"},
        "9411": {"comment":"C = year"},
        "9412": {"comment":"B = days in this month"},
        "9417": {"comment":"Day"},
        "9420": {"comment":"After the last day: day 1"},
        "9421": {"comment":"Month wraps after $12"},
        "9426": {"comment":"Month 1"},
        "9427": {"comment":"Year: $99 + 1 gives $00 (DAA)"},
        "9432": {"comment":"Only for a year byte of $FF"},
        "9433": {"synopsis":"Adds 1 to one BCD clock field.\nEntry: HL = the field's address - 1; B = the field's last value.\nExit: HL = the field. If the field held B it becomes 0 and the routine returns to its caller\n(go on to the next field); otherwise the field gets its value + 1 (BCD) and the routine\ndrops its return address, so it returns from its caller (the tick ends).\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"To the field"},
        "9435": {"comment":"At its last value?"},
        "9436": {"comment":"Wrap to 0 (LD keeps the flags)"},
        "9438": {"comment":"Yes: on to the next field"},
        "9439": {"comment":"BCD + 1"},
        "9443": {"comment":"Drop the return address"},
        "9444": {"comment":"Returns from the caller"},
        "9445": {"synopsis":"Gives the number of days of a month.\nEntry: D = month (BCD 01-12), C = year (BCD).\nExit: B = days (BCD) from MONTH_DAYS; February's entry ($80) becomes $28, or $29 when the\nyear divides by 4 (00 counts).\nChanges: AF, HL; DE and C are kept.","comment":"Keep DE and C"},
        "9447": {"comment":"DE = month"},
        "9450": {"comment":"HL = MONTH_DAYS - 1"},
        "9454": {"comment":"Year: tens bit 0, units bits 1-0"},
        "9459": {"comment":"Odd tens: units 2 or 6 give 0"},
        "9461": {"synopsis":"Carry is set when the masked year is 0: a leap year.","comment":"Carry: leap year"},
        "9468": {"comment":"$80 + $A8 + leap carry = $28 or $29"},
        "9470": {"synopsis":"Returns the day count in B.","comment":"C restored"},
        "9471": {"comment":"B = days"},
        "9474": {"synopsis":"Days in each month (BCD), indexed by the BCD month from $2501 (DAYS_IN_MONTH): entries for\nmonths 01-09, six unused zeros for $0A-$0F, then months 10-12. February's $80 is a marker\nthat DAYS_IN_MONTH turns into 28 or 29.","comment":"January"},
        "9475": {"comment":"February (28 or 29)"},
        "9476": {"comment":"March"},
        "9477": {"comment":"April"},
        "9478": {"comment":"May"},
        "9479": {"comment":"June"},
        "9480": {"comment":"July"},
        "9481": {"comment":"August"},
        "9482": {"comment":"September"},
        "9483": {"comment":"Months $0A-$0F (not BCD): unused"},
        "9489": {"comment":"October"},
        "9490": {"comment":"November"},
        "9491": {"comment":"December"},
        "9492": {"synopsis":"Checks a BCD value that must not be 0, then falls into CHECK_BCD.\nEntry: A = value, B = the limit.\nExit: as CHECK_BCD; 0 fails.","comment":"Zero?"},
        "9495": {"synopsis":"Checks a BCD value against a limit for the set time and set date services.\nEntry: A = value, B = the limit (the value must be below it).\nExit: returns with A kept when both digits are 0-9 and A < B. Otherwise drops its return\naddress and returns error $EB (.ITIME) from the service itself.\nChanges: F.","comment":"Keep the value"},
        "9496": {"comment":"Tens digit 0-9?"},
        "9500": {"comment":"Units digit"},
        "9502": {"comment":"0-9?"},
        "9506": {"comment":"Value back"},
        "9507": {"comment":"Below the limit?"},
        "9510": {"synopsis":"Bad digit: drops the value pushed at CHECK_BCD, then BCD_BAD.","comment":"Drop the saved value"},
        "9511": {"synopsis":"Drops the return address and returns error $EB (.ITIME) to the service's caller.","comment":"Drop the return address"},
        "9512": {"comment":".ITIME: invalid date or time"},
        "9515": {"synopsis":"Service 5, EXOS 30 (load relocatable module): reads a module from the channel kept at $BF80\nand writes it from DE on. Segment 0 has paged the destination's segment into page 1; every\nbyte is written through page 1 (RELOC_PUT_BYTE). The module is a bit stream, read most\nsignificant bit first (RELOC_GET_BITS):\n1. 0 + 8 bits: one byte, stored as it is.\n2. 1 00 + 16 bits: a word; the word plus its own load position is stored (two bytes).\n3. 1 01 1 + 16 bits: skips that many bytes of the destination.\n4. 1 01 0 then 0 + 2 bits: sets the top two bits of the load position (the Z80 page the\n   following words are relocated for) to those bits; 1 01 0 then 1 restores the top bits of\n   the original load address (kept at $BF7F).\n5. 1 10: the end, A = 0.\n6. 1 11: error $ED (.IREL).\nA read error ends the load with the EXOS error.","comment":"Keep the load address's high byte"},
        "9519": {"comment":"Bit buffer empty: read a byte first"},
        "9521": {"comment":"HL = the load position"},
        "9522": {"synopsis":"Loop: reads the next three-bit code and acts on it.","comment":"Marker for three bits"},
        "9527": {"comment":"First bit 0: a literal byte?"},
        "9531": {"comment":"Six more bits: the byte"},
        "9536": {"comment":"Store it"},
        "9538": {"synopsis":"First bit 1: the next two bits pick the action.","comment":"00: a word to relocate?"},
        "9542": {"comment":"DE = the word"},
        "9545": {"comment":"Read error"},
        "9546": {"comment":"DE = word + its position"},
        "9549": {"comment":"Store low byte"},
        "9553": {"synopsis":"Stores D (the literal byte, or the high byte of a relocated word) and goes on.","comment":"Store D"},
        "9557": {"comment":"Next code"},
        "9559": {"synopsis":"Codes 01, 10 and 11.","comment":"01?"},
        "9562": {"comment":"10: the end, A = 0"},
        "9564": {"comment":".IREL: invalid relocatable module"},
        "9567": {"synopsis":"Code 01: one more bit chooses a skip (1) or a page change (0).","comment":"Read one bit"},
        "9570": {"comment":"Into carry"},
        "9573": {"comment":"DE = bytes to skip"},
        "9577": {"comment":"Past them"},
        "9580": {"synopsis":"Page change: one more bit; 1 takes the original load address's page, 0 reads a 2-bit page.","comment":"Read one bit"},
        "9584": {"comment":"The original high byte (LD keeps carry)"},
        "9589": {"comment":"Marker for two bits"},
        "9594": {"comment":"Page bits to bits 7-6"},
        "9596": {"synopsis":"Puts A's bits 7-6 into the top bits of H, the load position's page.","comment":"Merge bits 7-6 of A into H"},
        "9603": {"synopsis":"Writes A at the load position through page 1 ($4000-$7FFF, whatever HL's page bits say) and\nadvances HL.\nChanges: HL.","comment":"Same offset, page 1"},
        "9609": {"comment":"Load position back"},
        "9610": {"comment":"Next position"},
        "9612": {"synopsis":"Reads a 16-bit word from the stream, low byte first.\nExit: DE = the word, carry set; on a read error returns NC with A = the error.\nChanges: AF, B, C, DE.","comment":"D = low byte"},
        "9615": {"comment":"E = low byte; falls in for the high byte"},
        "9616": {"synopsis":"Reads eight bits.\nExit: A = D = the byte.","comment":"Marker for eight bits"},
        "9620": {"synopsis":"Reads one bit.\nExit: A = D = the bit (0 or 1).","comment":"Marker for one bit"},
        "9622": {"synopsis":"Reads bits from the stream into A, shifting them in from bit 0, until the marker bit set in\nA on entry reaches carry: A = 1 << (8 - n) reads n bits; bits already in A below the marker\nstay in front.\nEntry: A = the marker; B = bits left in C + 1, C = the current byte's bits.\nExit: A = D = the bits, carry set. When C is empty, reads the next byte from the channel at\n$BF80 (EXOS 5). A read error drops the saved A and its own return address, so it returns\nfrom its caller with A = the error.\nChanges: AF, B, C, D.","comment":"Bits left in C?"},
        "9624": {"comment":"Keep the marker"},
        "9626": {"comment":"The module's channel"},
        "9632": {"comment":"Read error?"},
        "9634": {"comment":"Marker back"},
        "9635": {"comment":"C = the new byte"},
        "9636": {"comment":"Eight bits in it"},
        "9638": {"synopsis":"Shifts the next bit of C into A; loops until the marker leaves A.","comment":"Next bit to carry"},
        "9640": {"comment":"Into A; marker out?"},
        "9643": {"comment":"D = the bits too"},
        "9645": {"synopsis":"Read error: drops the saved marker and the return address, so the caller's caller gets the\nerror.","comment":"Drop the saved marker"},
        "9646": {"comment":"Drop the return address"},
        "9648": {"synopsis":"Device read block through the device's read-character routine (TAPE and SERIAL jump here).\nEntry: HL = the read-character routine, DE = the user's buffer, BC = the byte count; page 1\nholds the channel's segment.\n1. Keeps page 1's segment in A' and pages the buffer into page 1 (PAGE_USER_BUF).\n2. For each byte: pages the channel back, calls the routine with IX and IY kept, then pages\n   the buffer and stores the routine's B. After each call EXX: the saved registers are\n   popped into the other register set, so the routine's B is read back from the set it used\n   and the two sets alternate byte by byte.\n3. A buffer address that runs past page 1 pages the next segment (the copy of DE on the\n   stack advances with each byte).\nExit: A = 0 when all bytes are read, or the routine's error; DE = the buffer address after\nthe last byte.","comment":"Page 1: the channel's segment"},
        "9650": {"comment":"Kept in A'"},
        "9652": {"synopsis":"Pages the user's buffer at the current address into page 1.","comment":"DE = the user's address"},
        "9654": {"comment":"Buffer into page 1"},
        "9659": {"synopsis":"Loop: reads one byte through the routine and stores it.","comment":"A = the buffer's segment"},
        "9661": {"comment":"Channel's segment"},
        "9662": {"comment":"Back into page 1"},
        "9664": {"comment":"A' = channel, A = buffer"},
        "9669": {"comment":"A = the channel's segment"},
        "9675": {"comment":"Read a character: B"},
        "9682": {"comment":"Keep the status"},
        "9683": {"comment":"The channel's segment"},
        "9686": {"comment":"Saved registers into the other set"},
        "9691": {"comment":"A = status, A' = buffer's segment"},
        "9692": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "9695": {"comment":"A = the channel's segment"},
        "9697": {"comment":"Swap: A = buffer's segment"},
        "9698": {"comment":"Buffer into page 1"},
        "9700": {"comment":"B from the routine's set"},
        "9703": {"comment":"Store the byte"},
        "9705": {"comment":"Advance the caller's DE"},
        "9708": {"comment":"One byte fewer"},
        "9709": {"comment":"Past page 1?"},
        "9713": {"synopsis":"Ends when BC reaches 0.","comment":"Bytes left?"},
        "9717": {"synopsis":"Returns DE as advanced over the bytes done.","comment":"DE = the advanced buffer address"},
        "9719": {"synopsis":"PRINTER, write block (entry +16): sends the user's bytes one at a time through PRINTER's\nwrite-character routine (PRN_WRITE_CHAR), falling into DEV_BLOCK_WRITE.","comment":"PRINTER's write character"},
        "9722": {"synopsis":"Device write block through the device's write-character routine (PRINTER falls in, TAPE and\nSERIAL jump here).\nEntry: HL = the write-character routine, DE = the user's buffer, BC = the byte count; page 1\nholds the channel's segment.\n1. Keeps the channel's segment and pages in the buffer's segment to learn it\n   (PAGE_USER_BUF), then pages the channel back; A' holds the buffer's segment.\n2. For each byte: reads it from the buffer through page 1, pages the channel back and calls\n   the routine with B = the byte, IX and IY kept. After each call EXX: the saved registers\n   are popped into the other register set, so the sets alternate byte by byte.\n3. A buffer address that runs past page 1 pages the next segment.\nExit: A = 0 when all bytes are written, or the routine's error; DE = the buffer address\nafter the last byte.","comment":"Keep the user's address"},
        "9723": {"synopsis":"Finds the segment of the user's buffer at the current address.","comment":"Page 1: the channel's segment"},
        "9725": {"comment":"Kept in A'"},
        "9728": {"comment":"Buffer into page 1"},
        "9731": {"comment":"The buffer's segment"},
        "9734": {"comment":"A = the channel's segment"},
        "9735": {"comment":"Back into page 1"},
        "9738": {"comment":"A' = the buffer's segment"},
        "9741": {"synopsis":"Loop: fetches one byte and writes it through the routine.","comment":"Keep count, address, routine"},
        "9744": {"comment":"Channel's segment"},
        "9747": {"comment":"A = the buffer's segment"},
        "9748": {"comment":"Buffer into page 1"},
        "9751": {"comment":"The byte"},
        "9753": {"comment":"Channel's segment"},
        "9754": {"comment":"Back into page 1"},
        "9756": {"comment":"A = buffer's segment"},
        "9764": {"comment":"Write the character in B"},
        "9771": {"comment":"Keep the status"},
        "9772": {"comment":"Channel's segment"},
        "9773": {"comment":"Into page 1"},
        "9775": {"comment":"Saved registers into the other set"},
        "9780": {"comment":"A = status, A' = buffer's segment"},
        "9781": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "9785": {"comment":"Advance the caller's DE"},
        "9788": {"comment":"Next byte"},
        "9789": {"comment":"Past page 1?"},
        "9793": {"synopsis":"Ends when BC reaches 0.","comment":"Bytes left?"},
        "9797": {"synopsis":"Returns DE as advanced over the bytes done.","comment":"DE = the advanced buffer address"},
        "9799": {"synopsis":"Pages a user's address into page 1. The top two bits of D pick the segment that was in that\npage at the EXOS call (USR_P0-USR_P3, $BFFC-$BFFF); it goes into page 1 and DE becomes the\nsame byte's page-1 address ($4000-$7FFF).\nEntry: DE = the user's address.\nExit: DE = its page-1 address.\nChanges: AF, D.","comment":"Page bits to bits 1-0"},
        "9805": {"comment":"USR_P0 + page"},
        "9810": {"comment":"That page's segment"},
        "9811": {"comment":"Into page 1"},
        "9813": {"comment":"Address into $4000-$7FFF"},
        "9819": {"synopsis":"Adjusts the word at HL + 2 (falls into ADJ_PTR). TAPE's buffer-moved routine uses it for the\nword at $B2D3.","comment":"Skip the first word"},
        "9821": {"synopsis":"Adds BC to a pointer word in RAM, for a device whose buffer has moved.\nEntry: HL = the word, BC = the distance moved; with Z set the result is also made a page-1\naddress ($4000-$7FFF). Both TAPE calls come with Z set (no flag here changes it).\nChanges: DE, HL.","comment":"Low byte"},
        "9824": {"comment":"HL = the pointer"},
        "9825": {"comment":"Moved by BC (Z is kept)"},
        "9826": {"comment":"Page-1 address wanted?"},
        "9828": {"comment":"Into $4000-$7FFF"},
        "9832": {"synopsis":"Writes the adjusted pointer back.","comment":"DE = the new pointer"},
        "9833": {"comment":"High byte"},
        "9837": {"synopsis":"Number of bytes SVC_TICK subtracts from SVC_STARTUP on: 229 ($E5), up to $2752 (SVC_STARTUP,\nits\nbanner and its texts)."},
        "9838": {"synopsis":"Service 6, the start-up after a cold start (segment 0 jumps to SEG1_SERVICE with A = 6).\n1. EXOS 0 (reset) with C = $20: relinks the devices and initialises the extensions again.\n2. Stack at $0200; interrupts on.\n3. If CRDISP_FLAG ($BFEF) is 0 (no extension asked to suppress it), shows the start-up\n   banner and waits for a key (START_BANNER).\n4. Closes the banner's channels $98, $97 and $96.\n5. Stores $AC XOR the 25 bytes at $FFD8-$FFF0 (offsets $3FD8-$3FF0 of this segment, giving\n   $A7) at $BF7E, the value SVC_TICK checks.\n6. Clears $BF78, so EXOS 26 offers the cold-start action to the extensions, and calls EXOS\n   26; an extension that takes control does not come back.\n7. If EXOS 26 returns, falls into START_BANNER (banner again, wait for a key) and returns\n   through the stack set at step 2.","comment":"Reset flags: bit 5"},
        "9840": {"comment":"EXOS 0: relink devices, init extensions"},
        "9842": {"comment":"Fresh stack"},
        "9846": {"comment":"CRDISP_FLAG"},
        "9849": {"comment":"Banner wanted?"},
        "9853": {"comment":"Close the banner's channels"},
        "9865": {"comment":"25 bytes of this ROM"},
        "9868": {"comment":"Seed"},
        "9870": {"comment":"Count"},
        "9872": {"synopsis":"Loop: XORs the 25 bytes into A.","comment":"Next byte"},
        "9876": {"comment":"$A7: kept for SVC_TICK"},
        "9879": {"comment":"Extensions get the cold start"},
        "9883": {"comment":"EXOS 26: scan ROM extensions"},
        "9885": {"synopsis":"Shows the start-up banner and waits for a key.\n1. Opens the channels of BANNER_CHANNELS through the list opener at WP_OPEN_CHANS (A'\n   non-zero: an\n   open error returns NZ): channel $98, VIDEO: in hardware text mode (MODE_VID 0, COLR_VID\n   0), 40 x 2; channel $97, VIDEO: in high-resolution pixel graphics with 256 colours\n   (MODE_VID 1, COLR_VID 3), 40 x 2; channel $96, KEYBOARD:.\n2. Displays two rows of each (EXOS 11, @@DISP): $98 at screen row 21, $97 at row 10.\n3. Writes BANNER_COPYRIGHT to $98.\n4. Until a key is waiting on $96 (EXOS 9), puts the graphics beam at (0, 71) and writes\n   \"ENTERPRISE\" on $97 letter by letter, each with an ink colour from R (ESC I), so the word\n   keeps changing colour.\nExit: A = 0 once a key is waiting, or NZ with an EXOS error.","comment":"The channel list"},
        "9888": {"comment":"A non-zero: open errors return"},
        "9889": {"comment":"Text page $98"},
        "9893": {"comment":"Graphics page $97"},
        "9897": {"comment":"KEYBOARD: on $96"},
        "9901": {"comment":"Text page"},
        "9903": {"comment":"@@DISP, from its row 1"},
        "9906": {"comment":"2 rows at screen row 21"},
        "9912": {"comment":"Graphics page"},
        "9917": {"comment":"2 rows at screen row 10"},
        "9923": {"comment":"Copyright line"},
        "9926": {"comment":"To the text page"},
        "9932": {"synopsis":"Loop: returns once a key is waiting, else redraws \"ENTERPRISE\".","comment":"Keyboard channel"},
        "9936": {"comment":"C = 0: a key is waiting"},
        "9938": {"comment":"Beam to the word's place"},
        "9941": {"comment":"On the graphics page"},
        "9945": {"synopsis":"Loop: writes the next letter of BANNER_NAME in a random ink; at its 0 goes back to\nBANNER_WAIT.","comment":"Next letter"},
        "9946": {"comment":"End of the word?"},
        "9950": {"comment":"Build a 4-byte list at $0100"},
        "9953": {"comment":"The letter"},
        "9955": {"comment":"Random ink colour"},
        "9959": {"comment":"ESC I: set ink"},
        "9962": {"comment":"ESC"},
        "9965": {"comment":"Four bytes"},
        "9967": {"comment":"Write it on the graphics page"},
        "9972": {"comment":"Next letter"},
        "9975": {"synopsis":"Writes a counted byte list to channel $97 (falls into WRITE_LIST).","comment":"Graphics page channel"},
        "9977": {"synopsis":"Writes a counted byte list to a channel.\nEntry: HL = the list (a count byte, then the bytes), C = the channel.\nExit: HL past the list; A = 0, or NZ with the EXOS error.\nChanges: AF, B, HL.","comment":"B = the count"},
        "9979": {"synopsis":"Loop: writes one byte of the list.","comment":"Keep count and channel"},
        "9981": {"comment":"The next byte"},
        "9985": {"comment":"Count and channel back"},
        "9990": {"synopsis":"Copyright line for the text page, written by WRITE_LIST: a count (37), then ESC o (cursor\noff), four spaces, character $80, a space and \"1985 Intelligent Software Ltd\".","comment":"37 bytes follow"},
        "10028": {"synopsis":"Counted list (6 bytes) for the graphics page: ESC A with x = 0 and y = 71 (two 16-bit\nvalues, low byte first), where the word is drawn.","comment":"6 bytes follow"},
        "10035": {"synopsis":"The word written letter by letter in changing colours, ended by $00."},
        "10046": {"synopsis":"Three lists for the opener at WP_OPEN_CHANS, one per call: a byte below $80 is an EXOS\nvariable\nnumber followed by its value (set with EXOS 16); a byte with bit 7 set is a channel followed\nby the address of its device name (opened with EXOS 1), which ends the list.","comment":"MODE_VID (22) = 0: hardware text"},
        "10048": {"comment":"COLR_VID (23) = 0: two colours"},
        "10050": {"comment":"X_SIZ_VID (24) = 40"},
        "10052": {"comment":"Y_SIZ_VID (25) = 2"},
        "10054": {"comment":"Channel $98, name at WP_DEV_VIDEO: \"VIDEO:\""},
        "10057": {"comment":"MODE_VID = 1: high-resolution graphics"},
        "10059": {"comment":"COLR_VID = 3: 256 colours"},
        "10061": {"comment":"Channel $97, \"VIDEO:\""},
        "10064": {"comment":"Channel $96, name at WP_DEV_KEYBOARD: \"KEYBOARD:\""},
        "10067": {"synopsis":"Device entry for calls a device does not support: returns error $E7 (.NOFN). PRINTER's read\ncharacter, read block, read status and set status, and TAPE's set status.","comment":"Error .NOFN"},
        "10070": {"synopsis":"Jumps to HL: DEV_BLOCK_READ and DEV_BLOCK_WRITE call it to call the device's character\nroutine.","comment":"Into the routine"},
        "10071": {"synopsis":"PRINTER's device pseudo-descriptor (ROM form): XX_NEXT $67BC (TAPE's XX_SIZE, a page-1\naddress), XX_RAM -2, DD_TYPE 0, DD_IRQFLAG 0 (no interrupt routine), DD_FLAGS 0, DD_TAB\n$6769 segment 0 (PRN_ENTRIES), DD_UNIT_COUNT 0, name \"PRINTER\" (its last letter is the first\nbyte of PRN_ENTRIES), XX_SIZE 15 at $276A. The device chain word at $0008 points at XX_SIZE."},
        "10089": {"synopsis":"PRINTER's entry table (addresses as run in page 3), in the order interrupt, open, create,\nclose, destroy, read character, read block, write character, write block (the shared block\nwriter at PRN_WRITE_BLOCK with PRN_WRITE_CHAR), read status, set status, special function,\ninitialise,\nbuffer moved. DD_IRQFLAG is 0, so the interrupt word is never used: it overlaps the name's\nlast letter \"R\" and XX_SIZE. Open and create share PRN_OPEN, close and destroy PRN_CLOSE;\nthe reads and the status calls go to DEV_NOFN (.NOFN, not supported)."},
        "10117": {"synopsis":"PRINTER, special function (entry +11): not supported.\nExit: A = $EA (.ISPEC).","comment":"Error $EA: .ISPEC"},
        "10120": {"synopsis":"PRINTER, open and create channel (entries +1, +2): asks EXOS 27 for a channel buffer of 0\nbytes; the printer keeps no data of its own.\nExit: A = EXOS 27's status.","comment":"Size 0: no buffer needed"},
        "10123": {"comment":"Allocate the channel buffer"},
        "10126": {"synopsis":"PRINTER, write character (entry +7): puts B on the printer's data port, waits until the\nprinter is ready, then pulses the strobe (port B5h bit 4) with the other bits of PORTB5\nkept. The wait gives up when FLAG_SOFT_IRQ holds ?STOP ($20). Falls into PRN_CLOSE for the A\n= 0 exit.\nEntry: B = the character.\nExit: A = 0, or $E5 (.STOP) if STOP was pressed while waiting.","comment":"The character"},
        "10127": {"comment":"Printer data port"},
        "10129": {"synopsis":"Loop until the printer is ready, or STOP is pressed.","comment":"FLAG_SOFT_IRQ"},
        "10132": {"comment":"?STOP soft interrupt pending?"},
        "10134": {"comment":"Error $E5: .STOP"},
        "10137": {"comment":"Printer status"},
        "10139": {"comment":"Not ready yet? (bit 3 = 0 when ready)"},
        "10141": {"comment":"Wait on"},
        "10143": {"comment":"PORTB5, the port's current value"},
        "10146": {"comment":"Strobe bit up"},
        "10148": {"comment":"Strobe on"},
        "10150": {"comment":"Strobe bit down again"},
        "10152": {"comment":"Strobe off"},
        "10154": {"synopsis":"PRINTER, close and destroy channel (entries +3, +4), and the A = 0 exit of PRN_WRITE_CHAR:\nnothing to release.\nExit: A = 0.","comment":"Status 0"},
        "10155": {"synopsis":"PRINTER, initialise and buffer moved (entries +12, +13): nothing to do; A is returned\nunchanged."},
        "10156": {"synopsis":"TAPE's device pseudo-descriptor (ROM form): XX_NEXT $6DA6 (SERIAL's XX_SIZE, a page-1\naddress), XX_RAM -2, DD_TYPE 0, DD_IRQFLAG 0 (no interrupt routine), DD_FLAGS 0, DD_TAB\n$67BB segment 0 (TAPE_ENTRIES), DD_UNIT_COUNT 0, name \"TAPE\" (its last letter is the first\nbyte of TAPE_ENTRIES), XX_SIZE 12 at $27BC."},
        "10171": {"synopsis":"TAPE's entry table (addresses as run in page 3), in the order interrupt, open, create,\nclose, destroy, read character, read block, write character, write block, read status, set\nstatus (DEV_NOFN: .NOFN, not supported), special function, initialise, buffer moved.\nDD_IRQFLAG\nis 0, so the interrupt word is never used: it overlaps the name's last letter \"E\" and\nXX_SIZE. Close and destroy share TAPE_CLOSE."},
        "10199": {"synopsis":"TAPE, special function (entry +11): not supported.\nExit: A = $EA (.ISPEC).","comment":"Error $EA: .ISPEC"},
        "10202": {"synopsis":"TAPE, open channel (entry +1): opens the one read channel and finds its file's header chunk.\n1. TAPE_NEW_CHANNEL refuses a second read channel (.2NDCH), keeps the unit (the remote) at\n   $B291 and the wanted name at $B292, and asks for a 4K channel buffer.\n2. Shows \"SEARCHING\" on the status line, then reads chunks with TAPE_READ_CHUNK until one is\n   a header ($B2D6 nonzero) read without a CRC error.\n3. Shows \"FOUND\" and the header's name; if a name was asked for and it differs, it searches\n   on (the found name stays on screen). A match shows \"LOADING\" and the name.\n4. Keeps the header's protection byte at $B2D8; a protected file (byte 0) cannot be opened\n   while a write channel is open: .PROT.\nEntry: A = the channel number, C = the unit, DE = the file name (length byte first), IX =\nthe channel RAM.\nExit: A = 0 with $B2D5 = 0 (data chunks follow); or an error: .2NDCH, EXOS 27's, .PROT,\n.STOP.","comment":"Keep the channel number"},
        "10203": {"comment":"The read channel, if one is open"},
        "10206": {"comment":"Where the unit and name go"},
        "10209": {"comment":"Refuse a second one; keep unit and name"},
        "10212": {"comment":"Error: .2NDCH or no buffer"},
        "10213": {"comment":"The channel number"},
        "10214": {"comment":"It is now the read channel"},
        "10217": {"comment":"\"SEARCHING\""},
        "10220": {"comment":"Status line: clear it, show the text"},
        "10223": {"synopsis":"Read the next chunk: back here until a good header with the wanted name comes.","comment":"No CRC error yet"},
        "10227": {"comment":"$FF"},
        "10228": {"comment":"No data chunk expected yet"},
        "10231": {"comment":"Read a chunk into the buffer"},
        "10234": {"comment":"STOP pressed: return its error"},
        "10236": {"comment":"A header chunk?"},
        "10240": {"comment":"No: a data chunk, search on"},
        "10242": {"comment":"Read with a CRC error?"},
        "10246": {"comment":"Yes: search on"},
        "10248": {"comment":"\"FOUND\", kept in HL' for a name mismatch"},
        "10252": {"comment":"11 characters"},
        "10255": {"comment":"Blank the status line's text"},
        "10258": {"comment":"The buffer's top: the header, downward"},
        "10261": {"comment":"Kept for the name copy"},
        "10262": {"comment":"The wanted name: length byte first"},
        "10265": {"comment":"Its length"},
        "10267": {"comment":"No name asked for: take any file"},
        "10269": {"comment":"Compare the length byte and the letters"},
        "10271": {"synopsis":"Loop: compare the wanted name with the header's, from the length byte on (the header runs\ndownward).","comment":"Next header byte"},
        "10273": {"comment":"Same?"},
        "10274": {"comment":"No: show \"FOUND\" and search on"},
        "10279": {"synopsis":"The name matches (or none was asked for): \"LOADING\" goes in HL.","comment":"\"LOADING\""},
        "10282": {"comment":"Into the other set: undone at TAPE_SHOW_FOUND"},
        "10283": {"synopsis":"Shows \"LOADING\" (a match: the two EXX cancel) or \"FOUND\" (a mismatch: HL' was \"FOUND\") with\nthe header's name after it, then searches on after a mismatch.","comment":"HL = the text to show"},
        "10284": {"comment":"Keep the compare's Z flag"},
        "10285": {"comment":"Status line: clear it, show the text"},
        "10288": {"comment":"The header's top"},
        "10290": {"comment":"Its name's length byte"},
        "10291": {"comment":"One space after the text"},
        "10292": {"comment":"Show the header's name"},
        "10295": {"comment":"The compare's result"},
        "10296": {"comment":"The header's protection byte"},
        "10297": {"comment":"Another name: search on"},
        "10299": {"comment":"A = 0 here: take the protection byte"},
        "10300": {"comment":"Keep it: 0 = protected"},
        "10303": {"comment":"Not protected: open"},
        "10305": {"comment":"A write channel open?"},
        "10309": {"comment":"No: open"},
        "10311": {"comment":"No data to read"},
        "10316": {"comment":"Error $E3: .PROT"},
        "10320": {"synopsis":"The file is opened: data chunks follow.","comment":"Status 0"},
        "10321": {"comment":"More chunks to read"},
        "10324": {"synopsis":"Open's exit: the buffer counts as empty and the CRC error flag is cleared; A is the status.","comment":"Keep the status"},
        "10328": {"comment":"No bytes in the buffer (the header is not data)"},
        "10331": {"comment":"CRC error flag cleared"},
        "10336": {"synopsis":"TAPE, create channel (entry +2): opens the one write channel and records its header chunk.\n1. Refuses while the open read file is protected ($B2D8 = 0): .PROT. TAPE_NEW_CHANNEL\n   refuses a second write channel (.2NDCH), keeps the unit at $B2AF and the name at $B2B0,\n   and asks for a 4K buffer.\n2. Takes the four tone-channel codes of the speed SP_TAPE asks for (fast TAPE_HALF_FAST or\n   slow\n   TAPE_HALF_SLOW) into $B2DD-$B2E0, and the output level from LV_TAPE into $B2DC (levels 0\nand 1\n   give 1; 2 to 6 give 3, 7, 15, 31 and 63; 7 and above give 63).\n3. Shows \"SAVING\" and the name on the status line, builds the header in the buffer\n   (PROTECT's value, then the name with its length byte, downward) and writes it as a header\n   chunk through TAPE_WR_BLOCK.\nEntry: A = the channel number, C = the unit, DE = the file name, IX = the channel RAM.\nExit: carry set and A = 0 when the header was written; else A = the error (.PROT, .2NDCH,\nEXOS 27's, or .STOP, with $B2D7 = $FF: the channel is dead).","comment":"Keep the channel number"},
        "10337": {"comment":"The open read file's protection byte"},
        "10341": {"comment":"Error $E3: .PROT"},
        "10343": {"comment":"Protected: refuse"},
        "10344": {"comment":"The write channel, if one is open"},
        "10347": {"comment":"Where the unit and name go"},
        "10350": {"comment":"Refuse a second one; keep unit and name"},
        "10353": {"comment":"Error: .2NDCH or no buffer"},
        "10355": {"comment":"It is now the write channel"},
        "10358": {"comment":"The fast codes"},
        "10361": {"comment":"SP_TAPE (EXOS variable 33)"},
        "10365": {"comment":"0: fast"},
        "10367": {"comment":"Nonzero: the slow codes"},
        "10370": {"synopsis":"Copies the speed's four tone-channel 0 codes (lead-in, 1 bit, 0 bit, sync) to $B2DD-$B2E0,\nthen turns LV_TAPE into the D/A level at $B2DC.","comment":"Lead-in, 1, 0, sync"},
        "10378": {"comment":"LV_TAPE (EXOS variable 35)"},
        "10382": {"comment":"Not 0?"},
        "10384": {"comment":"0 counts as 1"},
        "10385": {"synopsis":"Turns the level number (1-255) into a D/A amplitude: 2^n - 1, at most $3F.","comment":"7 or more?"},
        "10387": {"comment":"B = shifts"},
        "10388": {"comment":"The highest level"},
        "10390": {"comment":"Yes: take it"},
        "10393": {"comment":"Shift ones in"},
        "10394": {"synopsis":"Loop: shift a 1 in, n times."},
        "10397": {"synopsis":"Keep the amplitude.","comment":"D/A level for a high half-cycle"},
        "10400": {"comment":"Channel alive (not stopped)"},
        "10404": {"comment":"\"SAVING\""},
        "10407": {"comment":"Status line: clear it, show the text"},
        "10410": {"comment":"One space after it"},
        "10411": {"comment":"Kept: where the name goes on screen"},
        "10412": {"comment":"The buffer's top (IX)"},
        "10415": {"comment":"First header byte below it"},
        "10416": {"comment":"PROTECT (EXOS variable 34)"},
        "10419": {"comment":"Header byte 0: protection"},
        "10420": {"comment":"Then the name"},
        "10421": {"comment":"Kept: the header's name, for the screen"},
        "10422": {"comment":"The name: length byte first"},
        "10426": {"comment":"Length + 1 bytes to copy"},
        "10429": {"comment":"C = length + 2: the header's size"},
        "10430": {"synopsis":"Loop: copy the length byte and the name into the buffer, downward."},
        "10431": {"comment":"Into the header"},
        "10436": {"comment":"Bytes in the buffer: the header's (B = 0)"},
        "10440": {"comment":"The header's name"},
        "10441": {"comment":"The status line after \"SAVING \""},
        "10442": {"comment":"Show the name"},
        "10445": {"comment":"$FF: a header chunk"},
        "10447": {"comment":"Write the chunk"},
        "10450": {"comment":"Written: done"},
        "10451": {"comment":"STOP: the channel is dead"},
        "10454": {"comment":"$FF"},
        "10456": {"synopsis":"Common start of open and create: refuses a second channel of the kind, keeps its remote and\nname, clears the status line and asks EXOS 27 for a 4K buffer (one chunk).\nEntry: A = that kind's channel number ($B28F or $B290: 0 when none is open), C = the unit,\nDE = the name (length byte first), HL = the remote byte (the name follows it).\nExit: A = 0 or the error, NZ on an error ($E9 .2NDCH, or EXOS 27's).","comment":"One already open?"},
        "10457": {"comment":"Error $E9: .2NDCH"},
        "10460": {"comment":"Unit 1?"},
        "10461": {"comment":"Yes: 0, REM1"},
        "10463": {"comment":"Else the unit as it is"},
        "10464": {"synopsis":"Keep the remote (0 = REM1, else REM2) and copy the name.","comment":"The remote: 0 for units 0 and 1"},
        "10465": {"comment":"The name goes after it"},
        "10467": {"comment":"Its length"},
        "10468": {"comment":"With the length byte"},
        "10471": {"comment":"Keep the name"},
        "10473": {"comment":"Clear the status line's text"},
        "10476": {"comment":"4K: one chunk"},
        "10479": {"comment":"Allocate the channel buffer"},
        "10482": {"synopsis":"TAPE, close and destroy channel (entries +3, +4). For the read channel it forgets the\nchannel and clears the protection flag ($B2D8 = $FF). For the write channel it writes what\nis in the buffer as the last data chunk (even an empty one: the end of the file), unless\nSTOP killed the channel ($B2D7 nonzero), and forgets it. Both clear the status line's text.\nEntry: A = the channel number.\nExit: A = 0.","comment":"The read channel?"},
        "10485": {"comment":"Flags kept"},
        "10487": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "10489": {"comment":"The write channel stopped?"},
        "10493": {"comment":"No: write the last chunk (A = 0: data)"},
        "10496": {"comment":"No write channel now"},
        "10502": {"synopsis":"The read channel: forget it; a new file is not protected.","comment":"No read channel now"},
        "10505": {"comment":"$FF"},
        "10506": {"comment":"No protected file open"},
        "10509": {"synopsis":"Clear the status line's text; A = 0."},
        "10512": {"synopsis":"TAPE, read character (entry +5): takes the next byte from the buffer; an empty buffer reads\nthe next chunk while one is due ($B2D5 = 0).\n1. After the last chunk: .EOF, but .CCRC once first if a CRC error cut the chunk short\n   ($B2D9).\n2. A header chunk where data was expected is .CCRC too.\n3. Any error ends the reading: $B2D5 = $FF, the buffer empty, the status line's text\n   cleared.\nEntry: A = the channel number.\nExit: A = 0 and B = the byte; or A = the error: .NOFN (not the read channel), .EOF, .CCRC,\n.STOP.","comment":"Not the read channel: .NOFN"},
        "10516": {"synopsis":"Returns the next byte of the buffer, or reads a chunk when it is empty. TAPE_READ_BLOCK\ncalls this for each byte.","comment":"Bytes left in the buffer"},
        "10520": {"comment":"None?"},
        "10524": {"comment":"The read pointer"},
        "10527": {"comment":"The byte"},
        "10528": {"comment":"The buffer runs downward"},
        "10532": {"comment":"One byte fewer"},
        "10537": {"comment":"Return it in B"},
        "10538": {"comment":"Status 0"},
        "10540": {"synopsis":"The buffer is empty: read the next chunk if one is due, else end the file.","comment":"Last chunk read already?"},
        "10544": {"comment":"No: read the next chunk"},
        "10547": {"comment":"The CRC error flag"},
        "10550": {"comment":"Not read (end, or STOP)"},
        "10552": {"comment":"A header?"},
        "10556": {"comment":"No: data, return its first byte"},
        "10558": {"comment":"A header: report a CRC error"},
        "10560": {"synopsis":"No chunk read: STOP (Z) returns its error; else .CCRC once after a CRC error, then .EOF.","comment":"STOP: return .STOP"},
        "10562": {"comment":"A CRC error to report?"},
        "10564": {"comment":"Error $E4: .EOF"},
        "10566": {"comment":"No: end of file"},
        "10568": {"synopsis":"Report the CRC error once: clear its flag, A = .CCRC.","comment":"Reported once"},
        "10570": {"comment":"Error $D0: .CCRC"},
        "10572": {"synopsis":"Ends the reading with the error in A: no more chunks, the buffer empty, the status line's\ntext cleared.","comment":"No more chunks"},
        "10577": {"comment":"The buffer is empty"},
        "10583": {"comment":"Keep the error"},
        "10584": {"comment":"Clear the status line's text"},
        "10589": {"synopsis":"TAPE, read block (entry +6): the shared block reader at DEV_BLOCK_READ, calling\nTAPE_NEXT_BYTE for\neach byte.\nEntry: A = the channel number, BC = the count, DE = the address.\nExit: as the block reader; .NOFN when A is not the read channel.","comment":"Not the read channel: .NOFN"},
        "10593": {"comment":"Each byte from TAPE_NEXT_BYTE"},
        "10596": {"comment":"The shared block reader"},
        "10599": {"synopsis":"TAPE, write character (entry +7): puts B in the buffer (downward) and writes the buffer as a\ndata chunk when it holds 4096 bytes.\nEntry: A = the channel number, B = the byte.\nExit: A = 0; or .NOFN (not the write channel), .EOF (the channel was stopped), .STOP (STOP\nwhile writing: the channel is then dead, $B2D7 = $FF).","comment":"Not the write channel: .NOFN"},
        "10603": {"synopsis":"Puts B in the write buffer, writing a full buffer out. TAPE_WRITE_BLOCK calls this for each\nbyte.","comment":"Channel stopped earlier?"},
        "10607": {"comment":"Error $E4: .EOF"},
        "10609": {"comment":"Yes: refuse"},
        "10610": {"comment":"The write pointer"},
        "10613": {"comment":"Store the byte"},
        "10614": {"comment":"The buffer runs downward"},
        "10618": {"comment":"Bytes in the buffer"},
        "10621": {"comment":"One more"},
        "10625": {"comment":"$1000 bytes (a full chunk)?"},
        "10629": {"comment":"Carry: success when nothing is written"},
        "10630": {"comment":"Full: write it (A = 0: data)"},
        "10633": {"comment":"Done or written: A = 0"},
        "10635": {"comment":"STOP: the channel is dead"},
        "10638": {"comment":"$FF"},
        "10640": {"synopsis":"TAPE, write block (entry +8): the shared block writer at DEV_BLOCK_WRITE, calling\nTAPE_PUT_BYTE for\neach byte.\nEntry: A = the channel number, BC = the count, DE = the address.\nExit: as the block writer; .NOFN when A is not the write channel.","comment":"Not the write channel: .NOFN"},
        "10644": {"comment":"Each byte to TAPE_PUT_BYTE"},
        "10647": {"comment":"The shared block writer"},
        "10650": {"synopsis":"TAPE, read status (entry +9), for the read channel only: C = 0 while the buffer holds bytes,\nelse $B2D5 (0: a chunk is still to come, $FF: the end).\nEntry: A = the channel number.\nExit: A = 0 and C; or .NOFN for another channel.","comment":"Not the read channel: .NOFN"},
        "10654": {"comment":"Bytes left in the buffer?"},
        "10659": {"comment":"0: a byte is ready"},
        "10663": {"comment":"Else 0 or $FF: chunk to come or end"},
        "10667": {"synopsis":"Shared exit: A = 0."},
        "10669": {"synopsis":"TAPE, buffer moved (entry +13): moves the read pointer ($B2D1) of the read channel, or the\nwrite pointer ($B2D3) of any other, by the offset, through the shared pointer adjusters at\nADJ_PTR and ADJ_PTR_2.\nEntry: A = the channel number, BC = the offset.","comment":"The read channel?"},
        "10672": {"comment":"Its read pointer"},
        "10675": {"comment":"Yes: adjust it"},
        "10678": {"comment":"Z for ADJ_PTR_2"},
        "10679": {"comment":"Two bytes on: the write pointer"},
        "10682": {"synopsis":"Turns both remote relays off (REM1 and REM2 = $FF) through TAPE_SET_REMOTE.","comment":"REM1"},
        "10683": {"comment":"$FF: off"},
        "10685": {"comment":"REM1 off"},
        "10688": {"comment":"A = $FF: REM2, falls through"},
        "10689": {"synopsis":"Switches a remote relay: sets or clears its bit of port B5h (bit 6 REM1, bit 7 REM2), keeps\nPORTB5, and writes the value into the EXOS variable (REM1 = 36 at $BFE9, REM2 = 37 at\n$BFEA). TAPE_INIT puts its address at $BFC3, where segment 0's VAR_SET_REMOTE calls it when\na program writes REM1 or REM2.\nEntry: A = 0 for REM1, else REM2; D = 0 for on (the motor runs), else off.\nChanges: A, BC, E, L.","comment":"Bit 6: REM1"},
        "10691": {"comment":"REM1 (EXOS variable 36)"},
        "10694": {"comment":"Which remote?"},
        "10695": {"comment":"REM1"},
        "10697": {"comment":"REM2 (EXOS variable 37)"},
        "10698": {"comment":"Bit 7: REM2"},
        "10699": {"synopsis":"Sets the relay's bit, clears it again for off.","comment":"E = on or off"},
        "10701": {"comment":"PORTB5"},
        "10704": {"comment":"The relay's bit on"},
        "10705": {"comment":"Off?"},
        "10709": {"comment":"Yes: bit off"},
        "10710": {"synopsis":"Writes the port and the variables.","comment":"Relays and the keyboard row"},
        "10712": {"comment":"Kept in PORTB5"},
        "10715": {"comment":"The new value"},
        "10716": {"comment":"Into REM1 or REM2"},
        "10719": {"synopsis":"TAPE, initialise (entry +12): puts TAPE_SET_REMOTE's address at $BFC3 for segment 0's\nREM1/REM2 handling, clears the tape's 86 bytes of variables $B28D-$B2E2, marks no protected\nfile open ($B2D8 = $FF) and turns both relays off.","comment":"Segment 0 calls it for REM1/REM2 writes"},
        "10725": {"comment":"Clear $B28D-$B2E2"},
        "10738": {"comment":"$FF"},
        "10739": {"comment":"No protected file open"},
        "10742": {"comment":"Both relays off"},
        "10745": {"synopsis":"Clears the status line's text, then shows a message there (TAPE_SHOW_TEXT).\nEntry: HL = the message's length byte.\nExit: DE = the position after the message.","comment":"Keep the message"},
        "10746": {"comment":"Clear the status line's text"},
        "10750": {"synopsis":"Shows a message at the status line's text position $BEBE (TAPE_COPY_TEXT).","comment":"The status line's text"},
        "10753": {"synopsis":"Copies a message stored backward to DE: HL points at its length byte (at most 17 are copied)\nand the letters run downward in front of it, so the copy reads forward.\nEntry: HL = the length byte, DE = the destination.\nExit: DE past the copy, HL below the message; Z and A = 0 for an empty one.\nChanges: A, B, DE, HL.","comment":"Its length"},
        "10754": {"comment":"At most 17"},
        "10756": {"comment":"17 or more?"},
        "10759": {"comment":"Empty?"},
        "10760": {"comment":"Yes: nothing to copy"},
        "10761": {"comment":"Copy all of it"},
        "10762": {"synopsis":"Start at the letter in front of the length byte (B = the count).","comment":"The last letter first"},
        "10763": {"synopsis":"Loop: copy the letters, reading downward."},
        "10764": {"comment":"Into the destination, forward"},
        "10770": {"synopsis":"Fills the status line's text from $BEBE with 31 spaces (TAPE_CLEAR_N).\nExit: A = 0.","comment":"31 places"},
        "10773": {"synopsis":"Fills BC + 1 places of the status line from $BEBE with spaces.\nEntry: BC = the count less one.\nExit: A = 0.","comment":"Space"},
        "10775": {"comment":"The status line's text"},
        "10781": {"comment":"First one, then copied on"},
        "10784": {"comment":"Status 0"},
        "10786": {"synopsis":"Status-line messages of the TAPE device, each stored backward with its length byte after it\n(the code points at the length byte): \"LOADING\", \"SAVING\", \"SEARCHING\", \"FOUND\", five\nspaces, \"PAUSE\" (bit 7 set on each letter) and the level meter (a space, $9F $9F $A0 $A0).\nThis entry: the letters of \"LOADING\"."},
        "10793": {"synopsis":"The length byte of \"LOADING\" (7); the code points HL here and TAPE_COPY_TEXT copies the\nletters in front of it.","comment":"\"LOADING\": 7 letters"},
        "10794": {"synopsis":"The letters of \"SAVING\", stored backward (last letter first) in front of the length byte\nTXT_SAVING."},
        "10800": {"synopsis":"The length byte of \"SAVING\" (6); the code points HL here and TAPE_COPY_TEXT copies the\nletters in front of it.","comment":"\"SAVING\": 6 letters"},
        "10801": {"synopsis":"The letters of \"SEARCHING\", stored backward (last letter first) in front of the length byte\nTXT_SEARCHING."},
        "10810": {"synopsis":"The length byte of \"SEARCHING\" (9); the code points HL here and TAPE_COPY_TEXT copies the\nletters in front of it.","comment":"\"SEARCHING\": 9 letters"},
        "10811": {"synopsis":"The letters of \"FOUND\", stored backward (last letter first) in front of the length byte\nTXT_FOUND."},
        "10816": {"synopsis":"The length byte of \"FOUND\" (5); the code points HL here and TAPE_COPY_TEXT copies the\nletters in front of it.","comment":"\"FOUND\": 5 letters"},
        "10817": {"synopsis":"The letters of five spaces, stored backward (last letter first) in front of the length byte\nTXT_BLANK5."},
        "10822": {"synopsis":"The length byte of five spaces (5); the code points HL here and TAPE_COPY_TEXT copies the\nletters in front of it.","comment":"5 spaces: blanks the meter's place"},
        "10823": {"synopsis":"The letters of \"PAUSE\" with bit 7 set on every letter, stored backward (last letter first)\nin front of the length byte TXT_PAUSE."},
        "10828": {"synopsis":"The length byte of \"PAUSE\" with bit 7 set on every letter (5); the code points HL here and\nTAPE_COPY_TEXT copies the letters in front of it.","comment":"\"PAUSE\": 5 letters"},
        "10829": {"synopsis":"The letters of the level meter: a space, two $9F and two $A0 characters, stored backward\n(last letter first) in front of the length byte TXT_METER."},
        "10834": {"synopsis":"The length byte of the level meter: a space, two $9F and two $A0 characters (5); the code\npoints HL here and TAPE_COPY_TEXT copies the letters in front of it.","comment":"The meter: 5 characters"},
        "10835": {"synopsis":"Is A the read channel? Compares A with $B28F.\nEntry: A = a channel number.\nExit: Z when it is; A = $E7 (.NOFN) either way.","comment":"The read channel's number"},
        "10840": {"synopsis":"Is A the write channel? Compares A with $B290.\nExit: Z when it is; A = $E7 (.NOFN) either way.","comment":"The write channel's number"},
        "10843": {"synopsis":"Compare A with the channel number at HL; A = .NOFN.","comment":"This channel?"},
        "10844": {"comment":"Error $E7: .NOFN, flags kept"},
        "10847": {"synopsis":"Reads one chunk from tape into the channel buffer (downward from IX - 1), with interrupts\noff and the motor of the read channel's relay running.\n1. Keeps SP at $B2DA (a STOP returns from here through it), shows the level meter at $BED8\n   and starts the tape (TAPE_IO_BEGIN: relay on, RST 38h made a RET, keyboard row 7 selected\nfor\n   STOP). Keeps the status line's palette colours 2 and 3 (from LP_POINTER + 10) at $B2E1;\n   the cycle timers flash them with the input level.\n2. Lead-in (TAPE_FIND_LEADIN): averages 32 cycles, then wants 1024 cycles each within 2 of\n   the average; their average is the bit threshold (a cycle shorter than it is a 1 bit). The\n   speed is found from the tape this way.\n3. The sync (TAPE_FIND_SYNC): half-cycles are timed until one is at least 4 longer than the\n   lead-in's; a shorter-than-expected one restarts the search. Then a byte that is not used,\n   and $6A, else the search restarts.\n4. The block count: 0 an empty chunk, $FF a header ($B2D6 = $FF, one block), else data; a\n   count other than 16 is the file's last chunk ($B2D5 = $FF).\n5. Each block: its byte count (0 = 256; a short block also ends the file), the bytes, and a\n   CRC-16 checked against the one computed while reading (TAPE_READ_BYTE). A bad CRC sets\n   $B2D9 = $FF and keeps only the whole blocks before it, and ends the file.\n6. $B2CD = the bytes read, the read pointer $B2D1 at the buffer's top; the status line shows\n   \"PAUSE\" while chunks are to come, blanks the meter otherwise, and gets its colours back;\n   TAPE_IO_END stops the tape.\nEntry: IX = the buffer's top + 1, $B291 = the relay.\nExit: carry set and A = 0; or (STOP) A = $E5 (.STOP), Z, carry clear.","comment":"STOP returns to the caller through this"},
        "10851": {"comment":"The level meter"},
        "10854": {"comment":"Its place on the status line"},
        "10857": {"comment":"Show it"},
        "10860": {"comment":"The read channel's relay"},
        "10863": {"comment":"Tape on: relay, RET at $0038, row 7"},
        "10866": {"comment":"No bytes read yet"},
        "10870": {"comment":"Kept: the buffer's top"},
        "10872": {"comment":"The bytes go downward from IX - 1"},
        "10874": {"comment":"The read pointer"},
        "10878": {"comment":"LP_POINTER: the status line's LPB"},
        "10881": {"comment":"+11: palette colour 3"},
        "10885": {"comment":"Colours 2 and 3"},
        "10888": {"comment":"Kept, to put back at the end"},
        "10892": {"comment":"DE = their address, kept in DE'"},
        "10894": {"comment":"Tone channel 0's code, high bits 0"},
        "10895": {"comment":"Channel 0 code high"},
        "10897": {"synopsis":"Looks for the lead-in, and starts over when a cycle breaks it: averages 32 cycles, then\nwants 1024 cycles each within 2 of that average while it sums their lengths (in HL' and B')."},
        "10898": {"comment":"HL':B' = the sum of the lengths"},
        "10904": {"comment":"Code 45: the timing step for cycles"},
        "10906": {"comment":"Channel 0 code low"},
        "10908": {"comment":"Time to the end of a cycle (an edge)"},
        "10911": {"comment":"Sum of 32 lengths"},
        "10914": {"comment":"32 cycles"},
        "10916": {"comment":"D = 0: DE = the length"},
        "10917": {"synopsis":"Loop: sum 32 cycle lengths.","comment":"Time one cycle: A = E = its length"},
        "10920": {"comment":"Add it"},
        "10923": {"comment":"Times 8: H = sum / 32"},
        "10926": {"comment":"The average"},
        "10927": {"comment":"Rounded by the next bit"},
        "10930": {"comment":"D = the average cycle"},
        "10931": {"comment":"1024 cycles to check"},
        "10934": {"synopsis":"Loop: 1024 cycles each within 2 of the average, their lengths summed into HL':B'.","comment":"Time one cycle"},
        "10938": {"comment":"Add the length to HL':B'"},
        "10940": {"comment":"Carry into HL'"},
        "10943": {"synopsis":"How far is this cycle from the average?"},
        "10944": {"comment":"The length"},
        "10945": {"comment":"Minus the average"},
        "10946": {"comment":"Not below?"},
        "10948": {"comment":"The size of the difference"},
        "10950": {"synopsis":"Within 2? Else the search starts over.","comment":"3 or more off?"},
        "10952": {"comment":"Yes: not a lead-in, start over"},
        "10954": {"comment":"One cycle fewer to check"},
        "10957": {"comment":"More to check"},
        "10960": {"comment":"Times 64: H' = the sum / 1024"},
        "10966": {"comment":"The average lead-in cycle"},
        "10967": {"comment":"Rounded by the next bit"},
        "10972": {"comment":"Kept: the threshold between 1 and 0 bits"},
        "10973": {"comment":"Code 30: the timing step for halves"},
        "10975": {"comment":"Channel 0 code low"},
        "10977": {"comment":"To the end of this cycle"},
        "10980": {"comment":"Two sums of half-cycles, one per phase"},
        "10984": {"comment":"B = 0: 256 halves"},
        "10985": {"comment":"D = 0"},
        "10986": {"synopsis":"Loop: time 256 half-cycles, summing them (twice each) into two sums, one per phase, swapped\nthrough the stack.","comment":"The other phase's sum"},
        "10987": {"comment":"Time a half-cycle: E = its length"},
        "10990": {"comment":"Add it twice"},
        "10994": {"comment":"One phase's average half"},
        "10995": {"comment":"Rounded"},
        "10998": {"comment":"Kept in D"},
        "10999": {"comment":"The other phase's sum"},
        "11000": {"comment":"Its average half"},
        "11001": {"comment":"Rounded"},
        "11004": {"comment":"H and L: the two phases' averages"},
        "11006": {"comment":"D = the bit threshold"},
        "11007": {"comment":"Time the next half-cycle"},
        "11010": {"synopsis":"Loop: time half-cycles, each against its phase's average, until one is at least 4 longer\n(the sync); one more than 2 shorter restarts the lead-in search.","comment":"The other phase's average"},
        "11013": {"comment":"Time a half-cycle"},
        "11016": {"comment":"Longer than this phase's average?"},
        "11017": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "11019": {"comment":"Up to 2 shorter?"},
        "11021": {"comment":"Yes: still lead-in"},
        "11023": {"comment":"Much shorter: start over"},
        "11026": {"synopsis":"A longer half-cycle: by 4 or more it is the sync.","comment":"Less than 4 longer?"},
        "11028": {"comment":"Yes: still lead-in"},
        "11030": {"comment":"Code 45 again: cycle timing"},
        "11032": {"comment":"Channel 0 code low"},
        "11034": {"comment":"The sync's other half"},
        "11037": {"comment":"The byte that is not used"},
        "11040": {"comment":"The next byte"},
        "11043": {"comment":"$6A?"},
        "11045": {"comment":"No: a false sync, start over"},
        "11048": {"comment":"One block for a header"},
        "11050": {"comment":"The block count"},
        "11053": {"comment":"0?"},
        "11054": {"comment":"Yes: an empty chunk"},
        "11056": {"comment":"The end-of-file flag"},
        "11059": {"comment":"$FF: a header?"},
        "11061": {"comment":"Yes: one block"},
        "11063": {"comment":"B = the blocks"},
        "11064": {"comment":"A full chunk (16 blocks)?"},
        "11066": {"comment":"Yes: more may follow"},
        "11068": {"comment":"Fewer: this is the last chunk"},
        "11070": {"synopsis":"A data chunk: $B2D6 = 0.","comment":"0: data"},
        "11071": {"synopsis":"Keeps the chunk's kind at $B2D6 ($FF a header, 0 data).","comment":"$B2D6"},
        "11072": {"comment":"The chunk's kind"},
        "11073": {"synopsis":"Loop per block: its byte count, the bytes into the buffer downward, the CRC check.","comment":"Keep the block count"},
        "11074": {"comment":"The block's byte count"},
        "11077": {"comment":"0: 256 bytes"},
        "11078": {"comment":"B = the count"},
        "11079": {"comment":"256: not the end"},
        "11081": {"comment":"A short block: the file's last"},
        "11086": {"synopsis":"Start the block's CRC from 0."},
        "11087": {"comment":"CRC = 0"},
        "11091": {"synopsis":"Loop: read the block's bytes into the buffer, downward.","comment":"Read a byte"},
        "11094": {"comment":"Into the buffer"},
        "11097": {"comment":"Downward"},
        "11099": {"comment":"One more byte read"},
        "11103": {"comment":"The CRC computed over the data"},
        "11106": {"comment":"The CRC's low byte, read"},
        "11109": {"comment":"Clear the carry for the compare"},
        "11110": {"comment":"Kept with A"},
        "11111": {"comment":"The computed CRC"},
        "11112": {"comment":"BC = it"},
        "11113": {"comment":"The CRC's high byte, read"},
        "11117": {"comment":"HL = the CRC read"},
        "11120": {"comment":"Same as the computed one?"},
        "11122": {"comment":"The block count"},
        "11123": {"comment":"No: a CRC error"},
        "11125": {"comment":"Next block"},
        "11127": {"comment":"All read"},
        "11129": {"synopsis":"A CRC error: flag it, keep only the whole blocks before this one, and end the file.","comment":"$FF"},
        "11131": {"comment":"CRC error flag"},
        "11134": {"comment":"The bytes read"},
        "11137": {"comment":"Minus one"},
        "11138": {"comment":"Rounded down to whole blocks"},
        "11143": {"synopsis":"No more chunks after this one.","comment":"$FF"},
        "11145": {"comment":"The end of the file"},
        "11148": {"synopsis":"Keeps the byte count, puts the message and the colours back, stops the tape.","comment":"Bytes in the buffer"},
        "11152": {"comment":"The buffer's top again"},
        "11154": {"comment":"\"PAUSE\" or a blank, colours back"},
        "11157": {"comment":"Tape off; A = 0, carry set"},
        "11160": {"synopsis":"Shows \"PAUSE\" in the meter's place while chunks are to come ($B2D5 = 0, or a header was just\nread), five spaces otherwise, then puts the status line's palette colours 2 and 3 back from\n$B2E1 (DE' holds their address).","comment":"\"PAUSE\""},
        "11163": {"comment":"More chunks to come?"},
        "11167": {"comment":"Yes: \"PAUSE\""},
        "11169": {"comment":"A header just read?"},
        "11173": {"comment":"Yes: \"PAUSE\""},
        "11175": {"synopsis":"Blanks the meter's place and puts the palette colours back. The tape's STOP exit at\nTAPE_READ_STOP\ncomes here too.","comment":"Five spaces"},
        "11178": {"synopsis":"Shows the text at the meter's place, then puts the colours back.","comment":"The meter's place"},
        "11181": {"comment":"Show it"},
        "11184": {"comment":"DE = the colours' address"},
        "11185": {"comment":"The colours as they were"},
        "11189": {"comment":"Colour 2 back"},
        "11191": {"comment":"Colour 3 back"},
        "11193": {"synopsis":"Reads a byte from tape, least significant bit first: each bit is one cycle, a 1 when it is\nshorter than D (the lead-in cycle), and goes into the CRC in HL' (CRC_ADD_BIT).\nEntry: D = the threshold.\nExit: A = the byte.\nChanges: A, E, H, HL'.","comment":"Marker bit: 8 bits when it comes out"},
        "11195": {"synopsis":"Loop: time a cycle per bit.","comment":"Time a cycle: A = its length"},
        "11198": {"comment":"Shorter than the threshold: a 1"},
        "11199": {"comment":"Keep the bit in the carry"},
        "11200": {"comment":"$FF for a 1, 0 for a 0"},
        "11201": {"comment":"Into the CRC"},
        "11205": {"comment":"The bit in from the left"},
        "11207": {"comment":"Until the marker comes out"},
        "11209": {"comment":"The byte"},
        "11211": {"synopsis":"Times a half-cycle: waits for tone channel 0's next interrupt, then counts polls until the\ninput (port B6h bit 7) leaves the level it had at the start. Updates the level meter first\n(TAPE_LEVEL_SHOW).\nExit: A = E = the count; C = the input's level when the half started (bit 7 inverted).\nChanges: A, C, E, HL' kept.","comment":"Level meter colours"},
        "11214": {"comment":"Tape input"},
        "11216": {"comment":"C = the other level"},
        "11219": {"comment":"Count from 0"},
        "11221": {"comment":"Wait for channel 0's interrupt"},
        "11223": {"comment":"Count until the level changes"},
        "11225": {"synopsis":"Times a cycle: waits for tone channel 0's next interrupt, then counts polls while the input\n(port B6h bit 7) has C's level and then while it has the other one (TAPE_MEASURE).\nEntry: C = the level kept by TAPE_HALF_CYCLE.\nExit: A = E = the count.","comment":"Level meter colours"},
        "11228": {"comment":"Count from 0"},
        "11230": {"comment":"Wait for channel 0's interrupt"},
        "11232": {"synopsis":"Counts polls of the tape input in E: first while bit 7 of port B6h equals bit 7 of C, then\nwhile it differs. Each poll also tests the STOP key (row 7, bit 0) and leaves through\nTAPE_READ_STOP.\nBetween the halves tone channel 0 is held (A7h = $4F), and released at the end ($2BFE).","comment":"Keyboard row 7"},
        "11234": {"comment":"Bit 0: the STOP key"},
        "11235": {"comment":"Down: stop the tape, .STOP"},
        "11238": {"comment":"Count"},
        "11239": {"comment":"Tape input, bit 7 the data"},
        "11241": {"comment":"Against C's level"},
        "11242": {"comment":"Still C's level?"},
        "11245": {"synopsis":"The level changed: hold tone channel 0, then count the second part.","comment":"Tones held, left D/A, interrupt from tone 0"},
        "11247": {"comment":"Sync, D/A and interrupt control"},
        "11249": {"synopsis":"Loop: count while the input differs from C's level, testing STOP.","comment":"Keyboard row 7"},
        "11251": {"comment":"Bit 0: the STOP key"},
        "11252": {"comment":"Down: stop the tape, .STOP"},
        "11255": {"comment":"Count"},
        "11256": {"comment":"Tape input"},
        "11258": {"comment":"Against C's level"},
        "11259": {"comment":"Still the other level?"},
        "11262": {"comment":"Channel 0 counts again from this edge (sync off)"},
        "11266": {"comment":"Timing"},
        "11269": {"comment":"Reset the tone interrupt latch, keep it enabled"},
        "11273": {"comment":"A = loops counted over the cycle"},
        "11275": {"synopsis":"Marks the tape input in palette colours 2 and 3 of the status line's line parameter block (DE' =\nLP_POINTER + 10, set at $2A7E; $2BB0 puts back the two bytes kept at $B2E1): $00, $92\nwhile the level comparator (port $B6 bit 6) sees no signal, $49, $00 while it does.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"DE' = LP_POINTER + 10"},
        "11276": {"comment":"Level comparator: 1 with no signal"},
        "11282": {"comment":"No signal: $00, $92"},
        "11288": {"synopsis":"A signal: $49, $00 (the LD A,$00 before is overwritten at once)."},
        "11290": {"comment":"Signal: $49, $00"},
        "11294": {"synopsis":"Writes the second byte and returns.","comment":"Second byte"},
        "11299": {"synopsis":"TAPE: writes the bytes of the channel's buffer as one recorded block (from TAPE create with\nA =\n$FF for the header block, from close and from write character with A = 0).\n1. Keeps A in $B2D6 and SP in $B2DA (TAPE_STOP_EXIT unwinds to it), resets the buffer\n   pointer\n$B2D3 to IX-1 and starts the motor of the unit in $B2AF (TAPE_IO_BEGIN), then waits about\n65536 loops for it to run up.\n2. Sets DAVE for writing: tone channel 0 period 1, port $A7 = $4E (left D/A, channels 1-2\nheld, the interrupt source is tone channel 0), output level 0.\n3. Lead-in: 5120 cycles (10240 for the header) at the leader period, one sync cycle, the\n   bytes\n$00 and $6A.\n4. The chunk count: ($B2CF) bytes in chunks of 256 (a last part counts as one), or $FF for\n   the\nheader.\n5. Each chunk: its length (0 = 256), its bytes taken downwards from IX, the CRC of its bytes\n(HL', low byte first). An empty buffer sends one more byte $00.\n6. Five cycles of leader, ($B2CF) = 0, then TAPE_IO_END.\nEntry: A = $FF for the header, 0 for data; IX = the byte above the buffer; ($B2CF) = its\nlength.\nExit: A = 0, Cy (TAPE_IO_END); STOP: A = $E5 (.STOP) through TAPE_STOP_EXIT.","comment":"$FF: the header block"},
        "11302": {"comment":"For TAPE_STOP_EXIT"},
        "11306": {"comment":"The buffer's first byte"},
        "11308": {"comment":"Write pointer back to the start"},
        "11312": {"comment":"The unit's remote: 0 REM1, else REM2"},
        "11315": {"comment":"Motor on, interrupts off"},
        "11318": {"comment":"65536 loops for the motor"},
        "11321": {"synopsis":"The motor run-up delay: 65536 loops (an even count of EX (SP),HL leaves HL).","comment":"Slow no-op pair"},
        "11327": {"comment":"Tone channel 0: period high byte 0"},
        "11330": {"comment":"Period low byte 1"},
        "11333": {"comment":"Left D/A, ch 1-2 held, IRQ from tone channel 0"},
        "11337": {"comment":"Output level 0"},
        "11341": {"comment":"5120 cycles of leader"},
        "11344": {"comment":"The header block?"},
        "11350": {"comment":"10240 cycles for the header"},
        "11353": {"synopsis":"Sends the leader, the sync cycle, the bytes $00 and $6A, then the chunk count.","comment":"The leader"},
        "11356": {"comment":"Sync cycle: low half"},
        "11360": {"comment":"High half"},
        "11364": {"comment":"Byte $00 (C = 0 after TAPE_WR_LEADER)"},
        "11367": {"comment":"Byte $6A"},
        "11372": {"comment":"Bytes in the buffer"},
        "11375": {"comment":"None?"},
        "11377": {"comment":"Full chunks of 256"},
        "11380": {"comment":"A part chunk left?"},
        "11384": {"comment":"It counts as one"},
        "11385": {"synopsis":"The header block sends $FF as its chunk count.","comment":"The header block?"},
        "11391": {"comment":"Count $FF"},
        "11392": {"synopsis":"Sends the chunk count in C.","comment":"The chunk count"},
        "11395": {"synopsis":"One chunk: its length, its bytes, its CRC; HL counts the bytes left.","comment":"256 or more left?"},
        "11397": {"comment":"D = the part left"},
        "11400": {"comment":"D = 0: 256 bytes"},
        "11402": {"synopsis":"Sends the chunk's length (0 = 256) and clears the CRC.","comment":"The chunk length"},
        "11406": {"comment":"CRC = 0"},
        "11411": {"synopsis":"Sends the chunk's bytes, taken downwards from IX.","comment":"Next buffer byte"},
        "11416": {"comment":"One fewer left"},
        "11420": {"comment":"Chunk done?"},
        "11423": {"comment":"Keep the count in DE"},
        "11425": {"comment":"CRC low byte"},
        "11429": {"comment":"CRC high byte"},
        "11434": {"comment":"Count back"},
        "11435": {"comment":"More bytes?"},
        "11439": {"comment":"A = 1: NZ, no extra byte"},
        "11440": {"synopsis":"An empty buffer (Z, C = 0) sends a byte $00 here; every block then ends with five leader\ncycles,\na wait for one more tone interrupt and ($B2CF) = 0.","comment":"Empty buffer: one byte $00"},
        "11443": {"comment":"5 cycles of leader"},
        "11449": {"comment":"Wait for the last half to end"},
        "11451": {"comment":"The buffer is empty"},
        "11458": {"comment":"Motor off, interrupts as before"},
        "11461": {"synopsis":"Writes leader cycles: each a low and a high half-period at the leader period ($B2DD). B\ncounts\nwithin C: B + 256 x (C - 1) cycles, or 256 x C with B = 0.\nExit: B = 0, C = 0.\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"Low half"},
        "11465": {"comment":"High half"},
        "11471": {"comment":"Next group of 256"},
        "11475": {"synopsis":"Writes the byte C to tape, bit 0 first: each bit adds to the CRC in HL' (CRC_ADD_BIT) and is\none\ncycle, a low then a high half-period at the period for a 1 ($B2DE) or a 0 ($B2DF).\nExit: C as on entry (eight rotations), B = 0.\nChanges: AF, B.","comment":"8 bits"},
        "11477": {"synopsis":"One bit: into the CRC, then a cycle at its period.","comment":"Next bit to bit 7"},
        "11479": {"comment":"NZ for a 1"},
        "11481": {"comment":"Into the CRC"},
        "11484": {"comment":"Low half"},
        "11488": {"comment":"High half"},
        "11495": {"synopsis":"Writes one half-period for the bit in bit 7 of C: Cy set gives level 0, Cy clear the output\nlevel ($B2DC).","comment":"A 1?"},
        "11499": {"comment":"Period for a 1"},
        "11504": {"synopsis":"A 0 bit: its period.","comment":"Period for a 0"},
        "11509": {"synopsis":"Writes one half-period at the leader period ($B2DD); Cy as in TAPE_WR_HALF.","comment":"Leader period"},
        "11514": {"synopsis":"Writes one half-period at the sync period ($B2E0); Cy as in TAPE_WR_HALF.","comment":"Sync period"},
        "11517": {"synopsis":"Writes one half-period: A is the period for tone channel 0 (port $A0); the next tone\ninterrupt\nends the current half and the level changes then, 0 with Cy set, the output level ($B2DC)\nwith\nCy clear. STOP (keyboard row 7 bit 0, selected by TAPE_IO_BEGIN) leaves through\nTAPE_STOP_EXIT.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"Period of the next half"},
        "11519": {"comment":"Keyboard row 7"},
        "11521": {"comment":"STOP pressed?"},
        "11525": {"comment":"The output level"},
        "11528": {"comment":"Cy clear: high"},
        "11530": {"comment":"Cy set: level 0"},
        "11531": {"synopsis":"Waits for the tone interrupt, then sets the level (falls into TAPE_WR_LEVEL).","comment":"The half ends (the RET at $0038 returns at once)"},
        "11533": {"synopsis":"Sets the output level (port $A8, left amplitude of channel 0 in D/A mode) to A, then resets\nthe\ntone interrupt's latch and keeps it enabled (port $B4 = 3).","comment":"Left output level"},
        "11535": {"comment":"Reset the tone interrupt latch, keep it enabled"},
        "11540": {"synopsis":"The four half-period codes for tone channel 0 (port $A0; a half lasts code + 1 DAVE ticks of\n4 us) at the fast speed, copied to $B2DD-$B2E0 by TAPE create ($2876): leader $34, a 1 bit\n$2A,\na 0 bit $3E, sync $56."},
        "11544": {"synopsis":"The same four codes for the slow speed (SP_TAPE not 0, $BFE6; read at $287F): leader $7C,\na 1 bit $63, a 0 bit $95, sync $C7."},
        "11548": {"synopsis":"Starts tape input or output: interrupts off, the motor of remote A on (TAPE_SET_REMOTE with\nD = 0; A\nkept\nin $B28E), the byte at $0038 kept in $B28D and replaced by RET so an interrupt only ends a\nHALT,\nand keyboard row 7 selected on port $B5 (PORTB5's upper bits kept) for the STOP tests.\nEntry: A = 0 for REM1, else REM2.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"No interrupts until TAPE_IO_END"},
        "11549": {"comment":"The remote, for TAPE_IO_END"},
        "11552": {"comment":"Motor on"},
        "11557": {"comment":"The interrupt entry"},
        "11560": {"comment":"Keep its first byte"},
        "11564": {"comment":"RET: an interrupt only wakes the HALT"},
        "11566": {"comment":"PORTB5"},
        "11569": {"comment":"Keep its upper bits"},
        "11571": {"comment":"Keyboard row 7 (STOP)"},
        "11576": {"synopsis":"Ends tape input or output: the motor off (TAPE_SET_REMOTE with D = $FF), the byte at $0038\nback,\noutput\nlevel 0, port $A7 = $20 (the interrupt source back to 50 Hz, no D/A, no sync), the interrupt\nenables back from IRQ_ENABLE_STATE ($BFC5), interrupts on.\nExit: A = 0, Cy.","comment":"The remote in use"},
        "11579": {"comment":"Motor off"},
        "11585": {"comment":"The interrupt entry's first byte back"},
        "11591": {"comment":"Output level 0"},
        "11595": {"comment":"IRQ from 50 Hz, no D/A"},
        "11599": {"comment":"IRQ_ENABLE_STATE"},
        "11602": {"comment":"Interrupt enables as before"},
        "11608": {"synopsis":"Adds one bit to the 16-bit CRC in HL': when the bit XOR bit 15 of HL' is 1, HL' is XORed\nwith\n$0810; then HL' turns left one place, that XOR result going into bit 0. Both paths take\nnearly\nthe same time. Shared by the TAPE writer, SERIAL and NET.\nEntry: NZ for a 1 bit, Z for a 0.\nChanges: AF, HL'."},
        "11609": {"comment":"Bit 1 as bit 7"},
        "11614": {"synopsis":"Works out the new bit against bit 15.","comment":"Against bit 15"},
        "11615": {"comment":"Cy = bit XOR bit 15"},
        "11618": {"comment":"Cy: CRC XOR $0810"},
        "11626": {"comment":"Bit 0 becomes 1"},
        "11629": {"synopsis":"No XOR: instructions that change nothing keep the time equal (and clear Cy).","comment":"HL unchanged, Cy clear"},
        "11633": {"comment":"Timing"},
        "11636": {"synopsis":"Turns HL' left, Cy into bit 0.","comment":"Shift, Cy into bit 0"},
        "11640": {"synopsis":"STOP while reading the tape: blanks the five status-line characters at $BED8\n(TAPE_BLANK_MSG, text at\nTXT_BLANK5) and puts back the input marker's bytes, then falls into TAPE_STOP_EXIT.","comment":"Clear the status line's tape text"},
        "11643": {"synopsis":"STOP during tape input or output: marks STOP held in the keyboard's old copy of row 7 ($BD27\nbit 0, so it is not seen again as a new key press), raises software interrupt $20 (?STOP),\nwaits\na little, ends the tape I/O (TAPE_IO_END) and returns from the routine that kept SP in $B2DA\n(TAPE_WR_BLOCK or the reader) with A = $E5 (.STOP), Z, NC.","comment":"Old copy of keyboard row 7"},
        "11646": {"comment":"STOP held: no new key press"},
        "11648": {"comment":"?STOP"},
        "11650": {"comment":"FLAG_SOFT_IRQ"},
        "11653": {"comment":"256 loops"},
        "11655": {"synopsis":"A short delay of 256 loops."},
        "11657": {"comment":"Motor off, interrupts back"},
        "11660": {"comment":".STOP; CP A gives Z and NC"},
        "11663": {"comment":"Back to the caller of the tape routine"},
        "11668": {"synopsis":"SERIAL's device pseudo-descriptor (ROM form): XX_NEXT $6DD2 (NET's, page-1 address), XX_RAM\n-2,\nDD_TYPE 0, DD_IRQFLAG $00 (no interrupt), DD_FLAGS $00, DD_TAB $6DA7 segment 0\n(SER_ENTRIES),\nDD_UNIT_COUNT 0, name \"SERIAL\", XX_SIZE 14. NET's XX_NEXT word points at XX_SIZE."},
        "11687": {"synopsis":"SERIAL's entry table (addresses as run in page 3): interrupt (SER_NO_WORK, unused:\nDD_IRQFLAG is\n0), open and create (SER_OPEN), close and destroy (SER_CLOSE), read character\n(SER_READ_CHAR),\nread block (SER_READ_BLOCK), write character (SER_WRITE_CHAR), write block\n(SER_WRITE_BLOCK),\nread status (SER_READ_STATUS), set status and special function (SER_NO_FN, error $E7 .NOFN),\ninitialise (SER_INIT), buffer moved (SER_NO_WORK)."},
        "11715": {"synopsis":"NET's device pseudo-descriptor (ROM form): XX_NEXT 0 (the last device of the chain), XX_RAM\n-2,\nDD_TYPE 0, DD_IRQFLAG $80 (external interrupt: the STATUS line), DD_FLAGS $00, DD_TAB $6DD3\nsegment 0 (NET_ENTRIES), DD_UNIT_COUNT 0, name \"NET\", XX_SIZE 11. SERIAL's XX_NEXT word\npoints at XX_SIZE."},
        "11731": {"synopsis":"NET's entry table (addresses as run in page 3): interrupt (NET_INTERRUPT), open and create\n(NET_OPEN), close and destroy (NET_CLOSE), read character (NET_READ_CHAR), read block\n(NET_READ_BLOCK), write character (NET_WRITE_CHAR), write block (NET_WRITE_BLOCK), read\nstatus\n(NET_READ_STATUS), set status (SER_NO_FN, error $E7 .NOFN), special function (NET_SPECIAL),\ninitialise (NET_INIT), buffer moved (NET_BUF_MOVED)."},
        "11759": {"synopsis":"The bit times for the 16 values of BAUD_SER, 3 bytes each, copied to $BC84-$BC86 by\nSER_SET_BAUD:\na word of delay loop counts for one bit (low byte the inner count, high byte the outer, as\nthe loops at $3368 and LINE_DELAY run them) and a count of samples ($BC86: how long a line\nlevel\nmust\nhold at $2E36 and LINE_RX_START). Values 14 and 15 are the same (9600 baud)."},
        "11807": {"synopsis":"NET, interrupt (entry +0): runs on the external interrupt (DD_IRQFLAG $80), which comes when\nanother machine pulls the STATUS line low. Receives one block into a channel's buffer.\n1. Nothing unless NET channels are open ($BC87 1-$7F) and STATUS is still low (port $B6 bit\n   5\nset: the inputs read inverted).\n2. Waits for DATA low, then for DATA high held ($BC86 samples), then counts bit times of\n   DATA\nhigh: exactly 9 (a start bit and eight 0 bits, the sync byte) before it goes low again.\n3. Reads destination, source and type into $BC8D-$BC8F ($BC8C = 0, the sync byte). The\ndestination (bits 7-6 = 01) must be ADDR_NET or 0 (to all); the source (bits 7-6 = 10) must\nhave a channel open for it, else the channel for any machine (slot 0); type bit 7 must be 1.\n4. Reads the 4-byte pattern again while it repeats (at least once); the byte that ends it\n   must\nbe the destination's complement. Then two bytes, the count's complement and the count.\n5. A block to this machine is acknowledged by pulling DATA low (NET_SEND_ACK).\n6. With data (type bit 0) and the channel's receive buffer free: reads the bytes and the CRC\ninto the buffer, checks the CRC, acknowledges again, sets the count (IX-4) and flags bits 1\nand 3; if no reader is waiting and CHAN_NET is $FF, sets CHAN_NET and MACH_NET and, when\nNET_IRQ is 0, software interrupt $30 (?NET).\n7. The type's end-of-record and end-of-file bits (5, 6) go into the flags (end of file only\n   for\na channel to one machine), bit 4 (a reader waiting) is cleared; NET_SAVE_FLAGS copies the\nflags to\nthe machine's slot and releases the lines.\nAny wrong byte, CRC or timeout returns at once without an acknowledge (STOP too).","comment":"$FF: SERIAL; n: NET channels open"},
        "11811": {"comment":"None open"},
        "11812": {"comment":"SERIAL owns the lines"},
        "11813": {"comment":"STATUS in: set while low"},
        "11817": {"comment":"Already released: too late"},
        "11818": {"comment":"Wait for DATA low"},
        "11824": {"synopsis":"Waits for DATA high, then for it to stay high ($BC86 samples).","comment":"Wait for DATA high"},
        "11830": {"comment":"Samples it must stay high"},
        "11834": {"synopsis":"DATA must stay high for B samples, else waits again.","comment":"DATA in: set while low"},
        "11838": {"comment":"Low again: start over"},
        "11842": {"comment":"Count bit times from 0"},
        "11844": {"synopsis":"Counts bit times while DATA stays high; 128 is too many.","comment":"128 bit times: give up"},
        "11846": {"comment":"Sample DATA one bit time later"},
        "11849": {"comment":"Still high?"},
        "11853": {"comment":"9 bit times: start bit and eight 0 bits?"},
        "11856": {"comment":"No: look for the sync byte again"},
        "11858": {"comment":"The sync byte of the pattern is 0"},
        "11863": {"comment":"Destination, source, type"},
        "11865": {"synopsis":"Reads the three header bytes after the sync byte into $BC8D-$BC8F.","comment":"Read a byte (Cy: failed)"},
        "11874": {"comment":"The destination byte"},
        "11877": {"comment":"Bits 7-6"},
        "11880": {"comment":"01: a destination?"},
        "11883": {"comment":"The address"},
        "11884": {"comment":"0: to all machines"},
        "11887": {"comment":"ADDR_NET"},
        "11890": {"comment":"Not for this machine"},
        "11892": {"synopsis":"Checks the source byte and finds the slot of a channel that takes it.","comment":"The source byte"},
        "11896": {"comment":"10: a source?"},
        "11899": {"comment":"A = the source address"},
        "11901": {"comment":"HL = its slot ($BC90 + 4A)"},
        "11904": {"comment":"A channel for that machine?"},
        "11908": {"comment":"Slot 0: the channel for any machine"},
        "11911": {"comment":"None open: ignore the block"},
        "11914": {"synopsis":"Keeps the slot's address in $BC88 and checks the type byte.","comment":"The slot taking the block"},
        "11918": {"comment":"The type byte"},
        "11919": {"comment":"Bit 7 must be 1"},
        "11922": {"comment":"Full repeats of the pattern"},
        "11924": {"synopsis":"Compares the next four bytes with the pattern; E counts the full repeats.","comment":"4 bytes a pattern"},
        "11929": {"synopsis":"Reads a byte and compares it with the pattern.","comment":"Next byte"},
        "11933": {"comment":"As in the pattern?"},
        "11940": {"comment":"One more full repeat"},
        "11943": {"synopsis":"The pattern stops: this must be the place of the sync byte, after at least one repeat, and\nthe\nbyte the destination's complement; then come the count's complement and the count.","comment":"The destination's complement?"},
        "11946": {"comment":"At the sync byte's place?"},
        "11950": {"comment":"At least one repeat?"},
        "11952": {"comment":"The count's complement"},
        "11958": {"comment":"The count (also in C)"},
        "11962": {"comment":"Complements of each other?"},
        "11964": {"comment":"The destination address alone"},
        "11968": {"comment":"To this machine: acknowledge"},
        "11971": {"comment":"The slot"},
        "11974": {"comment":"IX = its channel RAM, page 1 = its segment"},
        "11977": {"comment":"The source address"},
        "11982": {"comment":"Where the block came from"},
        "11985": {"comment":"The type"},
        "11988": {"comment":"Data follows?"},
        "11993": {"comment":"Receive buffer still full?"},
        "11997": {"comment":"Yes: refuse the data, no acknowledge"},
        "11998": {"comment":"HL = IX"},
        "11999": {"comment":"Receive buffer below IX-6"},
        "12005": {"comment":"D, E = the count (0 = 256)"},
        "12007": {"comment":"BC = count - 1"},
        "12010": {"comment":"HL = the first byte's place"},
        "12012": {"comment":"BC = 0"},
        "12013": {"comment":"CRC = 0"},
        "12017": {"comment":"STATUS still low?"},
        "12021": {"comment":"Released: the sender gave up"},
        "12022": {"comment":"Wait for DATA low"},
        "12028": {"synopsis":"Reads the data bytes upwards into the receive buffer.","comment":"Next data byte"},
        "12032": {"comment":"Into the buffer"},
        "12037": {"comment":"CRC of the data"},
        "12040": {"comment":"CRC low byte"},
        "12044": {"comment":"Matches?"},
        "12046": {"comment":"CRC high byte"},
        "12052": {"comment":"To this machine?"},
        "12056": {"comment":"Yes: acknowledge the data"},
        "12059": {"comment":"Bytes in the buffer"},
        "12062": {"comment":"Bit 1: buffer full"},
        "12066": {"comment":"Bit 3: data not yet announced"},
        "12070": {"comment":"A reader waiting?"},
        "12076": {"comment":"CHAN_NET"},
        "12079": {"comment":"Free ($FF)?"},
        "12083": {"comment":"Its channel number + 1 (descriptor byte IX+11)"},
        "12087": {"comment":"CHAN_NET = this channel"},
        "12090": {"comment":"The source machine"},
        "12093": {"comment":"MACH_NET"},
        "12096": {"comment":"NET_IRQ: 0 = software interrupt wanted"},
        "12102": {"comment":"?NET"},
        "12104": {"comment":"FLAG_SOFT_IRQ"},
        "12107": {"synopsis":"Takes the type byte for the end-of-record and end-of-file bits.","comment":"The type"},
        "12110": {"synopsis":"Copies the type's end-of-record (bit 5) and end-of-file (bit 6) bits into the flags,\nclearing\nbit 4; end of file is dropped for the channel to any machine.","comment":"End of record, end of file"},
        "12113": {"comment":"The channel's remote address"},
        "12117": {"comment":"A channel to one machine?"},
        "12119": {"comment":"No: no end of file"},
        "12121": {"synopsis":"Merges the bits into (IX-3) and stores the flags in the slot (NET_SAVE_FLAGS).","comment":"Flags: keep 7 and 3-0, clear 4"},
        "12130": {"comment":"Into the slot, lines released"},
        "12133": {"synopsis":"NET, open channel and create channel (entries +2 and +4): C = the unit, the remote machine's\naddress (0 = any machine).\n1. Errors: SERIAL open ($D7, .SEROP), ADDR_NET 0 ($D6, .NOADR: \"Network address not set\" in\nthe run), the unit equal to ADDR_NET or above 32 ($E8, .IUNIT), a channel for that machine\nalready open ($D5, .NETOP).\n2. The first NET channel clears the 33 four-byte slots at $BC90-$BD13.\n3. EXOS 27 allocates 517 bytes of channel RAM (two 256-byte buffers and five bytes); (IX-1)\n   = the\nunit, (IX-3) = 1, the counts (IX-4) and (IX-5) = 0; the machine's slot gets flag 1, IX and\nthe segment (NET_SET_SLOT).\n4. Counts the channel in $BC87, sets IRQ_ENABLE_STATE bit 6 (external interrupt), releases\nboth lines (port $B7 = 0), sets FORM_SER to 0 and the bit times from BAUD_SER\n(SER_SET_BAUD).\nExit: A = 0, or the error.","comment":"No interrupts while setting up"},
        "12134": {"comment":"$FF: SERIAL open"},
        "12139": {"comment":".SEROP"},
        "12142": {"comment":"ADDR_NET"},
        "12146": {"comment":"Set?"},
        "12148": {"comment":".NOADR (\"Network address not set\")"},
        "12151": {"synopsis":"Checks the unit: not this machine's address, 0-32.","comment":"The machine's own address?"},
        "12155": {"comment":"Above 32?"},
        "12159": {"synopsis":"Error $E8 (.IUNIT): an invalid unit.","comment":".IUNIT"},
        "12162": {"synopsis":"Finds the machine's slot; with channels already open, it must be free.","comment":"HL = the unit's slot"},
        "12165": {"comment":"Channels open?"},
        "12171": {"comment":"The slot's flags"},
        "12172": {"comment":"Keep HL, BC in the other set"},
        "12173": {"comment":"Free?"},
        "12176": {"comment":".NETOP: already open for it"},
        "12179": {"synopsis":"The first NET channel: clears all 33 slots.","comment":"Keep HL, BC in the other set"},
        "12180": {"comment":"Slots for machines 0-32"},
        "12193": {"synopsis":"Allocates the channel RAM and sets up the channel and its slot.","comment":"517 bytes: two buffers and five bytes"},
        "12198": {"comment":"Error"},
        "12199": {"comment":"HL = the slot, C = the unit"},
        "12200": {"comment":"The remote address"},
        "12203": {"comment":"Flags: open"},
        "12207": {"comment":"Nothing received"},
        "12211": {"comment":"Nothing to send"},
        "12215": {"comment":"Slot in use"},
        "12217": {"comment":"IX and the segment into the slot"},
        "12220": {"comment":"One more NET channel"},
        "12224": {"comment":"IRQ_ENABLE_STATE"},
        "12227": {"comment":"Bit 6: external interrupt on"},
        "12229": {"comment":"Both lines released"},
        "12232": {"comment":"FORM_SER = 0: 8 bits, no parity, 2 stop bits"},
        "12237": {"comment":"Bit times from BAUD_SER"},
        "12239": {"synopsis":"SERIAL, open channel and create channel (entries +2 and +4): only one SERIAL channel ($E9,\nerror .2NDCH, if open) and none while NET channels are open ($D7, .SEROP). Takes no channel\nRAM (EXOS 27 with DE = 0), empties the receive buffer ($BC83 = 0), marks SERIAL open ($BC87\n=\n$FF), pulls both lines low (port $B7 = 3, the serial idle state) and falls into\nSER_SET_BAUD.\nExit: A = 0, or the error.","comment":"No interrupts"},
        "12240": {"comment":"$FF: SERIAL; n: NET channels"},
        "12244": {"comment":".2NDCH: SERIAL already open"},
        "12247": {"comment":".SEROP: NET channels open"},
        "12250": {"comment":"Receive buffer empty"},
        "12254": {"comment":"No channel RAM"},
        "12258": {"comment":"Error"},
        "12259": {"comment":"SERIAL open"},
        "12264": {"comment":"DATA out and STATUS out low"},
        "12268": {"synopsis":"Copies the three bytes of BAUD_SER's entry (value modulo 16) in SER_BAUD_TIMES to\n$BC84-$BC86.\nExit: A = 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BAUD_SER"},
        "12271": {"comment":"Modulo 16"},
        "12274": {"comment":"Times 3"},
        "12277": {"comment":"SER_BAUD_TIMES"},
        "12283": {"comment":"Bit time, sample count"},
        "12293": {"synopsis":"NET, close channel and destroy channel (entries +6 and +8):\n1. Anything written since the last send goes out as a last block, with end of record and end\nof file set in its type (NET_SEND_BLOCK).\n2. The machine's slot is cleared; one NET channel fewer in $BC87. The last one turns the\nexternal interrupt off (IRQ_ENABLE_STATE bit 6).\n3. CHAN_NET and MACH_NET become $FF, except when other channels are open and this one had a\nblock waiting: then NET_NEXT_CHAN names the next.\nExit: A = 0."},
        "12294": {"comment":"Written to?"},
        "12300": {"comment":"Type: bit 7 always"},
        "12302": {"comment":"Bytes in the send buffer?"},
        "12308": {"comment":"Bit 0: data follows"},
        "12310": {"synopsis":"Adds end of record and end of file and sends the last block.","comment":"End of record, end of file"},
        "12312": {"comment":"The type for the send"},
        "12315": {"comment":"Send the block"},
        "12318": {"synopsis":"Frees the machine's slot and counts the channel out.","comment":"The remote address"},
        "12321": {"comment":"Its slot"},
        "12324": {"comment":"Block not announced yet? (kept in F')"},
        "12327": {"comment":"Slot free"},
        "12329": {"comment":"NET channels"},
        "12332": {"comment":"The last one?"},
        "12335": {"comment":"IRQ_ENABLE_STATE"},
        "12338": {"comment":"External interrupt off"},
        "12342": {"synopsis":"Other channels stay open: if this channel's block was waiting, finds the next."},
        "12343": {"comment":"Had a waiting block: name the next"},
        "12346": {"synopsis":"CHAN_NET and MACH_NET become $FF (no block waiting).","comment":"None"},
        "12348": {"comment":"CHAN_NET"},
        "12351": {"comment":"MACH_NET"},
        "12356": {"synopsis":"SERIAL, close channel and destroy channel (entries +6 and +8): releases both lines (port $B7\n=\n0) and marks SERIAL closed ($BC87 = 0).\nExit: A = 0."},
        "12357": {"comment":"Both lines released"},
        "12359": {"comment":"No SERIAL or NET channel"},
        "12363": {"synopsis":"NET, read character (entry +10): returns the next byte of the receive buffer in B.\n1. An empty buffer after a block marked end of record gives error $E4 (.EOF); the\n   end-of-record\nmark is cleared unless end of file is set too, so end of file keeps giving it.\n2. Otherwise sets flag bit 4 and waits with interrupts on until NET_INTERRUPT clears it (a\n   block\narrived); STOP gives $E5 (.STOP).\n3. The bytes are taken upwards from IX-6 - (count - 1); the last one clears flag bit 1. If\n   the\nblock was still announced (bit 3), it is cleared and NET_NEXT_CHAN names the next channel in\nCHAN_NET.\nExit: A = 0, B = the byte; or the error.","comment":"No interrupts while looking"},
        "12364": {"comment":"The flags"},
        "12367": {"comment":"Bytes in the buffer?"},
        "12371": {"comment":"End of record?"},
        "12375": {"comment":"End of file too?"},
        "12379": {"comment":"No: report end of record once"},
        "12383": {"synopsis":"Error $E4 (.EOF).","comment":".EOF"},
        "12386": {"synopsis":"Waits for a block: bit 4 set until NET_INTERRUPT clears it.","comment":"A reader waiting"},
        "12390": {"comment":"Let the interrupt in"},
        "12391": {"synopsis":"The wait, with a STOP test each time round.","comment":"Keyboard row 7"},
        "12394": {"comment":"STOP pressed?"},
        "12400": {"comment":"Still waiting?"},
        "12406": {"comment":"A block came: look again"},
        "12408": {"synopsis":"Takes the next byte from the receive buffer.","comment":"HL = IX"},
        "12411": {"comment":"The buffer's top byte is IX-6"},
        "12417": {"comment":"Bytes left"},
        "12423": {"comment":"HL = the next byte"},
        "12426": {"comment":"The byte"},
        "12427": {"comment":"One fewer (Z: the last)"},
        "12430": {"comment":"Keep Z"},
        "12431": {"comment":"The remote address"},
        "12434": {"comment":"Its slot"},
        "12438": {"comment":"The flags"},
        "12441": {"comment":"Bytes left?"},
        "12443": {"comment":"No: buffer empty"},
        "12445": {"synopsis":"Clears the announced bit 3 and stores the flags in the channel and its slot.","comment":"Was it announced?"},
        "12447": {"comment":"Not any more"},
        "12452": {"comment":"And in the slot"},
        "12453": {"comment":"Not announced: done"},
        "12455": {"synopsis":"When CHAN_NET names this channel (CHAN_NET + 1 = IX+11), points CHAN_NET and MACH_NET at the\nlowest machine whose slot has a block announced (flag bit 3), reaching its channel RAM with\nNET_SLOT_CHAN, or sets both to $FF when there is none.\nExit: A = 0.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL, IX.","comment":"CHAN_NET"},
        "12459": {"comment":"This channel?"},
        "12465": {"comment":"33 slots"},
        "12467": {"comment":"From machine 0"},
        "12470": {"synopsis":"Looks for a slot with a block announced.","comment":"A block announced?"},
        "12474": {"comment":"Next slot"},
        "12480": {"comment":"None: $FF for both"},
        "12485": {"synopsis":"Takes the channel number and the source machine from that channel's RAM.","comment":"IX = that channel's RAM"},
        "12488": {"comment":"Its source machine"},
        "12491": {"comment":"Its channel number + 1 (descriptor byte IX+11)"},
        "12495": {"synopsis":"Sets CHAN_NET to A and MACH_NET to B.","comment":"CHAN_NET"},
        "12499": {"comment":"MACH_NET"},
        "12503": {"synopsis":"Returns A = 0."},
        "12505": {"synopsis":"SERIAL, read character (entry +10): hands out the next byte of the receive buffer at $BC88\n($BC83 bytes, $BC82 the read index). When it is empty, fills it:\n1. Raises STATUS out (port $B7 = 1: the other end may send) and waits for a character as\n   long\nas it takes, then reads more with a timeout, up to 16.\n2. Pulls STATUS low again (port $B7 = 3) and still takes characters that come before a\ntimeout, up to 24 in all.\n3. Then hands out the first. STOP gives $E5 (.STOP).\nExit: A = 0, B = the byte; or the error.","comment":"Bytes waiting"},
        "12511": {"comment":"One fewer"},
        "12515": {"comment":"The read index"},
        "12519": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "12525": {"comment":"The buffer"},
        "12529": {"comment":"B = the byte"},
        "12532": {"synopsis":"The buffer is empty: fills it from the line.","comment":"No interrupts while receiving"},
        "12533": {"comment":"Read index 0"},
        "12536": {"comment":"Cy: no timeout for the first"},
        "12537": {"synopsis":"Reads characters with STATUS out high, up to 16.","comment":"STATUS out high: may send"},
        "12539": {"comment":"Read one into the buffer (A = count)"},
        "12542": {"comment":"Timeout or STOP"},
        "12544": {"comment":"16 yet?"},
        "12546": {"comment":"NC: fewer, read on with a timeout"},
        "12551": {"synopsis":"STOP returns $E5; a timeout ends the filling.","comment":".STOP?"},
        "12554": {"synopsis":"Pulls STATUS low: the other end must stop sending.","comment":"STATUS out low"},
        "12558": {"synopsis":"Takes characters still coming, up to 24 in all.","comment":"Keep STATUS low"},
        "12560": {"comment":"NC: with a timeout"},
        "12564": {"comment":"Timeout or STOP"},
        "12566": {"comment":"24 yet?"},
        "12572": {"synopsis":"STOP returns $E5; a timeout ends the filling.","comment":".STOP?"},
        "12575": {"synopsis":"Interrupts back on; hands out the first byte."},
        "12576": {"comment":"Take the first"},
        "12578": {"synopsis":"NET, read block (entry +12): the shared read-block loop at DEV_BLOCK_READ with NET_READ_CHAR\nfor each\nbyte.","comment":"Per byte: NET_READ_CHAR"},
        "12584": {"synopsis":"SERIAL, read block (entry +12): the shared read-block loop at DEV_BLOCK_READ with\nSER_READ_CHAR for\neach\nbyte.","comment":"Per byte: SER_READ_CHAR"},
        "12590": {"synopsis":"NET, write character (entry +14): puts B into the send buffer (downwards from IX-$106, count\nin IX-5) and sets flag bits 2 (bytes to send) and 7 (written to). The 256th byte sends the\nbuffer as a block of type $81 (data) through NET_SEND_BUF.\nExit: A = 0, or the error.","comment":"HL = IX"},
        "12593": {"comment":"The send buffer's top byte is IX-$106"},
        "12599": {"comment":"Bytes in it"},
        "12606": {"comment":"Store the byte"},
        "12607": {"comment":"Bytes to send"},
        "12611": {"comment":"Written to"},
        "12615": {"comment":"One more (0: 256)"},
        "12618": {"comment":"Not full: store the flags, A = 0"},
        "12623": {"comment":"Full: type $81, data follows"},
        "12630": {"synopsis":"Sends the send buffer as a block of the type in $BC83 (NET_SEND_BLOCK). STOP ($E5) empties\nthe buffer\n(NET_SENT); another error is returned.\nExit: NC and A = 0 when sent; else the error.","comment":"Send it"},
        "12633": {"comment":"Sent"},
        "12634": {"comment":".STOP?"},
        "12637": {"comment":"STOP: the buffer is emptied"},
        "12640": {"synopsis":"SERIAL, write character (entry +14): waits for STATUS in high (the other end ready; STOP\ngives\n$E5), then sends B as SER_SEND_BYTE does. Falls into it.","comment":"No interrupts while sending"},
        "12641": {"comment":"Wait for STATUS in high"},
        "12647": {"comment":"STOP"},
        "12649": {"synopsis":"Sends B on DATA out in the FORM_SER format: a start bit (DATA high), 8 or 7 data bits (bit 0\nfirst; FORM_SER bit 0 = 7 bits), a parity bit when bit 1 is set (odd with bit 2, of the\nwhole\nbyte), then 2 stop bits, or 1 with bit 3 (DATA low). Each bit lasts the bit time at $BC84;\nthe data bits add to the CRC kept at $BC80. A STOP press during it gives $E5 at the end.\nNET's\nsender calls it for every byte ($32AC on).\nEntry: B = the byte.\nExit: A = 0, or $E5 (.STOP) with Cy."},
        "12652": {"comment":"C = the byte"},
        "12653": {"comment":"FORM_SER"},
        "12656": {"comment":"8 data bits"},
        "12658": {"comment":"7 bits?"},
        "12662": {"comment":"7 data bits"},
        "12663": {"synopsis":"Sends the start bit and takes the CRC.","comment":"Start bit: DATA high"},
        "12667": {"comment":"The CRC so far"},
        "12671": {"synopsis":"Sends the data bits, bit 0 first.","comment":"Next bit into Cy"},
        "12673": {"comment":"Send it"},
        "12678": {"comment":"Keep the CRC"},
        "12683": {"comment":"FORM_SER"},
        "12684": {"comment":"7 bits?"},
        "12687": {"comment":"Clear Cy"},
        "12688": {"comment":"Eighth turn: C as it was"},
        "12690": {"synopsis":"Sends a parity bit when FORM_SER bit 1 asks for one.","comment":"Parity?"},
        "12693": {"comment":"Cy = odd parity"},
        "12694": {"comment":"Parity of the whole byte"},
        "12698": {"synopsis":"Sends one stop bit, a second one unless FORM_SER bit 3 is set.","comment":"Stop bit: DATA low"},
        "12701": {"comment":"1 stop bit?"},
        "12705": {"comment":"Second stop bit"},
        "12708": {"synopsis":"Checks STOP and returns."},
        "12711": {"comment":"Keyboard row 7"},
        "12714": {"comment":"STOP pressed?"},
        "12722": {"synopsis":"NET, write block (entry +16): the shared write-block loop at DEV_BLOCK_WRITE with\nNET_WRITE_CHAR for\neach byte.","comment":"Per byte: NET_WRITE_CHAR"},
        "12728": {"synopsis":"SERIAL, write block (entry +16): the shared write-block loop at DEV_BLOCK_WRITE with\nSER_WRITE_CHAR\nfor\neach byte.","comment":"Per byte: SER_WRITE_CHAR"},
        "12734": {"synopsis":"NET, read status (entry +18): C = 0 with bytes in the receive buffer, 1 when it is empty,\n$FF\nat the end of a record. End of record alone is reported once: its mark is cleared (and\nstored\nin the slot, NET_SAVE_FLAGS); end of file keeps it.\nExit: A = 0, C = the status."},
        "12735": {"comment":"C = 0: a byte is ready"},
        "12736": {"comment":"The flags"},
        "12739": {"comment":"Bytes in the buffer?"},
        "12742": {"comment":"C = 1: none"},
        "12743": {"comment":"End of record?"},
        "12746": {"comment":"C = $FF: end of record"},
        "12748": {"comment":"End of file too?"},
        "12751": {"comment":"No: report end of record once"},
        "12758": {"synopsis":"SERIAL, read status (entry +18): always C = 0, a character ready.\nExit: A = 0, C = 0."},
        "12761": {"synopsis":"SERIAL and NET, set status (entry +20), and SERIAL, special function (entry +22): error $E7\n(.NOFN), the call is not supported.","comment":".NOFN"},
        "12763": {"synopsis":"SERIAL, interrupt (entry +0, unused: DD_IRQFLAG is 0) and buffer moved (entry +26): nothing\nto\ndo."},
        "12764": {"synopsis":"NET, special function (entry +22), B = the subfunction: 16 (@@FLSH) NET_FLUSH, 17 (@@CLR)\nNET_CLEAR, others error $EA (.ISPEC)."},
        "12765": {"comment":"@@FLSH?"},
        "12769": {"comment":"@@CLR?"},
        "12773": {"comment":".ISPEC"},
        "12776": {"synopsis":"@@FLSH: when anything was written since the last send, sends the send buffer as a block\nmarked\nend of record (type $A0, $A1 with data) through NET_SEND_BUF.\nExit: A = 0, or the error."},
        "12777": {"comment":"Written to?"},
        "12782": {"comment":"Type: bit 7 always"},
        "12784": {"comment":"Bytes in the send buffer?"},
        "12790": {"comment":"Bit 0: data follows"},
        "12792": {"synopsis":"Adds the end-of-record bit and sends.","comment":"End of record"},
        "12797": {"comment":"Send it"},
        "12800": {"synopsis":"@@CLR: empties both buffers: the counts become 0 and the flags keep only bits 7 and 0. If\nthe\nchannel's block was still announced, NET_NEXT_CHAN names the next one in CHAN_NET.\nExit: A = 0.","comment":"The remote address"},
        "12803": {"comment":"Its slot"},
        "12806": {"comment":"Keep bits 7 and 0"},
        "12809": {"comment":"A block announced?"},
        "12811": {"comment":"Flags in the channel"},
        "12814": {"comment":"And in the slot"},
        "12815": {"comment":"Send buffer empty"},
        "12819": {"comment":"Receive buffer empty"},
        "12823": {"comment":"Announced: name the next"},
        "12828": {"synopsis":"SERIAL, initialise (entry +24): no SERIAL or NET channel open ($BC87 = 0).\nExit: A = 0."},
        "12829": {"comment":"No SERIAL or NET channel"},
        "12832": {"synopsis":"NET, initialise (entry +24): nothing to do (SER_INIT's RET)."},
        "12833": {"synopsis":"NET, buffer moved (entry +26): records the channel's new place in its machine's slot.\nEntry: IX = the channel's RAM, (IX-1) = its machine number.\nFalls into NET_SET_SLOT with HL = that slot.","comment":"The channel's machine number"},
        "12836": {"comment":"HL = its slot at $BC90 + 4n"},
        "12839": {"synopsis":"Stores IX in bytes 1-2 of the slot at HL and the segment now in page 1 in byte 3, so that\nthe\nreceiver can reach the channel's RAM from any segment (NET_SLOT_CHAN reads them back).\nEntry: HL = the slot (NET_SLOT_ADDR).\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"DE = the channel's RAM"},
        "12842": {"comment":"Bytes 1-2: IX"},
        "12847": {"comment":"Byte 3: the segment in page 1"},
        "12851": {"synopsis":"The addressed machine gave no acknowledge: releases both lines and waits a random time,\nup to 2 x 256 rounds of 256 loops, testing STOP each round; then backs off and sends again."},
        "12852": {"comment":"Release data and status out"},
        "12855": {"comment":"H = 2, L = a random even count"},
        "12861": {"comment":"Keyboard row 7 (the STOP key)"},
        "12864": {"synopsis":"Loop: tests STOP, spins 256 times, counts L then H down.","comment":"STOP pressed?"},
        "12872": {"synopsis":"Loop: 256 empty DJNZ turns."},
        "12880": {"synopsis":"A collision or a failed send: waits 1-16 (a random count) times ten bit times with\ninterrupts on, then falls into NET_SEND_BLOCK to try again."},
        "12881": {"comment":"A = 1-16 from the refresh counter"},
        "12886": {"synopsis":"Loop: ten bit times per count."},
        "12892": {"synopsis":"NET: sends the channel's write buffer as a block (from close, from write character when the\nbuffer is full and from special function 16). Interrupts are off.\nEntry: IX = the channel, (IX-1) = the destination machine (0 = everyone), (IX-5) = the byte\ncount (0 = 256), $BC83 = the block's flags byte (bit 7 set, bit 0 = data follows).\n1. Waits until the status line is free, then listens for a random 1-16 ten-bit-time periods;\ntraffic sends it back to waiting.\n2. Raises status out, resets the external interrupt latch and watches the data line for\nADDR_NET + 1 periods: data from another machine means a collision (NET_BACKOFF). A lower\naddress waits less, so it wins.\n3. Sends the header four times: $00, destination OR $40, ADDR_NET OR $80, the flags; then\n   the\ndestination's complement, the count's complement and the count.\n4. Unless broadcast, waits for the receiver's acknowledge (NET_GET_ACK); none: NET_NO_ACK.\n5. When bit 0 of the flags is set, sends the buffer (its bytes stored downwards from\nIX-$106) and the CRC that the bit routines kept at $BC80, and waits for the acknowledge\nagain.\n6. Marks the buffer empty and falls into NET_SAVE_FLAGS.\nExit: NC and A = 0 when sent; carry with A = $E5 (.STOP) when STOP was pressed, or with A =\n0\nwhen the status line dropped while waiting for the data line."},
        "12893": {"comment":"Status in"},
        "12897": {"comment":"Line free?"},
        "12899": {"synopsis":"Waits for the status line to go low (a sender finished).","comment":"Wait for status in low"},
        "12904": {"comment":"STOP pressed"},
        "12905": {"synopsis":"Listens for a random 1-16 ten-bit-time periods.","comment":"C = 1-16 from the refresh counter"},
        "12911": {"synopsis":"Loop: back to waiting when the status line rises.","comment":"Someone sending?"},
        "12923": {"comment":"Status out high: claim the line"},
        "12927": {"comment":"IRQ_ENABLE_STATE with bit 7: reset the external latch"},
        "12934": {"comment":"C = ADDR_NET + 1 periods"},
        "12940": {"synopsis":"Loop: watches the data line for ADDR_NET + 1 periods.","comment":"Data in high: another machine is sending?"},
        "12946": {"comment":"Release the lines and back off"},
        "12952": {"synopsis":"Loop step: waits one period."},
        "12958": {"comment":"Data and status out high"},
        "12968": {"comment":"The header goes out 4 times"},
        "12970": {"synopsis":"Loop: sends one copy of the 4-byte header.","comment":"Byte 0: $00"},
        "12976": {"comment":"D = the destination machine"},
        "12980": {"comment":"Byte 1: destination OR $40"},
        "12987": {"comment":"Byte 2: ADDR_NET OR $80 (the sender)"},
        "12996": {"comment":"Byte 3: the flags"},
        "13009": {"comment":"The destination byte's complement ends the copies"},
        "13015": {"comment":"E = the byte count"},
        "13019": {"comment":"Its complement, then the count"},
        "13028": {"comment":"Broadcast (machine 0)?"},
        "13032": {"comment":"Acknowledged?"},
        "13035": {"comment":"No: wait and send again"},
        "13038": {"comment":"Wait for data in low"},
        "13044": {"synopsis":"Sends the data part when the flags' bit 0 says there is one."},
        "13047": {"comment":"Data follows?"},
        "13052": {"comment":"Data and status out high"},
        "13056": {"comment":"Clear the CRC"},
        "13065": {"comment":"HL = IX - $106, the buffer's first byte"},
        "13074": {"comment":"C = the count (0 = 256)"},
        "13077": {"synopsis":"Loop: sends the buffer's bytes, going down in memory."},
        "13085": {"comment":"Then the CRC, low byte first"},
        "13096": {"comment":"Broadcast?"},
        "13100": {"comment":"Acknowledged?"},
        "13103": {"comment":"No: wait and send again"},
        "13106": {"comment":"Wait for data in low"},
        "13112": {"synopsis":"The block has gone: marks the write buffer empty (flags bit 2, count 0) and falls into\nNET_SAVE_FLAGS with A = 0.","comment":"Write buffer empty"},
        "13120": {"synopsis":"Copies the channel's flags (IX-3) into byte 0 of its machine's slot and releases both\nlines. Keeps AF.\nEntry: IX = the channel."},
        "13121": {"comment":"HL = the slot of machine (IX-1)"},
        "13131": {"comment":"Release data and status out"},
        "13136": {"synopsis":"Sends the parity bit of A (SERIAL and NET bit level, port B7h).\nEntry: A = the byte, carry clear for even parity, set for odd.\nChanges: AF, DE.","comment":"Odd parity?"},
        "13139": {"comment":"Even number of ones: send 0"},
        "13144": {"synopsis":"Odd parity: the opposite bit."},
        "13145": {"comment":"Even number of ones: send 1"},
        "13150": {"synopsis":"Sends the bit in carry."},
        "13152": {"synopsis":"Sends a 0 bit: data out low, status out high.","comment":"Data out low, status out high"},
        "13156": {"synopsis":"Sends a 1 bit: data and status out high.","comment":"Data and status out high"},
        "13158": {"synopsis":"Puts A on port B7h, holds it one bit time ($BC84) and folds bit 7 of C into the running\nCRC in HL' (CRC_ADD_BIT).\nEntry: A = the B7h value, C = the byte being sent.\nChanges: AF, DE."},
        "13160": {"comment":"DE = one bit time"},
        "13165": {"synopsis":"Loop: counts the bit time down."},
        "13171": {"comment":"Z = the bit is 0"},
        "13173": {"comment":"Update the CRC"},
        "13177": {"synopsis":"SERIAL: receives a byte (LINE_RX_BYTE) and appends it to the buffer at $BC88, counting\nit in $BC83.\nEntry: A = the B7h value while waiting, carry = no timeout.\nExit: NC and A = the new count; carry as LINE_RX_BYTE."},
        "13181": {"comment":"HL = $BC88 + the count"},
        "13191": {"comment":"Store the byte"},
        "13198": {"synopsis":"NET: receives a byte while the sender keeps the status line high.\nExit: NC and A = the byte; carry with A = 0 when the status line dropped, or with A = the\nerror ($E5, STOP). Keeps DE, HL."},
        "13200": {"synopsis":"Loop: waits for a byte, giving up when the status line drops.","comment":"Status in still high?"},
        "13207": {"comment":"B7h = 0, with a timeout"},
        "13212": {"comment":"A byte came"},
        "13214": {"comment":"Timed out: try again"},
        "13217": {"synopsis":"Returns with carry."},
        "13218": {"synopsis":"Restores DE and HL."},
        "13221": {"synopsis":"Receives one byte from the data line (port B6h bit 4): start bit, 8 data bits (7 when\nFORM_SER bit 0 is set) LSB first, stop bit; each sample updates the CRC kept at $BC80.\nEntry: A = the value for port B7h while receiving, carry set to wait without a timeout.\nExit: NC and A = C = the byte; carry with A = 0 on a timeout (8 rounds of the bit-time\ncount),\nor A = $E5 when STOP was pressed."},
        "13222": {"comment":"PORTB5 with keyboard row 7 (the STOP key)"},
        "13232": {"comment":"Handshake out"},
        "13234": {"synopsis":"Starts the 8 timeout rounds."},
        "13236": {"synopsis":"One timeout round of ($BC84) loops."},
        "13240": {"synopsis":"Loop: waits for the start bit (data in low).","comment":"Data in low: a start bit?"},
        "13252": {"comment":"STOP pressed?"},
        "13259": {"comment":"Next round"},
        "13262": {"comment":"Carry at entry: wait for ever"},
        "13264": {"comment":"Timed out: A = 0, carry"},
        "13267": {"synopsis":"Checks that the start bit lasts ($BC86) reads."},
        "13271": {"synopsis":"Loop: a glitch sends it back to waiting."},
        "13279": {"comment":"Wait past the start bit"},
        "13282": {"comment":"8 data bits, or 7 when FORM_SER bit 0 is set"},
        "13291": {"synopsis":"Loads the running CRC into HL' for the data bits."},
        "13296": {"synopsis":"Loop: samples a bit and shifts it into C from the top."},
        "13299": {"comment":"Carry = data in"},
        "13308": {"comment":"Keep the CRC"},
        "13312": {"comment":"7 bits?"},
        "13318": {"comment":"Shift once more with a 0 to right-align"},
        "13321": {"synopsis":"Waits for the stop bit (data in high) and returns the byte."},
        "13322": {"comment":"Wait for data in high"},
        "13331": {"synopsis":"Samples port B6h, folds its data bit (bit 4) into the CRC in HL' (CRC_ADD_BIT) and waits one\nbit time.\nExit: A = H = the sample.\nChanges: DE."},
        "13334": {"comment":"Z = data in low"},
        "13339": {"comment":"DE = one bit time"},
        "13344": {"synopsis":"Loop: counts the bit time down."},
        "13352": {"synopsis":"NET: raises status out with data out low, waits 4 bit times and reads the data line,\nwhich the receiver raises to acknowledge (NET_SEND_ACK).\nExit: Z when no acknowledge came.","comment":"Status out high, data out low"},
        "13361": {"comment":"Z = no acknowledge"},
        "13366": {"synopsis":"NET: acknowledges a block: raises data out for 8 bit times, then releases the lines.","comment":"Data out high"},
        "13375": {"comment":"Release the lines"},
        "13379": {"synopsis":"Waits B bit times (the count at $BC84 each). Keeps HL."},
        "13380": {"synopsis":"Loop: one bit time per count in B."},
        "13383": {"synopsis":"Loop: counts one bit time down."},
        "13393": {"synopsis":"Waits ten bit times."},
        "13399": {"synopsis":"A short pause of 64 DJNZ turns."},
        "13401": {"synopsis":"Loop: the 64 turns."},
        "13404": {"synopsis":"Returns HL = the slot of machine A in the table at $BC90 (4 bytes each: the channel's\nflags, its IX, its segment).\nEntry: A = the machine number (0-32).\nChanges: AF, DE."},
        "13414": {"synopsis":"Makes the channel of the slot at HL current: loads IX from bytes 1-2 and pages its segment\n(byte 3) into page 1.\nEntry: HL = the slot.\nExit: IX = the channel's RAM.\nChanges: A, DE, HL."},
        "13419": {"comment":"Page 1 = the channel's segment"},
        "13426": {"synopsis":"Waits for the B6h line in A (bit 4 data, bit 5 status) to go low.","comment":"Wanted: the bit clear"},
        "13430": {"synopsis":"Waits for the B6h line in A to go high.","comment":"Wanted: the bit set"},
        "13431": {"synopsis":"Waits until (B6h AND C) = B, testing STOP. Waiting for the status line, or with SERIAL\nopen ($BC87 = $FF), it waits for ever; waiting for NET's data line it gives up when the\nstatus line drops, dropping its return address so that it returns from its caller.\nEntry: C = the mask, B = 0 or the mask.\nExit: NC and Z when the line came; carry with A = 0 (gave up) or A = $E5 (STOP)."},
        "13432": {"comment":"PORTB5 with keyboard row 7 (the STOP key)"},
        "13441": {"comment":"Waiting for the status line?"},
        "13447": {"comment":"Carry when SERIAL is open"},
        "13452": {"synopsis":"Loop: keeps the wait-for-ever flag in carry'."},
        "13453": {"synopsis":"Loop: the wanted state?"},
        "13455": {"comment":"The wanted state?"},
        "13458": {"comment":"STOP pressed?"},
        "13465": {"comment":"Wait for ever?"},
        "13468": {"comment":"Status in still high?"},
        "13474": {"comment":"Gave up: drop the caller's return address"},
        "13477": {"synopsis":"Selects keyboard row 7 (the STOP key) on port B5h, keeping PORTB5's upper bits.","comment":"PORTB5: tape and printer bits kept"},
        "13487": {"synopsis":"STOP was pressed during a SERIAL or NET transfer: sets bit 0 of $BD27, puts the lines\nback at rest (both high for SERIAL, low for NET), raises the ?STOP software interrupt and\nreturns carry with A = $E5 (.STOP)."},
        "13492": {"comment":"Carry when SERIAL is open"},
        "13497": {"comment":"NET: both lines low"},
        "13501": {"comment":"SERIAL: both lines high"},
        "13503": {"synopsis":"Puts the rest state on port B7h."},
        "13505": {"comment":"FLAG_SOFT_IRQ = ?STOP ($20)"},
        "13510": {"comment":"Error .STOP"},
        "13514": {"synopsis":"Tells whether a command or help string's first word is \"WP\".\nEntry: B = the first word's length, DE = the string (length byte first).\nExit: Z when it is \"WP\" (BC, DE kept). Otherwise ends the extension scan for its caller:\ndrops the caller's return address and returns C = 0, A = $F0 (.NOSTR, \"Unrecognised\ncommand string\"). Segment 1 is the last ROM the scan calls, so a string nobody took ends\nhere."},
        "13515": {"comment":"Two letters?"},
        "13526": {"comment":"\"W\" and \"P\" as B, C would hold them"},
        "13532": {"comment":"It is WP"},
        "13533": {"synopsis":"Not the WP: answers with the .NOSTR error for the caller's caller.","comment":"Answered"},
        "13535": {"comment":"Error .NOSTR"},
        "13537": {"comment":"Return from the caller"},
        "13539": {"synopsis":"The extension ROM entry ($C00A): EXOS calls it in every extension scan, the action code\nin C (spec 9.2). 1 cold reset: WP_COLD; 2 command string: WP_COMMAND; 3 help string:\nWP_HELP; 5 explain error code: EXOS_ERR_TEXTS. Any other code returns with BC and DE\nunchanged."},
        "13541": {"comment":"1: cold reset, become the application"},
        "13545": {"comment":"2: command string"},
        "13549": {"comment":"3: help string"},
        "13553": {"comment":"5: explain an error code"},
        "13556": {"comment":"Other codes: not ours"},
        "13557": {"synopsis":"Action 3, the help string (DE, length byte first; B = its first word's length):\n1. Empty (general help): writes the line \"WP    version 2.1\" to the default channel and\nreturns with BC and DE unchanged, so the scan goes on.\n2. The string compared, length byte included, with the 8 bytes at WP_HELP_KEY XOR $A7 (a\nlength of 7 and \"ISL1985\"): a match unpacks the packed text at COPYRIGHT_PACKED into a\nlength-first\ntext at $BEE0 (TEXT_UNPACK_BUF) and writes it, then two new lines (the run printed\n\"Copyright INTELLIGENT SOFTWARE LTD\").\n3. \"WP\" writes the version line and the banner (WP_HELP_TEXT, 94 bytes).\n4. Anything else: WP_IS_WP_CMD answers .NOSTR.\nExit (2 and 3): C = 0, A = 0.","comment":"The string's length"},
        "13559": {"comment":"H = 19 bytes: the version line only"},
        "13561": {"comment":"Empty: general help"},
        "13565": {"comment":"The XOR-$A7 key"},
        "13568": {"comment":"8 bytes, length byte included"},
        "13570": {"synopsis":"Loop: compares the string with the decoded key."},
        "13571": {"comment":"Decode one key byte"},
        "13576": {"comment":"Different: try \"WP\""},
        "13582": {"comment":"The packed text"},
        "13585": {"comment":"Unpack it to $BEE0"},
        "13592": {"comment":"BC = its length"},
        "13597": {"comment":"Write it to the default channel"},
        "13601": {"comment":"Then CR LF CR LF"},
        "13610": {"comment":"Answered, status 0"},
        "13613": {"synopsis":"\"HELP WP\": writes the whole help text; another word ends with .NOSTR."},
        "13615": {"comment":"Not WP: .NOSTR for the caller"},
        "13618": {"comment":"94 bytes: version line and banner"},
        "13620": {"comment":"Answered"},
        "13622": {"synopsis":"Writes H bytes of WP_HELP_TEXT to the default channel, keeping BC and DE in the main set."},
        "13623": {"comment":"Keep BC, DE"},
        "13627": {"comment":"The default channel"},
        "13637": {"synopsis":"The help text that WP_HELP writes: the line \"WP    version 2.1\" CR LF (19 bytes, alone for\nthe general help), then the banner."},
        "13656": {"synopsis":"The banner of \"HELP WP\": \"Enterprise Word Processor\" and \"1985 Intelligent Software Ltd.\",\nindented, each ended by CR LF; the $80 before 1985 is a character above ASCII (the run\nshowed\nit as a space). It runs into WP_CRLF2."},
        "13727": {"synopsis":"CR LF CR LF: the end of the banner, also written after the \"ISL1985\" text."},
        "13731": {"synopsis":"The help key stored XOR $A7: decoded, a length byte of 7 and \"ISL1985\" (WP_HELP compares\nthe help string with it)."},
        "13739": {"synopsis":"Code copied to $0080 and run there: the WP's warm start (RST_ADDR = $0080). Puts segment 1\ninto page 3, sets the WP's stack and goes to WP_RESTART, which starts the WP afresh.","comment":"Page 3 = segment 1"},
        "13743": {"comment":"The WP's stack in page 0"},
        "13750": {"synopsis":"Action 2, a command string: \":WP\" starts the word processor (another word ends with .NOSTR).\nFalls into WP_RESTART.","comment":"Not WP: .NOSTR for the caller"},
        "13753": {"synopsis":"Reset flags $60 for a command or a warm start (spec 9.3).","comment":"Reset flags $60"},
        "13755": {"synopsis":"Starts the Enterprise Word Processor as the application (spec 9.3). Entered with A = 0 by\nthe\ncold reset action, $60 by WP_RESTART.\n1. EXOS 0 (reset) with C = A; a stack at $01CB in page 0; interrupts back on; ($0100) =\n   $08CA;\npage 2 = the system segment.\n2. Six entries of the table at WP_CHANS_START (WP_OPEN_FATAL): EXOS variables (NET_IRQ,\n   DEF_CHAN $CD,\nST_FLAG, KEY_EDIT $C8, the keyboard's) and the channels KEYBOARD: $C8 and VIDEO: $D0, $CC,\n$CA, $CB, $C9.\n3. Function keys 15 to 0 send ESC and $D0 + the key's number.\n4. The packed screen texts from WP_PK_PAGE_D0 to channels $D0, $CA, $CB and $C9\n   (WP_WRITE_PACKED): the screen\nshowed the F1-F8 names (Load Save Print Help 80 40 Click Exit) and the ruler.\n5. 40-column mode (WP_SET_MODE), which opens the editor $CD on video page $CE.\n6. The warm start code to $0080 (RST_ADDR) and the software interrupt routine WP_SOFT_IRQ.\nThen the main loop, WP_MAIN_LOOP.","comment":"The reset flags"},
        "13758": {"comment":"The WP's stack"},
        "13768": {"comment":"Page 2 = segment $FF, the system segment"},
        "13771": {"comment":"The variables and channels table"},
        "13776": {"synopsis":"Loop: six channels, each with the variables before it."},
        "13783": {"comment":"B = 8 (FKEY), C = key 15 first"},
        "13786": {"synopsis":"Loop: programs function key C with the 2-byte string ESC, $D0 + C, built at $0112."},
        "13789": {"comment":"The code: $D0 + the key"},
        "13801": {"comment":"KEYBOARD: program the function key"},
        "13807": {"comment":"Down to key 0"},
        "13810": {"comment":"The packed screen texts"},
        "13813": {"comment":"The texts go to channels $D0, $CA, $CB, $C9"},
        "13833": {"comment":"40 columns, open the editor"},
        "13837": {"comment":"The warm start code to $0080"},
        "13840": {"comment":"RST_ADDR = $0080"},
        "13852": {"comment":"The software interrupt routine (at $003D)"},
        "13858": {"comment":"From $3623 (inside): POP HL, XOR A, back to the loop's top"},
        "13861": {"synopsis":"The WP's main loop. Each turn shows an error first when A is not 0, closes channels $CF and\n$D1, sets FLG_EDIT to $20, puts \"ENTERPRISE WORD PROCESSOR\" on the status line, shows the\npages (ruler $CA, $CB, the text $CE in rows 4-23, $C9 at the bottom) and reads the editor\n$CD. A key other than ESC returns to the top through $3623, an entry inside LD HL,$AFE1\n(POP HL, XOR A). ESC is followed by the function key's code on the keyboard channel: $D0-$D7\n(F1-F8) jump through WP_FKEY_TABLE with the main loop as their return address and A = their\nstatus; other codes are ignored.","comment":"An error to show?"},
        "13865": {"comment":"Close the WP's file channels"},
        "13873": {"comment":"FLG_EDIT = $20"},
        "13878": {"comment":"The status line text"},
        "13884": {"comment":"$CA: 2 rows at screen row 1"},
        "13891": {"comment":"$CB: 1 row at row 3"},
        "13899": {"comment":"$CE (the text): 20 rows at row 4"},
        "13907": {"comment":"$C9: 2 rows at row 24"},
        "13915": {"comment":"Commands return to the loop"},
        "13919": {"comment":"Write code 0 to the editor"},
        "13925": {"comment":"Read from the editor"},
        "13929": {"comment":"Error: show it"},
        "13931": {"comment":"ESC (a function key)?"},
        "13935": {"comment":"Read the key's code from the keyboard"},
        "13942": {"comment":"F1-F8 send $D0-$D7"},
        "13950": {"comment":"Jump through WP_FKEY_TABLE"},
        "13960": {"synopsis":"JP (HL): the end of the key dispatch above, also called as \"call HL\" by the module loader at\n$3891 (CALL NZ here runs a loaded module's start-up at HL)."},
        "13961": {"synopsis":"The function keys' commands, one word each for F1-F8 (codes $D0-$D7); the screen names\nthem Load (WP_F1_LOAD), Save (WP_F2_SAVE), Print (WP_F3_PRINT), Help (WP_F4_HELP), 80 and 40\n(both WP_KEY_COLS),\nClick (WP_F7_CLICK) and Exit (WP_F8_EXIT)."},
        "13977": {"synopsis":"The WP's software interrupt routine (its address is at $003D): resets the stack and goes\nback to the main loop with the error .STOP ($E5) to show."},
        "13980": {"comment":"Error .STOP"},
        "13985": {"synopsis":"Shows error A on page $CC: writes the packed text at WP_PK_ERR_LINE to it (WP_WRITE_PACKED),\nthen the\nexplanation that\nEXOS 28 gives (\"Unknown error code\" when it gives none); blanks screen rows 1-3, shows the\nmessage row at row 2, and waits up to 2000 polls for a key.\nEntry: A = an EXOS error code."},
        "13986": {"comment":"The packed text at WP_PK_ERR_LINE to $CC"},
        "13995": {"comment":"The explanation to $01CB"},
        "14000": {"comment":"An empty explanation?"},
        "14004": {"comment":"Use WP_UNKNOWN_TEXT"},
        "14007": {"synopsis":"Writes the length-first message at DE to page $CC."},
        "14013": {"comment":"Rows 1-3 blank (C = 0)"},
        "14023": {"comment":"Row 1 of $CC at screen row 2"},
        "14031": {"comment":"Up to 2000 polls"},
        "14034": {"synopsis":"Loop: returns as soon as the keyboard has a character."},
        "14036": {"comment":"Keyboard status"},
        "14038": {"comment":"A key waiting?"},
        "14046": {"synopsis":"\"Unknown error code\", length byte first: the message when EXOS 28 has no explanation."},
        "14065": {"synopsis":"Shows rows 1-3 of page $D0 at screen row 1 (the prompts)."},
        "14069": {"synopsis":"Shows D rows of channel A from its row 1 at screen row 1."},
        "14071": {"synopsis":"Shows D rows of channel A from its row 1 at screen row E."},
        "14073": {"synopsis":"Shows D rows of video channel A from its row C at screen row E (C = 0 blanks them):\nspecial function 1 (DISP).\nExit: A = the status."},
        "14075": {"comment":"VIDEO: display the page"},
        "14078": {"synopsis":"F5 and F6: switches the text to 80 or 40 columns after asking. Prints \"Press ENTER for 40\ncolumn mode, this will delete your text\" on $D0; for F5 the second text moves the cursor\nback and writes \"8\" over the \"4\". ENTER sets the mode (WP_SET_MODE), any other key\nreturns to the main loop.\nEntry: A = 8 for F5, 10 for F6 (twice the table index).","comment":"Z for F6 (40 columns)"},
        "14081": {"comment":"The prompt"},
        "14091": {"comment":"F5: \"8\" over the \"4\""},
        "14096": {"comment":"Show the prompt rows"},
        "14099": {"comment":"Wait for a key"},
        "14106": {"comment":"ENTER?"},
        "14109": {"comment":"No: back to the loop"},
        "14112": {"synopsis":"Sets the editor's mode: MODE_VID 0 (40 columns) for A = 0, 2 (80 columns) otherwise; closes\nthe text page $CE and the editor $CD and opens them again from the table at WP_CHANS_TEXT,\nthen\nwrites code $FA to the editor.\nExit: A = 0."},
        "14117": {"synopsis":"Writes MODE_VID = D."},
        "14118": {"comment":"Write variable 22, MODE_VID"},
        "14131": {"comment":"VIDEO: $CE and EDITOR: $CD again"},
        "14140": {"comment":"Code $FA to the editor"},
        "14148": {"synopsis":"Runs one entry of a channel table, a failure being fatal: falls into WP_OPEN_CHANS with\nA = 0 and Z in AF'."},
        "14149": {"synopsis":"Runs one entry of a channel table at HL: bytes below $80 are EXOS variable numbers, each\nfollowed by the value to write; a byte with bit 7 is a channel number followed by the\ndevice name's address, opened (or $FF: channel $D1 created), and ends the entry. On .NORAM\nor .NOVID it closes channel $D2 and tries again.\nEntry: HL = the entry, AF' = what a failure does: Z shows \"FATAL WP ERROR\" on the status\nline and flashes the border for ever; NZ returns NZ with A = the error.\nExit: Z, HL = the next entry."},
        "14150": {"synopsis":"Loop: one byte of the entry."},
        "14151": {"comment":"A channel number?"},
        "14155": {"comment":"Write the variable"},
        "14158": {"comment":"D = its value"},
        "14164": {"synopsis":"Opens the channel, DE = its device name."},
        "14170": {"comment":"$FF: create instead"},
        "14176": {"synopsis":"Returns Z when the open or create worked; otherwise checks the error.","comment":"Opened"},
        "14178": {"comment":".NORAM?"},
        "14182": {"comment":".NOVID?"},
        "14186": {"synopsis":"Out of memory: closes channel $D2 and runs the entry's channel again."},
        "14191": {"comment":"Back to the channel byte"},
        "14195": {"comment":"Closed: try again"},
        "14197": {"synopsis":"Failed: returns the error, or stops for ever when AF' says so.","comment":"Z from the caller: fatal"},
        "14199": {"comment":"Return NZ, A = the error"},
        "14200": {"comment":"\"FATAL WP ERROR\" to the status line"},
        "14208": {"synopsis":"Loop: flashes the border for ever."},
        "14209": {"comment":"Border colour"},
        "14213": {"synopsis":"Creates channel $D1 on the device at DE."},
        "14219": {"synopsis":"Copies 31 characters from DE to the status line from its column 6 (ST_POINTER + 6).\nEntry: DE = the text.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"ST_POINTER"},
        "14232": {"synopsis":"Status-line text \"FATAL WP ERROR\", 31 bytes, centred in spaces with no end byte. The WP's\nchannel opener (the error exit at $3778) copies it with WP_STATUS_TEXT to the status line\n(ST_POINTER\n+ 6) and then flashes the border forever."},
        "14263": {"synopsis":"Status-line text \"ENTERPRISE WORD PROCESSOR\", 31 bytes padded with spaces, copied to the\nstatus line by WP_STATUS_TEXT when the WP starts ($3636)."},
        "14294": {"synopsis":"WP function key F7 (\"Click\", entry 6 of the key table at WP_FKEY_TABLE): toggles the\nkeyboard click.\nExit: A = 0, so nothing is shown as an error.","comment":"B = 2 toggle, C = 7 CLICK_KEY"},
        "14297": {"comment":"Key click on/off"},
        "14299": {"comment":"No error to report"},
        "14301": {"synopsis":"WP function key F8 (\"Exit\", entry 7 of the key table at WP_FKEY_TABLE): asks for a command\nline with\n\"Press ENTER to start BASIC.\" (WP_ASK_NAME) and passes it to the ROM extensions with EXOS\n26; ENTER alone sends \"BASIC\". ESC or an error returns to the WP.\nExit: A = status.","comment":"Prompt \"Press ENTER to start BASIC.\""},
        "14304": {"comment":"Read a line into $01CB"},
        "14307": {"comment":"ESC or an error?"},
        "14308": {"comment":"Length of the typed line"},
        "14310": {"comment":"Something typed? Send it"},
        "14312": {"comment":"Else the command \"BASIC\""},
        "14315": {"synopsis":"Passes the command string at DE to the ROM extensions.","comment":"Command string to every ROM extension"},
        "14317": {"comment":"A = status of the scan"},
        "14318": {"synopsis":"Command string \"BASIC\" with its length byte (5), sent by WP_F8_EXIT when only ENTER was\ntyped."},
        "14324": {"synopsis":"WP function key F3 (\"Print\", entry 2 of the key table at WP_FKEY_TABLE): asks for a device\nname\n(\"Press ENTER for parallel printer, or type device-name:\"); ENTER alone means \"PRINTER:\".\nCreates channel $D1 on it, sets FLG_EDIT to SEND NOW + SEND ALL so that reading the text\neditor ($CD) returns the whole document at once, and copies it character by character to $D1\nuntil the read fails.\nExit: A = 0 when it ended with .EOF, else the error.","comment":"Prompt for a device name"},
        "14327": {"comment":"Read a line into $01CB"},
        "14330": {"comment":"ESC or an error?"},
        "14331": {"comment":"Length of the typed name"},
        "14333": {"comment":"A name typed?"},
        "14335": {"comment":"Else \"PRINTER:\" with its length byte"},
        "14339": {"comment":"9 bytes into the name buffer"},
        "14345": {"synopsis":"Creates the output channel $D1 on the name at $01CB, then prints.","comment":"Create channel $D1 on the name"},
        "14348": {"comment":"A non-zero: an error returns, not fatal"},
        "14352": {"comment":"Not created?"},
        "14353": {"comment":"FLG_EDIT = $C0: SEND NOW + SEND ALL"},
        "14358": {"synopsis":"Loop: reads the next character of the document from the editor and writes it to $D1.","comment":"Next character of the document"},
        "14362": {"comment":"Read failed (.EOF at the end)?"},
        "14364": {"comment":"Send it to the device"},
        "14368": {"comment":"Next character"},
        "14370": {"synopsis":"WP function key F1 (\"Load\", entry 0 of the key table at WP_FKEY_TABLE): asks for a file name\n(\"LOAD\nthe document.\"), opens channel $D1 on it and falls into WP_LOAD_MODULE.","comment":"Prompt \"LOAD - the document.\""},
        "14373": {"comment":"Read a line into $01CB"},
        "14376": {"comment":"ESC or an error?"},
        "14377": {"comment":"Open channel $D1 on the name"},
        "14380": {"comment":"A non-zero: an error returns, not fatal"},
        "14383": {"comment":"Not opened?"},
        "14384": {"synopsis":"Loads the modules of the file on channel $D1 one after another (EXOS 29, header at $0102). A\nmodule EXOS or a ROM loads, a user relocatable module (type 2) and an editor document (type\n8, loaded into the text with the editor's special function 25) go on to the next module; a\nfile that is not in module form (.ASCII) is copied into the text as plain characters; the\nend header (.NOMOD) ends the load with A = 0.\nExit: A = 0 or an error code.","comment":"From channel $D1"},
        "14386": {"comment":"Module header to $0102"},
        "14391": {"comment":"Loaded? Next module"},
        "14393": {"comment":".ASCII: not a module file?"},
        "14397": {"comment":".ITYPE: a type nobody loaded?"},
        "14401": {"comment":".NOMOD: the end of the file?"},
        "14403": {"comment":"Other errors return"},
        "14404": {"comment":"Loaded, no error"},
        "14406": {"synopsis":"A module type EXOS left to the caller: type 2 (user relocatable) or 8 (editor document) is\nloaded here, any other returns .ITYPE.","comment":"B = the module type"},
        "14407": {"comment":"User relocatable module ($$REL)?"},
        "14411": {"comment":"Editor document ($$EDIT)?"},
        "14413": {"comment":"Neither: A = .ITYPE"},
        "14416": {"comment":"Editor channel of the text"},
        "14418": {"comment":"Special 25 (CHLD): load the text"},
        "14420": {"comment":"... from channel $D1"},
        "14424": {"comment":"Load failed?"},
        "14425": {"comment":"Next module"},
        "14427": {"synopsis":"Loop for a file that is not in module form: writes character B into the text and reads the\nnext one from $D1, until a read fails or a Ctrl-Z ($1A) comes.","comment":"Character B into the text"},
        "14431": {"comment":"Next character of the file"},
        "14435": {"comment":"Read failed?"},
        "14438": {"comment":"Ctrl-Z ends the text with A = 0"},
        "14442": {"synopsis":"Turns .EOF into success: returns A = 0 for .EOF, A unchanged for anything else.","comment":".EOF is a normal end"},
        "14445": {"comment":"No error"},
        "14447": {"synopsis":"Loads a user relocatable module: claims its size at the next free address kept at $0100 (it\nmust end below $4000), loads it there with EXOS 30, calls its initialisation entry (header\nword +4, $FFFF = none) and goes on to the next module. Exit on failure: A = .NORAM or the\nerror.","comment":"BC = module size from the header"},
        "14451": {"comment":"HL = next free address in page 0"},
        "14454": {"comment":"DE = where it loads"},
        "14456": {"comment":"A non-zero: NZ for the error exits"},
        "14457": {"comment":"Its end"},
        "14458": {"comment":"Past $FFFF?"},
        "14460": {"comment":"Past $3FFF?"},
        "14463": {"synopsis":"Returns .NORAM when the flags say NZ (no room for the module).","comment":".NORAM"},
        "14466": {"comment":"Claim the space"},
        "14469": {"comment":"Load it at DE from channel $D1"},
        "14473": {"comment":"Load failed?"},
        "14474": {"comment":"Initialisation offset from the header"},
        "14477": {"comment":"$FFFF means none"},
        "14479": {"comment":"Offset to address"},
        "14481": {"comment":"Call it (WP_JP_HL holds a JP (HL))"},
        "14484": {"comment":"Did it return an error?"},
        "14486": {"comment":"Next module"},
        "14488": {"synopsis":"WP function key F2 (\"Save\", entry 1 of the key table at WP_FKEY_TABLE): asks for a file name\n(\"SAVE\nthe document.\"), creates channel $D1 on it, has the editor save the text to it (special\nfunction 26) and closes the file with a 16-byte end header (WP_EOF_HEADER).\nExit: A = status.","comment":"Prompt \"SAVE - the document.\""},
        "14491": {"comment":"Read a line into $01CB"},
        "14494": {"comment":"ESC or an error?"},
        "14495": {"comment":"Create channel $D1 on the name"},
        "14498": {"comment":"A non-zero: an error returns, not fatal"},
        "14501": {"comment":"Not created?"},
        "14502": {"comment":"Editor channel of the text"},
        "14504": {"comment":"Special 26 (CHSV): save the text"},
        "14506": {"comment":"... to channel $D1"},
        "14510": {"comment":"Save failed?"},
        "14511": {"comment":"Then the end-of-file header"},
        "14513": {"comment":"16 bytes"},
        "14522": {"synopsis":"A 16-byte module header of type 10 ($$EOF), written after a saved document so the file ends\nas a module file should."},
        "14538": {"synopsis":"Writes D to EXOS variable 32 (FLG_EDIT), the flags of an editor read.\nEntry: D = flags.\nExit: A = status.\nChanges: BC.","comment":"B = 1 write, C = 32 FLG_EDIT"},
        "14544": {"synopsis":"Asks for a line on the WP's top lines:\n1. Opens the prompt editor $CF (an EDITOR: channel shown on the 3-row page $D0).\n2. Writes the prompt at DE into it with WP_WRITE_TEXTS and shows page $D0 (WP_SHOW_PROMPT).\n3. Reads characters from $CF into $01CC on until ENTER, then stores the length before them\n   at $01CB.\nEntry: DE = the prompt (a chain of length-prefixed texts).\nExit: NZ and DE = $01CB (length byte, then the line) when a line was typed (it may be\nempty); Z when not, with A = 0 for ESC or A = the error (.INAME after 256 characters).","comment":"Keep the prompt"},
        "14545": {"comment":"Open the prompt editor $CF"},
        "14548": {"comment":"A non-zero: an error returns, not fatal"},
        "14552": {"comment":"HL = the prompt"},
        "14553": {"comment":"Not opened?"},
        "14554": {"comment":"Write the prompt into the editor"},
        "14559": {"comment":"Show page $D0 at the top"},
        "14562": {"comment":"Line buffer, after its length byte"},
        "14565": {"comment":"At most 256 characters"},
        "14567": {"synopsis":"Loop: reads the next character from the prompt editor and stores it."},
        "14568": {"comment":"Next character of the line"},
        "14574": {"comment":"Read failed?"},
        "14576": {"comment":"ESC? Z with A = 0"},
        "14580": {"comment":"Store it"},
        "14582": {"comment":"ENTER ends the line"},
        "14587": {"comment":"Room for more?"},
        "14589": {"comment":".INAME: line too long"},
        "14591": {"synopsis":"Returns Z with A = the error code.","comment":"Z: no line, A = error"},
        "14593": {"synopsis":"ENTER: stores the line's length (without the ENTER) at $01CB and returns NZ.","comment":"Length byte of the line"},
        "14596": {"comment":"Characters before the ENTER"},
        "14599": {"comment":"NZ: a line was typed"},
        "14601": {"synopsis":"WP function key F4 (\"Help\", entry 3 of the key table at WP_FKEY_TABLE): shows the 40-row\nhelp page\n$D2 in 20 rows from screen row 4. When the page does not exist yet it opens it and writes\nthe packed help text (WP_PK_HELP) into it. ESC (which each function key sends first, so F4\nagain too) flips between rows 1-20 and 21-40; ENTER or space returns with A = 0. The run\nshowed both halves (\"ctrl F1  -  Reform paragraph\" ... and the cursor and erase keys).","comment":"C = 1: rows 1-20 first"},
        "14604": {"synopsis":"Displays the help page from row C; opens and fills it first if it is not there."},
        "14605": {"comment":"20 rows at screen row 4"},
        "14608": {"comment":"Help page channel"},
        "14610": {"comment":"B = 1: display the page"},
        "14612": {"comment":"Page already there?"},
        "14614": {"comment":"Open the 40-row help page $D2"},
        "14620": {"comment":"Restore the first row"},
        "14621": {"comment":"Not opened?"},
        "14623": {"comment":"20 rows at screen row 4"},
        "14628": {"comment":"Display the new page"},
        "14630": {"comment":"Write the help text into it"},
        "14638": {"synopsis":"Waits for a key while the help is shown."},
        "14639": {"synopsis":"Loop: reads keys from the keyboard channel $C8 until ENTER, space or ESC."},
        "14640": {"comment":"Read a key"},
        "14646": {"comment":"ENTER returns"},
        "14649": {"comment":"Space returns"},
        "14652": {"comment":"ESC? (each function key sends one first)"},
        "14654": {"comment":"Other keys: wait"},
        "14656": {"comment":"First row 1 <-> 21"},
        "14660": {"comment":"Show the other half"},
        "14662": {"synopsis":"Unpacks one packed WP text (WP_UNPACK) into the buffer at $02CA and writes it to a channel.\nEntry: A = channel, HL = the packed text.\nExit: A = status of the write, HL = past the packed text (texts in a row are written by\ncalls in a row).\nChanges: BC, DE.","comment":"Unpack into the buffer at $02CA"},
        "14665": {"comment":"Keep the start "},
        "14666": {"comment":"... and the channel"},
        "14671": {"comment":"HL = start; keep the source position"},
        "14673": {"comment":"HL = end, DE = start"},
        "14674": {"comment":"BC = length"},
        "14678": {"comment":"HL = past the packed text"},
        "14679": {"comment":"Write the text"},
        "14682": {"synopsis":"Unpacks a WP text. The text is a stream of bits read from the top bit of each byte:\n- 1 + 5 bits n: the letter $61 + n (lower case);\n- 01 + 8 bits: that byte as it is (capitals, control codes, escape sequences);\n- 00 + 5 bits n: n = 0 ends the text, else phrase n of WP_PHRASES, unpacked in place by a\n  call to itself.\nA text starts on a byte boundary and the bits after its end mark are unused.\nEntry: HL = the packed text, DE = where to write.\nExit: DE = past the text written, HL = past the last byte read.\nChanges: A, BC.","comment":"No bits left: the first read loads a byte"},
        "14684": {"synopsis":"Loop: reads the next code of the stream.","comment":"Marker for 1 bit"},
        "14689": {"comment":"The bit to carry"},
        "14690": {"comment":"0: not a letter"},
        "14692": {"comment":"1: 5 bits "},
        "14695": {"comment":"... a letter from \"a\" on"},
        "14697": {"synopsis":"Stores the character in A and reads the next code.","comment":"Store the character"},
        "14701": {"synopsis":"First bit 0: a second bit tells a byte (1) from a phrase number (0).","comment":"A = $80: read the second bit"},
        "14705": {"comment":"00: a phrase number"},
        "14707": {"comment":"01: marker for 8 bits, a byte"},
        "14714": {"synopsis":"Code 00: reads the 5-bit phrase number; 0 ends the text, else unpacks that phrase of\nWP_PHRASES and goes on.","comment":"5-bit phrase number"},
        "14718": {"comment":"0 ends the text"},
        "14719": {"comment":"Keep the stream position "},
        "14720": {"comment":"... and its bit count"},
        "14722": {"comment":"Phrase table WP_PHRASES"},
        "14727": {"synopsis":"Loop: steps over one phrase by its length byte (which counts itself).","comment":"Length of this phrase"},
        "14728": {"comment":"Step over it"},
        "14733": {"synopsis":"Counts the phrases down to the one wanted.","comment":"Phrase n reached?"},
        "14735": {"comment":"Past its length byte"},
        "14736": {"comment":"Unpack the phrase"},
        "14739": {"comment":"Back to the stream"},
        "14743": {"synopsis":"Reads 5 bits of the packed stream into A (falls into WP_BITS with the marker $08).","comment":"Marker: 5 bits"},
        "14745": {"synopsis":"Reads bits of the packed stream into A, top bit first, until the marker bit set in A on\nentry falls out ($80 reads 1 bit, $08 five, $01 eight).\nEntry: A = marker, HL = stream, C = the current byte, B = bits left in it.\nExit: A = the bits read, carry set; HL, B, C moved on.","comment":"A bit left in C?"},
        "14747": {"comment":"Next byte of the stream"},
        "14749": {"comment":"8 bits in it"},
        "14751": {"synopsis":"Shifts one bit of C into A.","comment":"Top bit of C "},
        "14753": {"comment":"... into A; the marker drops out last"},
        "14754": {"comment":"Marker not out yet?"},
        "14757": {"synopsis":"The phrases of the packed WP texts, numbered from 1: each a length byte that counts itself,\nthen the phrase packed as WP_UNPACK reads it. 28 phrases: colour escapes (ESC o, ESC s, ESC\nP 0-2, ESC I 1/3), runs of spaces, the help page's line starts (\"\\r\\n ESC I 3 ctrl F\", \"alt\nF\", \"ctrl  \", \"shift \"), \"  -  \" and words such as \" line\", \" paragraph\", \" margin\", \"\ncharacter\", \"Up or down\", the ERASE, DEL and INS heads and the cursor-arrow pairs\n(characters $8B $9B, $9E $8C)."},
        "14983": {"synopsis":"Packed text written to page $D0 (the WP's 3 top rows) at start-up ($35F2): only ESC C with\neight palette colours."},
        "14997": {"synopsis":"Packed text for page $CA (2 rows) at start-up: palette (ESC C), cursor and scrolling off\n(ESC o, ESC s), then \" F1 \" to \" F8 \" in boxes of alternating paper colour (ESC P 0/2), a\nrow of empty boxes under them."},
        "15066": {"synopsis":"Packed text for page $CB (1 row): the function keys' names in the same boxes: \"Load Save\nPrint Help 80 40 Click Exit\"."},
        "15121": {"synopsis":"Packed text for page $C9 (2 rows): what the function keys do with CTRL (\"Ref Cen Tab Left\nRel Up Col\") and ALT (\"Just UnTab Rlr Right Rst Down Pcol\"), in the same boxes."},
        "15222": {"synopsis":"Packed text for the error line $CC: palette, cursor off, clear the page (Ctrl-Z, $1A) and\n\"*** \"; WP_SHOW_ERROR writes the explained error text after it."},
        "15244": {"synopsis":"The packed help page (40 rows on channel $D2): rows 1-20 list the CTRL and ALT function-key\nactions (\"ctrl F1  -  Reform paragraph\" to \"alt  F7  -  Change paragraph colour\") and \"Press\nENTER to return to editing or F4  for more information.\"; rows 21-40 the cursor keys, ERASE,\nDEL and INS with shift and ctrl. Key names are in ink 3 (ESC I 3), the rest in ink 1. The\nrun read it all when F4 was pressed."},
        "15571": {"synopsis":"Writes a length-prefixed text to a channel. When the byte after it is 0 it goes on with \"\nthe document.\\rType filename and then ENTER.\\r\" (WP_TXT_DOCUMENT) on the prompt editor $CF,\nwhich\nfinishes the LOAD and SAVE prompts.\nEntry: A = channel, HL = length byte.\nExit: HL = the byte after the last text written, NZ (A = that byte, or an error).\nChanges: BC, DE.","comment":"BC = text length"},
        "15575": {"comment":"DE = the text"},
        "15576": {"comment":"Write it"},
        "15578": {"comment":"HL = the byte after it"},
        "15579": {"comment":"Not 0 there, or an error?"},
        "15581": {"comment":"0: append \" the document.\" "},
        "15584": {"comment":"... on the prompt editor"},
        "15588": {"synopsis":"WP_F8_EXIT's prompt: length byte, \"Press ENTER to start BASIC.\" and CR."},
        "15617": {"synopsis":"WP_F3_PRINT's prompt: length byte, \"Press ENTER for parallel printer,\", CR, \"or type\ndevice-name:\", CR."},
        "15673": {"synopsis":"WP_F1_LOAD's prompt head: length byte and \"LOAD\", then a 0 that makes WP_WRITE_TEXTS append\nWP_TXT_DOCUMENT."},
        "15679": {"synopsis":"WP_F2_SAVE's prompt head: length byte and \"SAVE\", then a 0 that makes WP_WRITE_TEXTS append\nWP_TXT_DOCUMENT."},
        "15685": {"synopsis":"End of the LOAD and SAVE prompts: length byte, \"- the document.\", CR, \"Type filename and\nthen ENTER.\", CR."},
        "15731": {"synopsis":"F5/F6's question on page $D0 ($3701): length byte, Ctrl-Z (clear), ESC o (cursor off) and\n\"Press ENTER for 40 column mode, this\" / \"will delete your text.  Press ESC to\" / \"return to\nediting.\". Its next byte is not 0, so WP_WRITE_TEXTS stops there."},
        "15829": {"synopsis":"Written after WP_TXT_40_COLS for F5 only: length byte 5, ESC = row 1 column 17 (\"!\" and \"1\"\nless $20) and \"8\", which turns \"40 column\" into \"80 column\". The $FF after it stops\nWP_WRITE_TEXTS."},
        "15836": {"synopsis":"WP channel table, the six calls at start-up ($35CB): Read by the WP's channel opener at\nWP_OPEN_FATAL: a byte below $80 and a value write that EXOS variable; a channel number ($80\nor more)\nand the address of a device name open that channel and end the call; $FF and a name create\nchannel $D1 instead. Variables: NET_IRQ $FF, DEF_CHAN $CD, ST_FLAG 0, KEY_EDIT $C8, LOCK_KEY\n0, KEY_IRQ $FF, STOP_IRQ 0, RATE_KEY 3, DELAY_KEY $19, then keyboard $C8; MODE_VID 0,\nCOLR_VID 0, Y_SIZ_VID 3, X_SIZ_VID 40, video page $D0 (3 rows); Y_SIZ_VID 1 for $CC, 2 for\n$CA, 1 for $CB; MODE_VID $0F and Y_SIZ_VID 2 for $C9; Y_SIZ_VID 20 for $CE, the text page."},
        "15890": {"synopsis":"WP channel table for the text (two calls at $3733): Y_SIZ_VID 20 and video page $CE; then\nVID_EDIT $CE, BUF_EDIT $3E and the text editor $CD."},
        "15902": {"synopsis":"WP channel table for the prompt editor (WP_ASK_NAME): VID_EDIT $D0, BUF_EDIT 1, FLG_EDIT $10\n(NO SOFT), then editor channel $CF."},
        "15911": {"synopsis":"WP channel table entry: open channel $D1 on the name typed at $01CB (WP_F1_LOAD)."},
        "15914": {"synopsis":"WP channel table entry: create channel $D1 on the name typed at $01CB ($FF selects create;\nWP_F2_SAVE, WP_F3_PRINT)."},
        "15917": {"synopsis":"WP channel table for the help page: MODE_VID 0, Y_SIZ_VID 40, video page $D2."},
        "15924": {"synopsis":"Device name \"VIDEO:\" with its length byte, for the WP's video pages."},
        "15931": {"synopsis":"Device name \"EDITOR:\" with its length byte, for the WP's editors $CD and $CF."},
        "15939": {"synopsis":"Device name \"PRINTER:\" with its length byte, copied to $01CB when F3's device name is left\nempty."},
        "15948": {"synopsis":"Device name \"KEYBOARD:\" with its length byte, for the WP's keyboard channel $C8."},
        "15958": {"synopsis":"Extension action 5 (explain error code), from the extension entry ($34F1). Answers every\ncode: codes $FF-$D0 with their text from ERR_TEXT_PACKED; $CF, a code the spec does not\nlist, with the copyright text (COPYRIGHT_PACKED); any other code with an empty text, which\nmeans an unknown code. The text is unpacked by IS-BASIC's text unpacker at TEXT_UNPACK_BUF\ninto $BEE0\nas a length byte and the text, first letter capitalised and a last space dropped.\nEntry: B = error code.\nExit: DE = $BEE0, B = $FF (the system segment, which holds it), C = 0 (answered).","comment":"Packed error texts"},
        "15961": {"comment":"Answer in the system segment"},
        "15964": {"comment":"Index = $FF - code"},
        "15966": {"comment":"Codes $FF-$D0 have texts"},
        "15970": {"comment":"Code $CF: the copyright text"},
        "15973": {"comment":"Its index 0, or an empty answer"},
        "15975": {"comment":"Not $CF? Empty answer"},
        "15977": {"comment":"$CF: unpack it"},
        "15978": {"synopsis":"Stores a zero length: the answer for a code with no text.","comment":"Length 0"},
        "15979": {"synopsis":"Unpacks text A of the table at HL into $BEE0 when carry is set, then answers.","comment":"Unpack text A as a counted string"},
        "15982": {"comment":"B = segment $FF, C = 0: answered"},
        "15986": {"synopsis":"The EXOS error texts for codes $FF (\"invalid EXOS function code\") down to $D0 (\"cassette CRC\nerror\"), 48 in a row, packed in 4-bit codes read by IS-BASIC's unpacker at TEXT_UNPACK: 0\nends a\ntext, 1-13 are \"EONRTAISCLDU \" (table at TEXT_CHARS), 14 and 4 bits one of\n\"PKFBVYWMGHQXZ$-/\"\n($23FF), 15 and 5 bits n either capitals up to the next space (n = 0) or phrase n - 1 of the\ntable at TEXT_WORDS. Letters come out in lower case. Texts are not byte-aligned: the\nunpacker\ncounts end codes to reach text n. The codes the spec gives no text ($F8, $F5, $F4, $F3, $EC,\n$DB) have an empty one. The run read up to $3FAE (\"network address not set\", code $D6)."},
        "16344": {"synopsis":"The packed text \"copyright INTELLIGENT SOFTWARE LTD\" (same coding as ERR_TEXT_PACKED), the\nanswer for error code $CF and for \":HELP\" with the right hidden string ($350E). Its 25 bytes\nare also part of the start-up tamper check (XOR at $2689, checked against COPYRIGHT_CHECK at\n$248B)."},
        "16369": {"synopsis":"Twelve bytes that nothing reads after the boot, a copy of $3F71-$3F7C in the error texts."},
        "16381": {"synopsis":"The check byte of the tamper check: the one-second tick (service 4, $2480) subtracts the 229\nbytes from SVC_STARTUP (start-up code) with borrow from the XOR of $AC and COPYRIGHT_PACKED\nkept\nat $BF7E, and compares the result with this byte ($4A, which matches the ROM as it is). A\nmismatch decrements a system-segment byte (address at $BFEC)."},
        "16382": {"synopsis":"The page's last word, $6318, which nothing reads after the boot. With it the words of the\n32K EXOS ROM add up to 0, as the boot's checksum (page 0, $008E) requires."}
      }
    }
  },
